job-13606q0:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Operations team supports Stripe’s mission (to ‘Increase the GDP of the Internet’) by enabling efficient, user-centered product development at scale. We create, manage, and implement central programs across Stripe that optimize Product development and delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team drives critical, cross-functional initiatives and delivers strategic analyses, such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining launch processes and policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing launch processes and execution within product orgs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Planning and alignment across Product, Go-to-Market, and Systems / Operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading commercial execution for priority product launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aggregating user feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a team-oriented group that collaborates closely with each other and our cross-functional stakeholders. Together, we identify opportunities to design and scale repeatable processes, and we bring clarity and insight to address ambiguous and complex problems at the intersection of go-to-market and product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end operational readiness and execution for priority product launches, establishing owners, milestones, decision forums, and launch plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously examine, experiment, and implement measured improvements to our operational model and processes (e.g. automating tasks, building agentic workflows, developing repeatable methodologies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build with a mindset of scale and flexibility for all internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product teams to help them execute on important strategic initiatives or drive operational scale and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and communicate relevant operational metrics to leadership and partnering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in product operations, technical program management, project management, a product ownership role, management consulting or related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previously worked cross-functionally with product and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have proficiency with Google suite, especially Google Sheets and Google Slides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI, automation, or workflow tools to drive operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem solving and analysis experience (solving business problems - commercial, operational, financial) in a GTM org and/or Sales-oriented environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record of delivering complex initiatives end-to-end with multiple stakeholders in a changing, ambiguous environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiastic “roll up your sleeves” mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with payments, fintech, and/or high-growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with and translating SQL and working with dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-0fxgef9:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design industry-leading experiences that reduce the friction for new users onboarding to Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand Stripe’s product suite, customer needs, and developments in AI/ML that could influence our growth strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to work across the entire Growth team, including customer acquisition, conversion, and retention experiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion design in growth (and growth in the design organization).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply design priorities and principles to growth projects, and help show how growth work makes progress toward design goals in the user experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineering and product to design, build, and launch user-facing product experiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our partner teams to help support their growth and onboarding needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with our user research team and support ongoing research projects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design reviews and share your work regularly with design and company leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Design, Product Development, or a related field, plus 4 years of experience in Design.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have experience in each of the following: Three years of experience in:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth related domains including onboarding journeys, email marketing, pricing pages, product upsells and cross sells, iterative conversion experiments, and product surfaces;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducting user testing and research, utilizing both qualitative and quantitative data to distill business and user objectives;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpreting user data and metrics, leveraging insights from A/B testing to inform product strategy and design improvements that align with both business and user goals;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UI, UX, and visual design software including Figma, animation tools After Effects, and ProtoPie; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with engineers to build and launch software applications, including incorporating design methodologies and engaging in testing and prototyping processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2 years of experience in crafting end to end user-focused onboarding journeys and creating compelling product demos, alongside developing solutions for growth-related domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $175,200 - $262,800/yr&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;50% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
