&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Privy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to make privacy and user ownership the default online. To do so, we build simple, flexible APIs and tools for developers that make it easy to build new products on crypto rails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Privy owns the abstractions and infrastructure layer above wallets, integrating across chains, third-party providers, and Stripe products like Treasury and Link. We get to solve hard technical problems while leveraging Stripe&#39;s distribution to reach customers like Ramp, Klarna, Deel, Kraken, Hyperliquid, and Fomo — powering experiences for both mainstream users and crypto natives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about Privy:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://privy.io/blog/announcing-our-acquisition-by-stripe&quot;&gt;Privy and Stripe: Bringing crypto to everyone&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Support Operations Associate at Privy, you will own the internal systems and workflows that keep our Developer Success team efficient, responsive, and focused. You’ll serve as air traffic control for support requests – triaging issues across our support stack (Pylon, Slack, HubSpot, and more), improving internal workflows, and maintaining CRM and support-data hygiene.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner closely with Account Management, Solutions Engineers, Forward Deployed Engineers, and Sales, while your day-to-day work will have impact across Privy, and Stripe as a whole.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-leverage operations role where attention to detail, a systems mindset, and a bias for execution will make you critical to making our customers successful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own triage and routing for inbound support tickets from both Privy developers and end users of Privy applications, ensuring issues are assigned, tracked, and resolved promptly and efficiently across the Developer Success team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain data hygiene, consistency, and accuracy across our support stack, including Pylon, Slack, HubSpot, and other systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams—including Sales, Engineering, and Product—to continuously improve the quality and efficiency of support processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain internal runbooks for ticket triage, escalations, and engineering-support handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify operational gaps and implement scalable workflows that help the team respond to customers more effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–3 years of experience in support operations, customer experience, technical program management, or a related operational role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and process-driven, with strong attention to detail and a bias toward action and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong intuition for customer sentiment and urgency, with sound judgment about how to prioritize and escalate issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with customer-support tooling, such as Pylon, Zendesk, Intercom, or Jira, and communication platforms like Slack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across systems and maintaining high-quality CRM data in tools such as HubSpot or Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, especially for issue tracking, coordination, and process documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems mindset and enthusiasm for building internal processes that scale with the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a developer-tools or infrastructure company, or experience working closely with engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with APIs, coding with AI, or using AI to automate tasks and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-122ebcb:
&lt;p&gt;Block is one company built from many blocks, all united by the same purpose of economic empowerment. The blocks that form our foundational teams — People, Finance, Counsel, Hardware, Information Security, Platform Infrastructure Engineering, and more — provide support and guidance at the corporate level. They work across business groups and around the globe, spanning time zones and disciplines to develop inclusive People policies, forecast finances, give legal counsel, safeguard systems, nurture new initiatives, and more. Every challenge creates possibilities, and we need different perspectives to see them all. Bring yours to Block.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Compensation Strategy &amp;amp; Program Lead&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team in an AI-first operating model—one where compensation rules, decisions, and reporting are increasingly encoded into automated workflows and self-service tools rather than handled case by case. As our primary compensation archetype, our Program Leads operate as internal product owners. Beyond hands-on partnership, they architect scalable frameworks, build self-service governance, and drive strategic total rewards programs across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working as part of a lean pod of peer Program Leads, you will take full ownership of major program pillars while collaborating closely on overarching compensation philosophy, automation initiatives, and data-driven tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own &amp;amp; Deliver Core Program Portfolios:&lt;/strong&gt; Take strategic and operational ownership of assigned program pillars (e.g., focal cycles, equity architecture, salary structures, geo-pay, promotions, or specialized incentive frameworks), with the agility to evolve and rotate portfolio ownership over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate within the Program Lead Cohort:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with peers to ensure strategic alignment, a cohesive global philosophy, and unified program delivery across different business areas and lifecycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build for Scalability &amp;amp; Self-Service:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Comp Ops and Data/Tooling to reduce manual triage by translating compensation rules into automated workflows, AI-assisted self-serve resources, and centralized reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish Policy as Code &amp;amp; Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Design transparent guardrails and delegation-of-authority frameworks that empower managers and People partners to make confident pay decisions autonomously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as a Macro-Level Strategic Advisor:&lt;/strong&gt; Advise senior leadership on talent market positioning, pay equity, and organizational design, prioritizing systemic improvements alongside the day-to-day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program / Product Orientation:&lt;/strong&gt; 6+ years of proven experience designing, iterating, and scaling enterprise compensation programs end-to-end, in addition to strong frontline consulting instincts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cohort Collaboration &amp;amp; Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; A high degree of independence in driving your portfolios, paired with strong cross-functional collaboration to maintain alignment across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems &amp;amp; AI-First Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; A strong instinct to solve edge cases through policy redesign, automation, and self-service tooling rather than repeated manual intervention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Data Rigor:&lt;/strong&gt; High proficiency in quantitative modeling and evaluating macro compensation metrics, with comfort partnering alongside data and operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Substantial compensation experience (level to be calibrated to the role) and fluency with modern comp planning, HRIS, and data/analytics tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
