&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-006u2z2:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bridge is building financial infrastructure that makes money more programmable and global. The Financial Partnerships team develops the ecosystem that powers Bridge and Stripe’s stablecoin products and financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works across Bridge and Stripe to develop strategic relationships with banks, exchanges, asset managers, liquidity providers, and stablecoin ecosystem partners. These partnerships support reserve management, liquidity, distribution, and card-related products for both businesses and their shared customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior Partnership Development Manager, you will define and execute the financial-partnership strategy that powers Bridge and Stripe’s stablecoin products and financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a strategic ecosystem of financial-partner relationships across markets. You will turn market insight into durable, high-impact partnerships, from strategy and negotiation through launch, expansion, and ongoing performance management. You will work directly with senior Stripe leaders and external executives to make investment tradeoffs, align priorities, and shape long-term product and partnership strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and lead multi-year partnership strategy across reserves, liquidity, distribution, card-related products, and the stablecoin ecosystem, using market and commercial insight to shape Bridge and Stripe priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a strategic financial-partner ecosystem across markets, including partnership health, commercial performance, executive alignment, escalations, and expansion opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source, evaluate, structure, negotiate, and lead high-impact partnerships with banks, exchanges, asset managers, liquidity providers, and stablecoin ecosystem partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set end-to-end deal strategy for complex, novel, or multi-market partnerships with material financial, product, operational, or regulatory implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead company-level tradeoffs across partner economics, customer needs, product requirements, operational readiness, risk, and long-term strategic value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Treasury, Legal, Compliance, Risk, Operations, Finance, Engineering, and go-to-market teams to set requirements, align senior stakeholders, and execute shared priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a differentiated point of view on financial services and digital assets, represent Stripe and Bridge with senior external stakeholders, and share expertise that strengthens the broader Partnerships organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, business development, corporate development, strategic finance, treasury, or a related field, including ownership of complex, high-impact external partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently set partnership strategy, influence senior executives, and drive cross-functional alignment on ambiguous, high-stakes company priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of structuring, negotiating, and managing high-value, multi-year partnerships with material strategic, financial, product, operational, or regulatory implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience working with financial institutions or infrastructure providers, such as banks, exchanges, asset managers, market makers, liquidity providers, payments companies, or stablecoin ecosystem participants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgment and experience leading both commercial and technical partnership conversations with senior internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in stablecoins, crypto, card issuing, or stablecoin-linked card programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing partnership strategy across multiple markets or partner types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing a company with industry groups, at conferences, or with senior external executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or guiding peers on partnership strategy, complex negotiations, or cross-functional execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1xb8pgs:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world is having a monetization moment – every ambitious company is replatforming their billing solution in response to AI. Stripes Billing is a team of deep functional and technical specialists who both lead and advise on deals for one of the most strategically important products in Stripe’s portfolio. Billing Sales is tasked with attacking a $100B market opportunity for automating the entire order to cash process and helping companies not get left behind in the AI era.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Head of Grower Sales (Billing),&amp;nbsp; you will use your leadership and management skills to manage and grow a team of Account Executives to drive expansion and retention of Stripe Billing across the AMER region. You will build and lead a team of sellers, while collaborating with the core sales leadership, marketing, product marketing, and product teams to develop deep product and industry knowledge and drive strategic deals. You will own the coaching, development, and performance of your team, driving the forecast of the business. You will be instrumental in leading in-depth product discussions with existing and prospective customers and building and executing against our go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop and lead a team of product sales executives focused on expansion and retention of our largest Billing Users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create go-to-market plans and solutions to meet our customer needs, in collaboration with Product, Sales, Finance and Marketing stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day operations, with a focus on performance against key sales metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for driving revenue, increasing attach rates, and new client acquisition at high rates of growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and guide the team in developing consultative and solution-based sales skills through all facets of the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get hands on engaged in the largest, most strategic opportunities, leading executive relationships and helping the team win new customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate, and enable individual development to promote career growth of direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with clarity and context with a compelling plan in line with Stripe’s direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create structure and focus for GTM ideas and product sales campaigns that the product team is exploring. Drive execution and measurement. Analyse results and make recommendations for action in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Constantly innovate and improve programs and program management mechanisms, suggesting new ideas, sharing best practices, and improving the business and customer engagement model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an adept sales leader, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization. You have a reputation and drive for building strategic relationships with executives (CEO, CFO, and CTO) across the AMER region, including core markets like NA, CA, and LATAM. You excel in building clear plans to grow a region through a high-functioning sales team, with strategic thought leadership and strong management. You see value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require both deep product understanding and technical knowledge, especially for AI industry users. You’re as comfortable working with clients as with internal stakeholders (including executives) and are excited to become an expert and share your knowledge. You possess an organized, self-starter mindset and excellent communication skills, with a track record for improving the processes and organizations around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of sales leadership experience, launching and growing high-functioning sales teams/products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in hyper-growth SaaS environments across the AMER region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in finance, revenue management, financial services, or similar software services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to be a self-starter, capable of driving business results without significant supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic “roll up your sleeves” mentality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, particularly for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke agreements with startup, SMB, and Commercial businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-0jhil2t:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the team + role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the trading team, our mission is to build highly intuitive, rapid-execution trading interfaces that make investing accessible and seamless for millions of users. Within our collaborative and high-performing design culture, we value deep craft, transparency, and a relentless focus on user experience. Together, we are investing heavily in design improvements and advanced tooling to support our next phase of product growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Designer, you will be fully accountable for the design strategy and execution of our core equities business line. You will lead the design of our central, longstanding product from initial concept to launch. In this high-visibility individual contributor role, you will collaborate with engineering, product management, and legal teams, communicate transparently with leadership, and help define our long-term product evolution. Your work will directly impact millions of customers, ensuring they have an exceptional experience when trading on Robinhood!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA and New York, NY offices, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and execute the product design strategy, creating cohesive and rapid trading experiences for millions of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and redesign core trading surfaces, such as the order form and ladder chart, to improve interaction speed and simplify complex financial concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate directly with engineering, product management, design leadership, and legal partners to guide projects from initial concept to final production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize and assess AI tools within your design process to optimize workflows and propose novel, user-friendly design solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide transparent project updates to leadership and help shape the long-term design standards across our broader trading team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing complex user interfaces and large, multifaceted products, ideally within financial technology, trading platforms, or complex editing applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, lead projects from zero to one, and deliver results against weekly milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills to coordinate across multiple teams and present design decisions clearly to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep focus on interaction craft, with a demonstrated ability to evaluate how multiple product surfaces work together as a cohesive system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to exploring and integrating emerging technologies, including AI tools, to enhance your design and prototyping processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top Tier benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the best AI tools on the market and continuous AI skill-building for every employee, technical or not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet - a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$166,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$195,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$146,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$172,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$129,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$152,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-1ecrmne:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h1 class=&quot;section-header section-header--large font-primary&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;About Digital Asset &amp;amp; the Canton Network&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Digital Asset builds the technologies that are reshaping the foundations of financial markets. Our mission is to create the world’s most trusted, privacy-enabled, and interoperable digital infrastructure for global finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of this mission is the Canton Network - the blockchain purpose-built for institutional finance. Uniquely combining privacy, compliance, and scalability, Canton enables real-time, secure settlement across multiple asset classes. Governed by the Canton Foundation with participation from leading financial institutions, it is the proven link between the promise of blockchain and the power of global finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2014 and headquartered in New York City, with offices in London, Zurich, Budapest, Hong Kong, and Sydney— we are on a mission to transform finance— and that transformation is now playing out rapidly on the Canton Network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you’re interested in playing a crucial role at the intersection of traditional and crypto-capital markets and want to help bring the next trillion dollars of finance on-chain, join us.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Staff CX Software Engineer is a role for people that come with prior experience and exposure to distributed computing, Canton Network and our product, including topology and performance considerations. These individuals will stand in front of a client to provide sound advice, and to provide a technical leadership role for the team when working with clients on client solutions. They are comfortable with facing off to executive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides direction to clients on physical and logical architectures for Canton Network solutions and integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gives direction on Canton Network topology concerns.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinates and leads planning of complex, cross-functional initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as the expert in Canton Network and DA Products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverages proficiency in multiple other languages.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Estimates highly complex solutions and systematically decompose complex technical problems to arrive at a solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defines strategy for a performance test plan: proactively reasons about, identifies, and remediates performance issues in solutions using Canton Network and DA Product components; and prioritizes salient performance concerns of a system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverages a level of expertise in a subset of Canton Network and DA Products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acts as a subject matter expert for other CX staff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works with and customizes helm charts to enable a client easy onboarding to k8s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering experience, including a history of successfully delivering complex systems or integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Breadth: Comprehensive understanding of full-cycle technical delivery, from system design and API strategies to cloud architecture and data modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has working knowledge of our product and Canton OS source code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery Excellence: Ability to establish engineering standards, design reusable components, and unblock delivery teams across multiple workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consultative Mindset: Experience in a consulting or client-facing role; able to translate complex business requirements into scalable technical roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial services domain knowledge and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a fast-moving environment with multiple competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious, pragmatic and adaptable, and able to learn quickly in complex environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Digital Asset, we are committed to compensation structures that reward impact consistently across our global teams. We support our people at every stage of life with comprehensive, family-forward benefits and flexible working models designed to help you do your best work.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support the well-being of our team members. Health and insurance benefits vary by region to ensure local relevance and compliance, and may include medical, dental, and vision coverage.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Digital Asset is an equal opportunity employer committed. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, religion, sexual orientation, age, disability, citizenship status, veteran status, or any other basis protected by applicable law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Eligibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; If and as required by applicable law, all persons hired to work at Digital Asset will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the location for which they have an offer to work and to complete the necessary employment eligibility verification documents upon hire.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ccommodations&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Applicants with disabilities who require accommodation during the application or interview process should contact &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:talent@digitalasset.com&quot;&gt;talent@digitalasset.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;California Privacy Act (CCPA)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; If you are based in California, we encourage you to read this important information for California residents linked &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.digitalasset.com/ccpacpranotice&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-199c3bj:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;As a Screening Compliance Analyst II on the CX Compliance team within Customer Experience, you&#39;ll conduct end-to-end screenings of customers, individuals, and entities to protect Coinbase from financial crime risk. This team ensures our global operations comply with AML, sanctions, and KYC regulatory requirements while delivering consistently high-quality outcomes. You&#39;ll analyze screening results independently, escalate potential compliance risks to the Financial Crime Risk Service (FCCS) team, and contribute to process improvements that strengthen the screening function&#39;s accuracy and scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end screening processes to identify potential risks associated with customers, individuals, and entities using screening tools and databases, ensuring timely and accurate disposition of alerts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze transaction activity and KYC information, conduct due diligence research, and recommend whether activity warrants escalation to the Financial Crime Risk Service (FCCS) team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain detailed documentation of screening decisions to demonstrate compliance with regulations, internal policies, and audit requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incorporate feedback from the Quality Assurance team and participate in calibration sessions to improve screening accuracy and consistency across the function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps in screening procedures and contribute recommendations for process improvements that reduce risk exposure and increase operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in compliance screening, financial crimes prevention, KYC/CDD, or investigations within financial services, crypto, or fintech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to analyze customer information against sanctions lists, PEP databases, and adverse media sources, and document findings with accuracy sufficient to meet regulatory audit standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with onboarding/KYC processes, sanctions screening tools (e.g., Hummingbird, World-Check, or similar), and regulatory frameworks governing customer due diligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to clearly summarize screening findings in writing, escalate risks with supporting evidence, and communicate outcomes to compliance stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability to support a 24/7 screening operation, including flexibility for shift work as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*This is an In-Office role (Based out of Hyderabad, India)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;The target annual &lt;strong&gt;base&lt;/strong&gt; salary for this position can range as detailed below. Total compensation may &lt;strong&gt;also&lt;/strong&gt; include bonus eligibility and benefits (including medical, dental, and vision).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual base salary range (excluding bonus):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;₹998,070&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;₹1,050,600 INR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Application Limit: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Candidates may submit a maximum of 3 applications within a 6-month period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer: &lt;/strong&gt;Coinbase is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. Applicants with criminal histories will be considered consistent with applicable federal, state, and local laws.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
