&lt;h3&gt;Sales Director, New Business APAC&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and lead the team that wins ComplyAdvantage&#39;s next generation of customers across Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who we are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make a safer world.&lt;/strong&gt; Our mission is to neutralize financial crime and protect the global financial ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar.&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to constant improvement, pushing the limits of our AI technology and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See it, own it, drive it forward.&lt;/strong&gt; We empower our people to take initiative, identify opportunities, and execute solutions with full accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Win as one team.&lt;/strong&gt; Success is a collective effort; we collaborate across functions, hubs, and borders to achieve our goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ComplyAdvantage is the financial industry&#39;s leading source of AI-driven financial crime risk data and detection technology. Our mission is to make a safer world by neutralizing the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing, corruption, and other financial crimes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 1,000 companies rely on us to understand who they&#39;re doing business with, powered by a global, real-time database of people and companies. Our solutions surface thousands of risk events daily from millions of structured and unstructured data points.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have five global hubs — New York, London, Singapore, Lisbon, and Cluj-Napoca — and are backed by Goldman Sachs, Ontario Teachers, Index Ventures, and Balderton Capital.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The opportunity&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;APAC is one of the fastest-growing regions for ComplyAdvantage, and it needs a sales leader to build the engine that scales it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Sales Director to run our new business function across the region: developing pipeline through a team of two Business Development Representatives (BDRs), converting it through a team of four Account Executives (AEs), and carrying the number for new-logo acquisition across APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to the Managing Director (MD), with your two BDRs and four AEs reporting into you. This is a &quot;see it, own it, drive it forward&quot; role: you&#39;re not inheriting a fixed playbook, you&#39;re building the team, the standards, and the operating rhythm that will define how ComplyAdvantage wins new business in the region for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the new business number for APAC.&lt;/strong&gt; Carry accountability for new-logo acquisition across the region, from qualified pipeline through to closed-won revenue. Drive average deal value up through stronger qualification and multi-threading, and identify early cross-sell and expansion opportunities across our product suite, including transaction monitoring, agentic AI, and ongoing screening.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and lead the team.&lt;/strong&gt; Recruit exceptional people into your team of two BDRs and four AEs, and sell them on the mission - you are part of what they&#39;re choosing. Coach in a way that builds independent operators rather than dependence: develop your team through data-driven feedback, regular development planning, and a player-coach presence on live deals, while giving people the room to work things out for themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the regional operating rhythm.&lt;/strong&gt; Stand up the standards that let the function scale in APAC: qualification criteria, territory planning, accurate forecasting, and pipeline and CRM hygiene, alongside onboarding and enablement paths built specifically for a new-business motion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Win as one team across functions and geographies.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Revenue Operations, Marketing, and Enterprise on inbound routing, thresholds, and nurture programs, and maintain a feedback loop to Product and to our global commercial leadership so APAC&#39;s insights shape the wider go-to-market strategy. Adopt and help refine the AI-assisted tools and workflows being built centrally, adapting them to what works for the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Represent APAC in the room.&lt;/strong&gt; Engage senior decision-makers at fintechs, payment companies, banks, and credit unions across the region, and act as ComplyAdvantage&#39;s voice in strategic regional conversations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a builder with commercial range - someone who can carry a new-business number and stand up the team and system that produce it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven sales leadership experience, ideally in SaaS, cloud, fintech, or regtech, with the instincts of a player-coach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building or scaling a new business function, including hiring, ramping, and coaching BDRs and AEs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of growing new-business revenue in a B2B environment, with some exposure to cross-sell or expansion motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Value-based selling and qualification rigor: you map solutions to real business pain, and you&#39;re comfortable qualifying out when the pain or the champion isn&#39;t there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Live and breathe MEDDIC, embedding it into the team’s sales process and holding the team accountable to its consistent execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A coaching philosophy that develops independent operators — you give people space to figure things out, with the inspection cadence to keep them on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and a fast-changing environment: proactive, resilient, and entrepreneurial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The credibility to engage senior decision-makers at fintechs, payment companies, banks, and credit unions, and to represent APAC in strategic discussions with global leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data fluency: you run the business on clean numbers, forecast accurately, and make territory and prioritization decisions analytically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to raise the bar and win as one team, demonstrating the cultural attributes needed to thrive in a high-growth, collaborative environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity as we want you to have a part of what we are building&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited Time Off Policy- A work-life balance and focus on our well-being are critical to keep us performing at our best&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to our Employee Assistance Programme to support you and your family’s wellbeing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical Insurance including enhanced Dental and Vision support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual learning budget to drive your performance and career development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Budget to set up your home office upon joining&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to empower every business to eliminate financial crime.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By harnessing AI, a unified platform, and an extensive partner ecosystem, we help customers turn compliance into a catalyst for growth, operational resilience, and enduring regulatory trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 3,000 enterprises across 75 countries rely on our end-to-end platform and the world’s most comprehensive financial crime risk intelligence. With full-stack agentic automation, we help organizations automate up to 95% of KYC, AML, and sanctions reviews, cut onboarding times by 50%, reduce false positives by 70%, and handle 7x more work with the same staff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ComplyAdvantage is headquartered in London and has global hubs in New York, Lisbon, Singapore, and Cluj-Napoca. It is backed by Balderton Capital, Index Ventures, Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan, Goldman Sachs, and Andreessen Horowitz. Learn more about compliance re-engineered for the age of AI at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://complyadvantage.com&quot;&gt;complyadvantage.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-098aavq:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;BitGo is the leading infrastructure provider of digital asset solutions, delivering custody, wallets, staking, trading, financing, and settlement services from regulated cold storage. Since our founding in 2013, we have focused on enabling our clients to securely navigate the digital asset space. With a global presence and multiple Trust companies, BitGo serves thousands of institutions, including many of the industry&#39;s top brands, exchanges, and platforms, and millions of retail investors worldwide. As the operational backbone of the digital economy, BitGo handles a significant portion of Bitcoin network transactions and is the largest independent digital asset custodian, and staking provider, in the world. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://www.bitgo.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://www.bitgo.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;www.bitgo.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced, hands-on Onboarding Manager to own and drive BitGo’s client onboarding function for our MAS-regulated Singapore entity. Reporting to BitGo’s APAC Managing Director, this role will own the end-end client lifecycle; including client onboarding, ongoing due diligence, periodic reviews and off-boarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a player/coach role where you will manage and mentor an Onboarding Associate while remaining deeply hands-on in day-to-day execution. You will own and manage onboarding cases directly, and help establish strong operating standards across the function. You will have the opportunity to shape BitGo Singapore’s onboarding operating model as the business continues to scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines strong KYC/KYB expertise and a solid understanding of MAS regulatory requirements paired with commercial and operational judgement. You are resourceful, pragmatic, and creative in solving problems, comfortable owning complex cases end to end, and able to find practical ways forward when the path is not always clear. You partner effectively with cross-functional stakeholders, challenge inefficient ways of working, and thrive in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Onboarding and Offboarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and progress onboarding applications end to end, ensuring high execution quality, robust documentation and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage onboarding queues and priorities to maintain strong throughput and adherence to service level expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify information gaps and manage requests for information efficiently to minimize unnecessary client friction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Compliance on cases requiring additional review or escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own client offboarding end to end, including sanctions and risk driven terminations, dormant and inactive account closures, and coordination of account wind-down with Operations and Compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and manage client-facing exit communications, ensuring exits are executed cleanly, defensibly, and with appropriate documentation and record retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales, Customer Success, Solutions Engineering, Operations, Compliance, and other cross-functional stakeholders to move clients through onboarding effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate onboarding requirements and blockers clearly to internal stakeholders and help drive cases toward resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance regulatory and risk requirements with commercial priorities and client experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence, Controls and Assurance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and continuously improve onboarding processes, workflows, controls, and operating standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Data Science and Analytics, Compliance, and Operations teams to improve onboarding systems and workflow logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development of onboarding quality assurance practices and scalable service level frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, track, and report onboarding metrics including turnaround time and backlog aging and use them to drive improvements in efficiency and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support external audit and regulatory examinations, including producing onboarding and CDD files for sampling, participating in process walkthroughs, and evidencing controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own remediation of audit and review findings relating to onboarding, tracking actions through to closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the APAC onboarding function as a whole, providing guidance and subject matter expertise to colleagues handling onboarding cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish high standards for execution, ownership, documentation, and client experience across the APAC onboarding function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by example as a hands-on operator, taking ownership of outcomes rather than simply managing workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in client onboarding, KYB/AML operations, financial crime operations, or a closely related function in the fintech, digital assets or payments industry; 1–2 years of experience leading or owning an onboarding function is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of MAS’ regulatory requirements and expectations around KYB, corporate structures, beneficial ownership, and AML onboarding processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting external audits or regulatory reviews, including evidencing controls and remediating findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial awareness and ability to balance risk requirements with onboarding efficiency and client experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management and communication skills with the ability to work effectively across Sales, Operations, Compliance, and other teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage escalations and make sound decisions in complex or ambiguous situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong critical thinking, problem solving, pattern recognition, and project management skills, with excellent attention to detail, organization, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment where processes and requirements continue to evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive mindset with a track record of identifying problems, challenging inefficient processes, and driving improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mandarin language skills will be a significant advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join BitGo?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Disrupting an industry takes vision, innovation, passion, technical chops, drive to deliver, collaboration, and execution. Join a team of great people who strive for excellence and personify our corporate values of ownership, craftsmanship, and open communication. We are looking for new colleagues who bring innovative ways of thinking and problem solving, and who want to be part of the team that changes the world’s financial markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here are some of the benefits of working at BitGo:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base salary, bonus, and stock options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer equipment to suit your needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great colleagues and inspiring startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1fpf3re:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The credit risk operations team plays a critical role in ensuring a healthy financial ecosystem for businesses around the world. This team will directly impact the company&#39;s bottom line and growth capabilities by supporting new and emerging businesses. The Credit Operations team is responsible for conducting credit risk assessments, underwriting small and mid-size users, and proposing mitigation strategies that enable Stripe to take smart risks for our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will manage and develop a group of Credit Risk Operations Associates that are focused on commercial credit underwriting and risk mitigation. The Credit Risk Operations Team Lead will cultivate the engagement of their team members while guiding them to be the best they can be, through feedback, coaching, mentoring, and advocacy within the organization. This means helping to set team goals, and using metrics to efficiently measure and guide team performance in pursuit of those goals. To be a fit, you will have a strong operations mindset, possess a deep understanding of commercial credit risk, be able to move quickly, and be passionate about delivering an incredible user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, coach, and develop a new team of in-office Credit Risk Operations Associates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute on commercial credit underwriting frameworks that allow your team to evaluate business models and financial statements of successful venture-backed startups to established entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide your team to identify commercial credit risk and propose risk mitigation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive strong operational delivery and process improvement helping to maintain credit risk tolerance and&amp;nbsp; balance credit&amp;nbsp; loss and customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a great culture and ensure team members are happy, effective, and growing in their career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear goals and direction, and provide regular feedback on team members’ performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be data-driven in your analysis of performance, and in your decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transmit and foster our values, serving as a beacon of Stripe’s user-centric philosophy and culture of transparency, empathy, inclusion, and empowerment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage operational performance to deliver KPIs&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage capacity and scheduling to ensure adequate coverage&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help resolve roadblocks and issues as they arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a point of escalation for complex credit underwriting reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 6+ years of experience with commercial credit underwriting, financial statement analysis, risk modeling and cash flow forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to transform business and financial data into a cohesive narrative that outlines potential credit risks and presents dynamic mitigation strategies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2+ years of direct people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership skills, strong analytical abilities, and excellent communication skills are essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to partner effectively with internal globally distributed stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational background including new process launches and service delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill and credibility doing the core work of a user facing team with a high bar for quality, and a willingness to lead by example&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for process improvement and innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree/diploma in Finance or Accounting, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, e-commerce, or fintech mitigating credit risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building and scaling new teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-0rszvdi:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps Stripe users extend their online presence into the physical world. The Terminal team’s mission is to make it as easy for businesses to accept in-person payments as the Stripe API has done for online payments. With Terminal, businesses can unlock in-person payments use cases that are right for their business model, whether it’s creating a flagship retail experience, extending their website to a pop-up store, or enabling a mobile point of sale at their next event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a&amp;nbsp; Software Quality Assurance Engineer to join the Stripe Terminal Device Software Quality Assurance team. In this role, you will own the quality assurance process and results for firmware and device operating system components across our payment terminal devices. You&#39;ll work closely with software development teams to define quality standards, develop test strategies, and drive software quality improvements through technical expertise and process enhancements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own software quality for Terminal device software components, including firmware and the device operating system, and ensure software quality targets are met for customers. Collaborate with developers during software planning, change review, and release meetings to understand new features, specifications, expected behaviors, and the impact and risks of changes. Create spot tests before branch cut.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand customer use cases, Product Requirements Documents, and Software Design Documents. Work with developers to create test plans that improve coverage across configurations, user scenarios, and reliability testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform Bluetooth validation across multiple devices, edge cases, and recovery scenarios. Validate devices with enterprise network configurations and security types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute testing for power performance, battery behavior, sleep and wake reliability, and resilience under extended or degraded operating conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain lab setups and test environments that reflect production-like usage conditions and support repeatable validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-lead software quality incident remediation with engineering teams, including root cause analysis and solution development. Establish and maintain software quality assurance processes, and influence cross-functional teams at Stripe and drive quality and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and optimize test cases. Collaborate with automation engineers to expand automated test coverage, guide manual software quality assurance team members in high-quality software testing, and mentor junior software quality engineers on technical skills, test design, work quality, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, software engineering, or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of software quality assurance experience for embedded systems or firmware, including analyzing software changes and assessing their impact on test coverage by reviewing release notes and software design documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing test strategies, test plans, and test cases based on product requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify the root causes of software defects and proactively identify and mitigate risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, communication, ownership, and influencing skills to drive quality improvements across teams, along with excellent verbal and written English communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payment terminal devices, EMV certification, or Payment Card Industry compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of embedded systems, real-time operating systems, and firmware development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payment processing systems or financial technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of mentoring junior team members on technical skills and test design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

job-1eg38dn:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. We build the most powerful and flexible tools for running an internet business — handling billions of dollars each year and enabling millions of businesses worldwide to scale faster by building on Stripe. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our tax team works with Stripes across the company to develop an efficient operating model as our international business scales and expands into new markets and launches new products. EMEA Tax supports Stripe’s growth across the region by helping the company meet its tax obligations, manage tax risk, and make well-supported decisions as Stripe’s products, systems, and operations evolve.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be based in Dublin and report to the EMEA Tax lead, who is located in Dublin. This role will develop and lead a best-in-class global R&amp;amp;D incentives programme.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be Stripe’s&amp;nbsp; European R&amp;amp;D incentives lead, responsible for developing and leading Stripe’s R&amp;amp;D incentives programmes in Ireland and the UK. You will support Stripe’s US federal and state research-credit programme and will explore new opportunities as Stripe continues to expand globally. You will build trusted relationships with engineering and product teams, establish repeatable processes for identifying and documenting qualifying work, and ensure Stripe can support its global R&amp;amp;D incentives claims with contemporaneous evidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You must be able to work effectively with cross-functional teams and independently lead complex, high-impact work. You will translate complex technical activity into clear documentation, and help Stripe enhance its global R&amp;amp;D incentives processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Stripe’s European lead and technical expert for R&amp;amp;D incentive and grant claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the annual US federal and state research-credit study, quarterly tax-return and FIN 48 estimates, and tax-audit requests relating to US federal and state research credits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end technical documentation required to support Stripe’s European R&amp;amp;D incentives, from project identification and engineering interviews through evidence collection, writing technical reports, and retention of audit-ready files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the analysis of eligible R&amp;amp;D expenditure and preparation of robust financial calculations to support Stripe’s R&amp;amp;D incentives claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and lead process improvements that enhance the efficiency and robustness of Stripe’s R&amp;amp;D incentive claims, including strengthening controls, developing scalable and automated process enhancements, and improving data and documentation quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with technical responses to tax authority queries relating to R&amp;amp;D incentives claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Finance, Engineering, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor changes in relevant tax legislation, tax authority guidance, and R&amp;amp;D incentive and claim practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor engineering growth across Stripe and assess new R&amp;amp;D tax incentives and grant opportunities globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–8 years of relevant experience preparing or managing Irish R&amp;amp;D tax credit claims or global R&amp;amp;D incentive claims.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engineering or computer science qualification or a technology-related background combined with finance qualifications or experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the Irish R&amp;amp;D tax credit regime, including the assessment of qualifying activities, technical uncertainty, systematic investigation or experimentation, technical documentation, and eligible expenditure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and oral communication skills, including strong technical report writing and engineering-interviewing skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project-management experience, with the ability to independently lead high-impact projects, manage detailed evidence requirements, and deliver across multiple jurisdictions’ deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, sound professional judgment, and the confidence to challenge unclear project descriptions or unsupported assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, informal, and often ambiguous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to learn, ability to quickly acquire knowledge, and ability to work autonomously and within a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with UK and US federal and state research credits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Irish Revenue R&amp;amp;D audits, tax authority enquiries, or evidence reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analysing eligible R&amp;amp;D expenditure and preparing financial calculations for R&amp;amp;D tax-credit claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying for and preparing documentation in support of IDA grants in Ireland, or R&amp;amp;D tax credits and grants globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-office expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Office-assigned Stripes in most of our locations are currently expected to spend at least 50% of the time in a given month in their local office or with users. This expectation may vary depending on role, team and location. This approach helps strike a balance between bringing people together for in-person collaboration and learning from each other, while supporting flexibility when possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay and benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual salary range for this role in the primary location is €94,600–€141,800. This range may change if you are hired in another location. This salary range may be inclusive of several career levels at Stripe and will be narrowed during the interview process based on a number of factors, including the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and specific location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specific benefits and details about what compensation is included in the salary range listed above will vary depending on the applicant’s location and can be discussed in more detail during the interview process. Benefits/additional compensation for this role may include equity, company bonus; retirement plans; health benefits; and wellness stipends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We look forward to hearing from you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, we&#39;re looking for people with passion, grit, and integrity. You&#39;re encouraged to apply even if your experience doesn&#39;t precisely match the job description. Your skills and passion will stand out—and set you apart—especially if your career has taken some extraordinary twists and turns. At Stripe, we welcome diverse perspectives and people who think rigorously and aren&#39;t afraid to challenge assumptions. Join us.&lt;/p&gt;

job-1bt33ci:
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2 ace-line old-record-id-doxlgBf035uaq9uFOlfIpBvpHye&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-doxlgL44UKGZInnVDg8qVIVb96b&quot;&gt;At OKX, we believe that the future will be reshaped by crypto, and ultimately contribute to every individual&#39;s freedom. OKX is a leading crypto exchange, and the developer of OKX Wallet, giving millions access to crypto trading and decentralized crypto applications (dApps). OKX is also a trusted brand by hundreds of large institutions seeking access to crypto markets. We are safe and reliable, backed by our Proof of Reserves. Across our multiple offices globally, we are united by our core principles: &lt;em&gt;We Before Me&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Do the Right Thing&lt;/em&gt;, and &lt;em&gt;Get Things Done&lt;/em&gt;. These shared values drive our culture, shape our processes, and foster a friendly, rewarding, and diverse environment for every OK-er. OKX is part of OKG, a group that brings the value of Blockchain to users around the world, through our leading products OKX, OKX Wallet, OKLink and more.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2 ace-line old-record-id-R8eidjpqForcoYxTZHLlUInigJd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-doxlgUAQMlK2gcm1bSPEYUCXBPf&quot;&gt;The Global Legal team provides legal advice and guidance to OKX and its affiliated entities across all coverage areas and geographic locations, and supports business growth by working with all teams within the company to help them achieve their goals. Our team has attorneys around the world, and handles legal matters in literally hundreds of countries across the globe.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2 ace-line old-record-id-doxlgikicwVFIix3ETA6wVuMSTh&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-bullet1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-ZmSKd6YP0oRju6xV8Ealv3CNgUc&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Criminal referrals, law enforcement and prosecution support:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-bullet2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-ZCvqdEm9goAIaOxa3TglvlwJgPc&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Own OKX’s framework for identifying conduct that warrants criminal referral and work directly with relevant authorities to follow-through on charging and prosecution.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-AjBmddkIKozgjbx5mFulNxCngc6&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Working closely with teams in Risk and Compliance, build and package referral files to an acceptable prosecutorial standard.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-U02Id4JulofR97xTBTnlOramgkd&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Drive referred matters through to charge and prosecution.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-B5Z5dR0P7ophwOxz4HulAI6pgDe&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Serve as the senior legal relationship owner for police and prosecutors and develop and maintain relationships throughout the region.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-TB2Odh1alokCGnxRTKPlvsdNgQb&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Civil litigation:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-bullet2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-PQQWduTmJoDrQ6x4Ru9lX4vngNg&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Own and lead the regional civil docket end-to-end including intake, early case assessment, strategy and resolution both on the defence and plaintiff side.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-ZlCBdKmxho8WRQxf5bJl71PFgZg&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Lead the affirmative side of civil disputes, e.g., recovery actions, injunctions, disclosure applications, applications against counterparties, service providers, bad actors, etc.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-F0LVdY7h1oDKA6xtzK3l8TdDgFd&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Assess and develop strategy for defensive civil claims including consumer claims at volume, market conduct issues, and coordinate on relevant contentious employment matters.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-YFDjdBt2toSPQWxzASUlZ2SggRd&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Manage and lead commercial disputes.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Ed3SdoNtXorsBgx0Av4lLlG1gkc&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Arbitration&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-bullet2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-PbfadMhIsoh4YQx4I20lpmWGgQz&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Real depth of arbitration experience preferred. Lead OKX’s arbitrations in the region as counsel-in-charge, including pleadings, document production, witness and expert evidence, hearings, enforcement proceedings.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-JLFldGr8aoblC1xGnnClslv0g8b&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Assess mass arbitration exposure in conjunction with business priorities and develop strategic plan for risk mitigation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-QalVdR8VQoitJsx6goelQmR9gxf&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Advise business and business Legal teams on dispute resolution clauses.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-DgUZdiPaHoCppvxaNCzlA82ygkg&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Regulatory Enforcement &amp;amp; Internal Investigations&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-bullet2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Jac3d9uHqoyJ4xxCg7plRWqCgxf&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Develop strategy and lead OKX’s response to regulatory enforcement inquiries working in close collaboration with Global Regulatory Legal team.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-O022dIYjYo55WWx1gFYloS2ZgMg&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Scope, lead and where appropriate personally conduct sensitive internal investigations. Deliver as needed root causes analysis and collaborate cross-functionally on remediation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Y4Sfd9ZPfoKiDAx0sBMl1JRqg6e&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Team leadership: &lt;span class=&quot;text-only&quot;&gt;Lead and develop the in-region team, embed AI to drive efficiency, and partner across Legal, Compliance, Risk, Finance, HR and Communications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-VhmudhA0voDnrgx7RUOl1oJwg6g&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div data-lark-html-role=&quot;root&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text-only&quot;&gt;External counsel, budget and reporting: Select and manage external counsel and experts; own the regional contentious budget and in-house/outside counsel decisions; ensure proper matter tracking and disclosure; deliver decision-ready reporting to the Global Head and governance forums.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2 ace-line old-record-id-doxlgIshb9SqkyFtBToiCGL08ph&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For In You &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-bullet1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-K0gwdz7pZog7pQxNDlfl4yEBgYc&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Admitted as solicitor or barrister in Hong Kong; based in Hong Kong or Singapore.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Iog9dHODIo3qljxJt6ElZIcIgCf&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;12+ years post-qualification experience in contentious work, with Asia experience. More experienced candidates will be considered.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-PXWKdgb7poEdQtxh4a6lZkytgRh&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Prosecutorial or criminal enforcement background (prosecutor, government trial lawyer, or criminal/regulatory enforcement counsel), plus arbitration and trial experience and a track record leading a team. Prior in-house experience preferred.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Ty0Qdam8yomLmpxmKbplDCPEg3e&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Sound judgment under ambiguity; able to operate in a fast-paced environment with a growing regulatory landscape.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-LL2Ad6zTxo3ky7xClHilwLMJgKC&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fluent written and spoken English. Mandarin and/or Cantonese at professional working level strongly preferred — a material advantage for law enforcement and regulatory engagement in the region.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-AdCpd7wmOonV7BxnG1alwycEg6g&quot; data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Willing to travel across the region.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
