&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role requires a variety of&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;markg6nqix883&quot; data-markjs=&quot;true&quot; data-ogac=&quot;&quot; data-ogab=&quot;&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-ogsb=&quot;&quot;&gt;physical&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;activities to effectively perform essential job functions. The position involves frequent walking (75%), sitting (50%), and standing (50%), with regular bending, stooping, and reaching (25–50%). Employees must be able to lift, carry, push, and pull items up to 25 lbs. Strong fine motor skills and full use of hands are essential, as the role demands constant grasping, writing/typing, and use of technology. Visual and auditory acuity—including color, depth, peripheral vision, and the ability to adjust focus—is required&amp;nbsp;100% of the time. Occasional driving or climbing may also be necessary.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you need assistance with this application, please contact (636) 227-2600. Please do not contact the office directly – only resumes submitted through this website will be considered.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;EyeCare Partners is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All applicants will be considered for employment without attention to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran or disability status.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

job-1nxpgjs:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Account Managers work cross-functionally to support Stripe’s largest and most complex users. Through trusted relationships we offer customized, strategic consultations and proactively identify opportunity areas to help businesses deliver more value to their customers, optimize technical operations on their teams, and accelerate their global growth with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will strategically support Stripe’s billing user segment consisting of complex and high-growth billing companies. You will develop deep relationships with your assigned accounts’ key stakeholders through frequent in-person meetings and technical account planning sessions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide a gold standard experience to your assigned accounts&#39; key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the wider Operations team to provide current state, resources, and knowledge to enable a gold standard experience across teams interacting directly with the user via support channels, external documentation, or product/feature feedback or development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster long-term user relationships that grow loyalty to Stripe and Stripe products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally both internally and within your user&#39;s organizations to provide and implement operational solutions on subjects not limited to fraud/disputes, declines, product adoption, and global expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Account Management and other user-facing teams as part of a larger effort to support users on Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead user-facing meetings both in person and through video chat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on the continued design of this support offering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create user-facing content for long-term solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with other Technical Account Managers supporting billing accounts as a subject matter expert on the billing industry to deliver differentiated technical support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage in frequent on-site visits with billing users to deepen relationships, surface technical challenges early, and deliver strategic guidance to their engineering, product, and business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive publication of user case studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in enterprise-level client-facing work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise supporting billing companies, usage-based, and hybrid monetization models; invoicing; revenue recovery; tax; revenue recognition; and the technical and operational challenges of scaling billing infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and energized by the challenge of solving difficult user-related problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead complex integration conversations in a highly consultative and proactive manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APIs and ability to explaining API concepts to Stripe&#39;s largest and most technical customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in SQL and comfort building complex queries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity using AI coding agents to solve problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical troubleshooting skills and experience interfacing with technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept client relationship management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operations-savvy mindset, with an ability to identify and eliminate process friction while continuing to build scalable processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience practicing in small to medium scale project management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and self-starting mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideal experience with tools like Postman, xCode, Python, Webhooks, ETL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideal experience in the payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1jwrhb8:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe and Bridge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Bridge, acquired by Stripe in 2025, is an entirely new payments platform, built with stablecoins, to simplify global money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a driven, strategic, and results-oriented PMM to join the product marketing team at Bridge, focused on our Open Issuance, Orchestration and FX product lines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an early PMM for Bridge, you’ll be responsible for product marketing across the lifecycle, from helping shape the product with market insights, to crafting messaging, to growing product awareness and adoption in partnership with Sales, Marketing, Product, and more. This is a highly-cross functional role that will work both across the teams at Bridge and at Stripe to help grow the Bridge business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be embedded with the Bridge team while also being part of the Stripe product marketing team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a storyteller. &lt;/strong&gt;You have deep empathy for our core audience and are able to adapt how you communicate to best reach and engage your audience. You can translate complex infrastructure concepts—stablecoin issuance, cross-border FX, payment orchestration—into clear, compelling narratives that differentiate Bridge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead with data. &lt;/strong&gt;You like working with data and insights and pair that with your passion for users to generate balanced and thoughtful points of view for how to take products to market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep things organized&lt;/strong&gt;. You are able to manage highly interdependent, complex projects and keep various work streams on track. You&#39;re comfortable running multiple launches in parallel across different product lines and coordinating across Bridge, Privy, and Stripe teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have a passion for fintech and crypto. &lt;/strong&gt;You are keen to learn about how things work and are able to explain technical concepts in ways that everyday people can understand. You’re deeply curious about fintech and crypto and translate that passion into impactful product marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be ambitious and thrive in complexity. &lt;/strong&gt;You are eager to make an impact at Bridge (and consequently, Stripe). You thrive in a fast-moving, dynamic, hyper-growth environment and are able to operate fluidly between the 30,000-foot strategy level and the micro-detail to get things right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act as a team player. &lt;/strong&gt;Product Marketers collaborate with basically every team in the business. You are able to work with a range of disciplines to execute on your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end product marketing strategy for Open Issuance, Orchestration and FX, including messaging, positioning, ICP definition, sales enablement, and demand generation campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive go-to-market for product expansions (new currencies, corridors, pricing improvements), ensuring GTM teams have the right positioning, playbooks, and enablement content from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain competitive positioning in a crowded market, clearly articulating Bridge&#39;s differentiation to the right developer and customer segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead marketing for product releases and launches across your product areas, coordinating with product, comms, content, and demand gen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain sales and marketing assets (case studies, solution pages, pitch decks, one-pagers, enablement and trainings) that drive pipeline conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a liaison between Bridge and Stripe product marketing to bring connectivity across the marketing strategy for both parts of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flex into other Bridge marketing needs as they arise, supporting the broader team during peak moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience including B2B product marketing, marketing, product management, and management consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be agile and thrive in a fast-paced and dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working in businesses that offer API-based products, fintech and crypto experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Action-oriented and comfortable moving forward without clear guidelines or instructions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent writing and communication skills with the ability to simplify complex topics for diverse audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and a data-driven mindset for decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional relationship builder at all levels of an organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1fb0445:
&lt;h3&gt;About the position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Graphic Designer to join our Creative Engagement team and bring visual life to the financial, technological and mathematical work happening at Jane Street. In this role, you&#39;ll help shape and care for how the firm looks across our many departments, programmes, spaces and events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work is deeply intellectual, so we&#39;re hoping to find someone who loves taking abstract ideas and turning them into clear, engaging designs that celebrate the thoughtful things our colleagues are doing across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The variety of work is what our designers love most: you might find yourself creating print and digital assets for recruiting materials, giving a conference booth its visual identity, bringing our puzzles and games to life, developing swag and branded packaging, shaping logos and brand systems and much more. We work collaboratively, so you&#39;ll get to be a design generalist and pitch in wherever the team needs you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No previous finance experience is needed—just genuine curiosity and an enthusiasm for interesting design challenges. We do ask for a portfolio when you apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 6+ years of design experience across a range of project types and scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent taste, with strong typography, layout and colour fundamentals and meticulous attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable running several projects at once at different stages, taking some from brief to final files, picking up others midway&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand production: prepress, spec&#39;ing for fabrication and handoff to web dev&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign and PowerPoint, and comfortable in Google Suite, especially Slides and Docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Happy to present your work to stakeholders, and you treat feedback and iteration as part of the fun of solving a design puzzle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give clear, useful feedback on other designers&#39; work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious about what you&#39;re designing for—you&#39;ll happily ask a colleague to explain the maths or the trading concept behind a project&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you&#39;re a recruiting agency and want to partner with us, please reach out to agency-partnerships@janestreet.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

job-1gcuc0k:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We simplify wealth creation. Founded in 2014 in Vienna, Austria by Eric Demuth, Paul Klanschek and Christian Trummer, we’re here to help people trust themselves enough to build their financial freedom — for now and the future. Our user-friendly, trade-everything platform empowers both first-time investors and seasoned experts to invest in the cryptocurrencies, crypto indices, stocks*, precious metals and commodities* they want — with any sized budget, 24/7. Our global team works across different cultures and time zones, bringing our products to more than 7 million customers, making us one of Europe’s safest and most secure platforms that powers modern investing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Austria but operating across Europe, our products are built by fast-moving, talented, “roll-up-your-sleeves-and-make-it-happen” kind of people. It’s these diverse perspectives and innovative minds operating as ONE TEAM that keep Bitpanda at the cutting edge of our industry. So if you’re someone who thinks big, moves fast and wants to make an impact right from day one, then get ready to join our industry-changing team. Let’s go!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Growth, Engagement &amp;amp; Retention Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you own Bitpanda’s rewards flywheel. You turn activity across our product offerings into a single measure of loyalty value, and that value into the reason a customer stays, pays, and brings others with them.&amp;nbsp;Your north star is a power user: someone deeply engaged. Revenue diversification and customer lifetime value are your measures of progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the baseline: define the core customer health metrics such as cohort retention, product attach, CLV by segment, churn drivers, and engagement depth to diagnose value leakage, size growth opportunities, and guide investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the rewards flywheel and engagement strategy: design the earning and redemption logic that connects Trading, Earn, Card, and future products through a shared loyalty currency, and map the core engagement loops across the customer lifecycle; from activation to habit, reward to reinvestment, referral, community, and status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decide, based on evidence, which rewards, nudges, and growth mechanics maximize net value, evaluating reward cost, breakage, cannibalization, and cost-to-serve. Product teams own their products; you own the cross-product incentive layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore a subscription or membership model as one possible accelerator. If the evidence supports it, define pricing, tiering, and benefits for a recurring revenue layer with clear attach, retention, and margin targets; one of several mechanisms available to you, not a predetermined solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate community belonging and customer value by designing compliant, learning-focused status mechanics alongside strategic external benefits partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth, retention, and monetisation expert: &lt;/strong&gt;5+ years of Product Management in a high-growth B2C consumer platform — ideally crypto, fintech, neobank, marketplace, or loyalty/rewards. You&#39;ve shipped or scaled a subscription, loyalty, or rewards product, and you connect what makes customers loyal directly to recurring revenue and retention, understanding tiering, points economics, and the traps: breakage, cannibalization, reward fatigue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems thinker: &lt;/strong&gt;You can own a shared rewards ledger spanning multiple verticals without owning the verticals themselves, building connective tissue between verticals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-stack product thinker: &lt;/strong&gt;Comfortable across commercial/pricing design, UX, and the entitlements, ledgers, and attribution plumbing that make tiers and rewards work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-driven and experimentation-led: &lt;/strong&gt;You make decisions through evidence, not intuition. You define success metrics, build customer and business baselines, size opportunities, and use cohort analysis, segmentation, and rigorous A/B testing to identify value creation and leakage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear and compelling communicator: &lt;/strong&gt;You articulate commercial trade-offs to Finance as confidently as product vision to engineers, and write PRDs that leave no room for ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Flexibility to work where you thrive&lt;/strong&gt; – Enjoy the freedom of our Hybrid working model, combining onsite collaboration and remote work, with an additional 25 days per year to work from a city or country of your choice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Reward for your impact&lt;/strong&gt; – Receive a competitive total compensation package aligned with Bitpanda’s pay-for-impact policy, including participation in our stock option plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Support for your mental wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt; – Access confidential coaching, counselling, and mental health resources whenever you need them through OpenUP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time to recharge&lt;/strong&gt; – On top of your standard annual leave, prioritise your wellbeing in 2027 with 3 additional days of paid time off to rest, reset, and recharge, available once you’ve been with us for 6 months.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Continuous learning and growth&lt;/strong&gt; – Grow your skills and stay ahead in your career with unlimited access to Udemy’s library of online courses at your own pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Exclusive perks and rewards&lt;/strong&gt; – Enjoy discounts, rewards, and perks from partners worldwide across lifestyle, wellness, tech, and travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Support during life milestones&lt;/strong&gt; – Take advantage of up to 8 additional weeks of gender-neutral new parent leave to welcome and bond with your new addition to the family.&lt;/li&gt;
