&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width=&quot;582&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Mechanical Systems Expert is Managed Services&#39; expert embedded in a data center build - supporting design review and commissioning to ensure cooling systems are operable and maintainable at turnover. Every design decision eventually becomes someone&#39;s 3 a.m. problem; this role reviews the design and witnesses the testing on behalf of that person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Some of the key responsibilities you should expect are the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operability Design Review&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review mechanical and cooling designs - chilled water plants, air and liquid cooling systems, CDUs, CRAHs, heat rejection, water treatment - through an operations lens: maintenance access and laydown, isolation and redundancy behavior, degraded-mode operation, instrumentation adequacy, and failure-mode consequences. File review comments that change designs, not just document concerns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Construction-Phase Verification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Walk mechanical installations at key milestones: pipe routing and support, valve access, equipment clearances, insulation quality, and cleanliness/flushing protocol compliance - catching operability problems while they&#39;re still cheap to fix.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commissioning Witness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Witness Level 3-5 commissioning of mechanical systems: functional performance tests, staging and failover sequences, failure scenarios, and integrated systems testing. Drive operational issues into the Cx log with clear acceptance criteria and verify closure personally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turnover Readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verify mechanical turnover packages: O&amp;amp;Ms, as-builts, valve tags and system labeling, water treatment baselines, spare parts and consumables lists, and PM program inputs (frequencies, procedures, vendor contacts). Validate training actually equips operators to run the plant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations Transition Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support early operations stabilization post-turnover: alarm tuning input, setpoint refinement, and first-months troubleshooting alongside the operations team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Feedback&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Feed operational lessons into Hut 8 mechanical design standards and the next project&#39;s basis of design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
