&lt;p&gt;The Electrical SME is Managed Services&#39; electrical expert embedded in a data center build - supporting design review and commissioning witness to ensure electrical systems are operable and maintainable at turnover. The electrical system is the facility&#39;s spine; this role makes sure it can be operated, switched, and maintained safely by the team inheriting it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some of the key responsibilities you should expect are the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operability Design Review&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review electrical designs - MV/LV distribution, generator plants, UPS systems, EPMS - for operability: maintenance access and working clearances, switching practicality and arc-flash exposure during real operating procedures, redundancy behavior under maintenance conditions, and labeling/mimic clarity. Push back where the design assumes maintenance that can&#39;t safely be performed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Construction - Phase Verification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Walk electrical installations at key milestones: equipment setting and clearances, terminations and torque documentation, grounding, and cable management quality - flagging operability and quality issues to the MEP superintendent early.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing &amp;amp; Commissioning Witness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Witness NETA acceptance testing and Level 3-5 commissioning: protective device testing, generator and UPS transfer sequences, load bank testing, pull-the-plug scenarios, and integrated systems testing. Drive operational findings into the Cx log and verify closure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turnover Readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verify electrical turnover packages: test records and settings files, one-lines and as-builts, arc-flash labels matching final studies, spare breakers and critical spares, PM program inputs, and switching procedures. Confirm operator training covers real switching and emergency scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Energization &amp;amp; Early Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support energization sequences and early operations stabilization: alarm and EPMS tuning input, operating procedure refinement, and first-months troubleshooting with the operations team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Feedback&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Feed operational lessons into Hut 8 electrical standards and future basis-of-design decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
