job-12w2bwb:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Partner Solutions Architecture (PSA) team, you will be responsible for providing technical guidance to Stripe&#39;s partners. Our goal is to drive growth through co-solutioning, education, and enablement with our partner ecosystem. You&#39;ll serve as a critical technical liaison to Stripe&#39;s Partner Development Managers, creating comprehensive technical business plans that identify, incubate, and bring to market service and solution offerings built on or with Stripe. A Partner Solutions Architect at Stripe is intellectually curious, entrepreneurial, and energized by building deep technical trust with partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a PSA, the expectation in-role is to build highly consultative trusted relationships with executives and technical decision makers at Stripe, Salesforce, Adobe and the ecosystem of commerce enterprise partners between both to provide strategic and technical thought leadership, and become a trusted advisor in solving mission-critical business challenges for Salesforce, partners and users. Particularly within the enterprise space. We architect business models with them so they can drive new monetization opportunities and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with priority Salesforce, Adobe partners, including GSIs, to build out their Stripe capabilities and solutions to grow their business and drive non-linear growth in Stripes business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute enablement plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be at the forefront of technical discussions &amp;amp; solution deep-dives with partners on the value Stripe can provide to their clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with CTO’s, engineering &amp;amp; other technical leads at key partners to share technology roadmaps, demonstrate the latest innovations, and define a solution strategy to expand the partnership revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate success internally through QBRs, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide oversight, guidance, and assistance during the partners sales process to ensure mutual success in joint opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate the Stripe GTM selling teams, notably our Solutions Architecture teams, on key Salesforce solutions and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for key partners within specific sales regions and identify areas for sales partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on technical content (sample code, demos, etc.) to show partners how to implement specific use cases or best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Partner-focused guidance on Stripe’s product through feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in a similar customer-facing engineering role such as solution consultant, solutions architect, sales engineer, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of deep experience in Commerce space, Order-to-cash processes and ecosystem (like Salesforce, Adobe commerce offerings)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective group-facilitation skills and confidence in proposing and leading customer meetings to gain strategic footing and pursue opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of the software development lifecycle and API architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding spoken and written communication skills, presentation skills, and confidence in explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn Stripe solutions such as Payments, Billing, Connect, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand how a wide variety of applications such as ERP, CRM, Billing, Tax and legacy systems interact with each other in an enterprise technology ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time management skills and the ability to juggle competing priorities while working with multiple strategic opportunities and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within the Salesforce technology stack &amp;amp; ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a customer facing, domain expert in a software company; presenting, and architecting solutions for enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with integrating Stripe or other RESTful APIs into web applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in systems design, building and deploying complex applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in driving global enterprise technical sales for top-tier enterprise application companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in helping customers adopt and consume software in a cloud model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about learning and actively seeks out knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and confidently to develop a path forward with customers under ambiguous circumstances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic and creative thinker who can proactively identify challenges and maintain a positive approach when facing difficult obstacles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

job-0p86xzz:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Solutions Engineer for Turkey / EMEA&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be the go-to product and technical expert for Alpaca&#39;s enterprise partners across and the wider Turkey / EMEA region. You will bridge technical and business conversations: a customer-facing engineer with strong API knowledge, experience supporting enterprise customers, fluency in Turkish for customer interactions, and sufficient English proficiency to collaborate effectively with our global team. You will support enterprise partners and expand our base of enterprise partners in Turkey / EMEA, acting as the technical bridge between local partners, vendors, and regulators and Alpaca&#39;s global engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support and relationship management for existing enterprise customers in Turkey / EMEA , acting as a trusted technical advisor throughout the partner lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Sales and Solutions teams on pre-sales technical discussions, solution design, and API consultations, and present compelling product and technical use cases to prospective clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide new enterprise customers through API integration, implementation, and onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of Turkish customers by collaborating with Product and Engineering teams to improve localized experiences; translate complex business and technical requirements (often originating in Turkish) into clear specifications for Alpaca&#39;s global engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the product and technical subject matter expert, capable of thoroughly understanding and articulating all aspects of the Alpaca platform to diverse audiences and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with local compliance and operations teams to understand local and regional product requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical Solutions engagement end-to-end: discovery calls, solution validation, RFPs, and security questionnaires that win deals; lead demo strategy and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create Solutions support materials and documentation for new features and products, including Turkish-language collateral where needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate in Turkish with local regulators, vendors, and partners, and relay those requirements to global product and engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers successfully adopt Alpaca&#39;s platform while maintaining a high standard of technical and customer support; travel within Turkey / EMEA as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay updated on internal product development timelines and work closely with the product team to test and roll out new features to partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for (Must-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise / B2B customers in a technical, sales engineering, or solutions engineering role (typically 3+ years), ideally at API or SaaS-first companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of REST APIs, SDKs, and software integration workflows; hands-on experience with APIs, WebSockets, Postman, Grafana, and JSON.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Native or business-level Turkish&lt;/strong&gt;, with excellent customer communication skills and a solid understanding of Turkish business culture - essential for partner, vendor, and regulator communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business-level English&lt;/strong&gt; for collaborating with global, cross-functional teams; able to drive clarity on goals, set expectations, and collect feedback effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to translate complex technical concepts into simple, understandable terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter who thrives in a startup environment, manages multiple assignments simultaneously, works independently, and drives projects to completion with close attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Might Be (Nice-To-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, capital markets, brokerage, or financial APIs; experience at a Broker-Dealer or securities firm in Turkey / EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of brokerage, post-trade, and settlement operations, as well as regulatory context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Closing enterprise deals alongside Account Executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US securities qualifications (e.g., SIE and/or Series 7).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Metabase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with the FIX protocol.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with OpenAPI, ReadMe, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited to learn more about the securities industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

