job-03opeod:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Corporate Security helps keep Stripe secure and Stripes safe by building practical, risk-based programs that enable the company to operate and grow. We are looking for an experienced Regional Security Manager to join our team. As the Regional Security Manager Americas at Stripe, you will be responsible for developing our core physical-security deliverables to office locations in the Americas (North America and parts of Latin America), and help evolve our program to support Stripe around the globe. You will work cross functionally within the Corporate Security team, and alongside other business teams at the company to keep Stripe secure and Stripes safe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Regional Security Manager Americas, reporting to the Head of Global Security Operations, you will lead and continuously improve physical security operations across North America and relevant parts of Latin America. This is an individual-contributor role: you will manage regional contractors and vendor relationships, but will not directly manage employees at this time. You will translate regional risk into scalable programs, build trusted partnerships with internal teams and service providers, and help evolve Stripe’s global security operating model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role. The successful candidate will spend 50% of their time in one of our AMER office locations in San Francisco, New York, Seattle, or Chicago. We are not entertaining remote candidates at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional physical-security operations for the Americas, including security governance, escalations, incident response, service delivery, and performance reporting; contribute to global programs as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with teams such as Workplace, People, IT, Events, business leaders, and external providers to deliver a security program that scales with business needs while preserving a high-quality employee and visitor experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or coordinate risk, threat, vulnerability, and site-security assessments; document material risks; prioritize mitigations; and track delivery to closure. Conduct annual site-security assessments and risk reviews for company sites and relevant vendor sites to evaluate and improve controls in line with regional risk and established standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and test clear policies, standard operating procedures, and playbooks covering office security, escalation, incident documentation, event support, and crisis response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage regional security contractors, service providers, and guard-force partners through defined scopes, service-level expectations, key performance indicators, quarterly business reviews, and corrective-action plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Business Continuity, Crisis Management, and Environmental Health &amp;amp; Safety to ensure regional emergency and crisis-response plans are current, practicable, and exercised regularly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Security Systems team as a regional decision maker to define and support physical-security technology design for new offices, relocations, expansions, and significant workplace changes. Ensure appropriate CCTV, alarm, and access-control capabilities are in place, functional, and aligned to regional risk and escalation needs across the region’s offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional operational planning and budgeting: forecast spend, identify cost and service improvements, and manage approved programs responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver security-awareness and education initiatives that help employees make safer decisions and strengthen Stripe’s security culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional security projects that reduce risk, improve resilience, and produce measurable operational outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an experienced physical-security leader who pairs sound judgment with a practical, service-oriented approach. You can move comfortably between strategic program design and hands-on operational problem solving. You communicate clearly with executives, frontline partners, and vendors; make progress amid ambiguity; and build durable relationships across diverse geographic and business contexts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of progressively responsible physical-security, corporate-security, or closely related risk-management experience supporting a multinational organization, including responsibility for operations in the Americas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing, operating, and measuring risk-based physical-security programs across multiple sites or jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting risk, threat, vulnerability, or site-security assessments and translating findings into prioritized, practical mitigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing security vendors or guard-force/service-provider relationships through scopes of work, performance measures, service reviews, and issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or materially contributing to incident, emergency, or crisis-response planning and exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program and project-management skills, with the ability to prioritize multiple concurrent initiatives and communicate tradeoffs, risks, and progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment, discretion, and a demonstrated commitment to employee safety, privacy, and an inclusive workplace experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel within the Americas and internationally up to 25%, including occasionally on short notice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a technology, financial-services, or other fast-growing, globally distributed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting office construction, relocations, expansions, or physical-security system design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with access-control, video-surveillance, alarm, or other enterprise physical-security technologies and the governance that accompanies them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing security operations at large scale public events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant degree, CPP/PSP, or comparable professional certification; equivalent practical experience is also valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established professional relationships across the security industry, public-sector partners, or relevant regional networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in Spanish&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1h0wm4b:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a SMB Hunter Sales Manager at Stripe, you will play an instrumental role in fueling Stripe’s growth through new customer acquisition. In this role, you will build and lead a team of high-performing Account Executives, helping them to develop their skills and deliver on their ambitious targets, as well as roll your sleeves up to work directly with customers. We are looking for a proactive leader who has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity, operating in a high-growth environment, managing high-performing teams and solving complicated problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have management and leadership experience scaling a technology sales team and possess first-class analytical, communication and relationship-building skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop and lead a team of Account Executives who focus on small and medium, high-growth, tech-forward businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior leadership to develop the long-term vision and strategy for the team, and manage day-to-day operations with a focus on performance against key sales and growth metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for increasing revenue and new client acquisition at high rates of growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and guide the team in developing consultative and solution-based sales skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate and enable development of team members to promote career growth and impact for Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively and cross-functionally across the organization to help shape Stripe’s products and solutions to meet customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a personal and direct role in building and maintaining enduring customer relationships, up to C-level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement programs to improve pipeline generation efforts and improve overall efficiency for the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant experience, with 2+ years of people management experience preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading sales in an early stage, high-growth technology environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hire, train and coach a high-performance sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build relationships with strategic client and industry thought leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated passion for start-ups and new technology businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand and articulate technical concepts, and translate them into industry- or business-relevant terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage internet/software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience forecasting and managing a high growth commercial business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience running complex sales cycles, ideally with both commercial and enterprise size companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience leading a team in an office outside of the company headquarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in the payments industry and/or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1lxz9n5:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join the Customer Advocacy and Programs team, a small, high-impact team inside Customer Success that amplifies the voice of the customer and turns feedback into measurable change. We synthesize customer input and frontline insights to surface the highest-value opportunities, then partner with Product, GTM, Support, Operations, and technical teams to turn those opportunities into durable tools, programs, and improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to help Stripe’s user-facing teams deliver more strategic, effective, and scalable experiences for users. We build the capabilities that help Customer Success Managers and the broader field better understand users, identify opportunities, and deliver value, while extending Customer Success impact beyond named coverage. We are establishing a more unified approach to Customer Success tooling and efficiency, with product discipline from problem discovery through adoption and measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Program Manager, Customer Success Efficiency and Scale, you will act as the product leader for a portfolio of internal tools, AI-enabled workflows, assets, and scaled programs that enable Customer Success and other user-facing teams. You’ll turn frontline pain points and user needs into a prioritized roadmap, define clear requirements and success measures, and partner with technical, data, and operational teams to deliver solutions that are adopted and create measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Although this role is titled Program Manager, it requires a strong product-management mindset and experience: deep user discovery, strategic prioritization, crisp product requirements, cross-functional delivery, and continuous iteration based on adoption and outcomes. You’ll operate in a highly ambiguous environment, create clarity across a broad stakeholder set, and balance near-term improvements with a longer-term vision for scaling Customer Success capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the roadmap:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Set and prioritize the Customer Success Efficiency and Scale roadmap, balancing user needs, business impact, feasibility, and organizational priorities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discover and define problems: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with Customer Success Managers, Sales, and other user-facing teams to identify pain points, validate opportunities, and determine where tooling, automation, AI, or self-service can create leverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape solutions: &lt;/strong&gt;Translate validated needs into clear product briefs, requirements, success metrics, and launch plans. Partner with technical teams to deliver scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive delivery and adoption:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate cross-functional execution, manage dependencies and trade-offs, and ensure each launch has a clear enablement, measurement, and iteration plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale Customer Success (CS) impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Build tools, assets, and programmatic motions that help Sales and other teams deliver CS-caliber value where dedicated CSM coverage is not available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in product management, program management with substantial product ownership, business operations, consulting, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading products, platforms, workflows, or customer-facing solutions from discovery and prioritization through launch, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and user empathy, with the ability to turn ambiguous qualitative and quantitative inputs into clear strategy and requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading complex, cross-functional work across technical, operational, and go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and structured problem-solving skills, including the ability to evaluate trade-offs and design scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and influence skills, with the ability to create clarity and drive alignment across frontline teams and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of comfort with AI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal tools, automation, AI-enabled workflows, or self-service experiences for customer-facing or go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with engineering, data, analytics, or AI teams to scope and deliver technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing multi-quarter roadmaps that balance quick wins with longer-term foundational investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1xb64vx:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world&#39;s biggest financial problems. We&#39;re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it&#39;s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We&#39;re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Crypto Data Science team is on a mission to accelerate Robinhood&#39;s position as the leading platform for crypto investors. We partner with product, engineering, finance, and research to shape the strategies behind our fastest-growing business. From launching new products to expanding internationally, our team turns complex data into clear decisions — and our work directly influences how millions of customers experience crypto at Robinhood.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Data Science Manager for the Crypto team, you will lead a high-impact team delivering insights, models, and strategies that shape Robinhood&#39;s crypto product roadmap and growth. This role partners with product, engineering, and executive leadership to ensure data is at the core of our strategic decisions. Learn more about what the crypto team is up to &lt;a href=&quot;https://robinhood.com/web3-wallet/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA office, with in-person attendance expected at least 5 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and scale a team of data scientists and analytics engineers working across product and ML domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Crypto product, engineering, finance, and research teams to drive key initiatives such as international expansion, pro trader growth, and Wallet app adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver robust, data-driven recommendations and analyses to shape product direction, with a focus on stock tokens, perpetuals, and blockchain opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of excellence in analytics, experimentation, and impact within your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Crypto Data Science in cross-functional leadership forums and contribute to overall Crypto org strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in data science, including at least 2+ years of people management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with Python and SQL in a production or analytics environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in product data science roles, with a track record of delivering strategic insights and scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the crypto ecosystem, with 3–4 years of direct experience highly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence, influence across teams, and outstanding communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership expectations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ambitious roadmap requires a great culture shaped by exceptional leaders. Here’s what we expect from them:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high performance by setting clear, focused goals, giving real-time feedback, stretching top talent, and scaling impact through focus, innovation, and tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and retain top talent by setting a high bar, hiring only those who raise it, investing in onboarding, and addressing talent issues quickly and fairly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create community by connecting work to purpose, removing friction while prioritizing safety, building trust and inclusion, and leading from the front with integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, bonus programs, equity ownership, and 401(k) matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top Tier benefits to fuel your work, including 100% paid health insurance for employees with 90% coverage for dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the best AI tools on the market and continuous AI skill-building for every employee, technical or not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet — a highly flexible benefits spending account for wellness, learning, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, fertility benefits, and mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$247,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$290,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$217,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$255,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$193,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$226,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-1fpmlh4:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Apps connect Stripe with the tools businesses already use, bringing relevant data and workflows into the Stripe Dashboard and third-party systems. The Strategic Apps team owns a portfolio of integrations with enterprise systems that are critical to our users’ workflows—from quote-to-cash and support to reporting. We help users embed Stripe more deeply into the way they run their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Staff Product Manager to set the strategy and lead execution for Strategic Apps. You will own a portfolio of existing and new integrations, including those with systems such as Salesforce, and determine where Stripe should invest based on user needs, Stripe’s product and industry priorities, and market signals. You will work across Stripe and directly with external partners to deliver reliable, high-quality integrations that drive adoption and business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision, product strategy, roadmap, and success metrics for a portfolio of strategic apps, making and communicating clear trade-offs amid significant ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, prioritize, and validate the highest-value user problems and integration opportunities through direct user research, ecosystem analysis, and quantitative evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams across Engineering, Design, Data Science, Finance, Sales, User Support, Marketing, Partner Management, and other product teams to deliver and evolve integrations end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering to define product requirements, technical approach, and quality standards for integrations, including APIs, documentation, edge cases, reliability, security, compliance, and ongoing maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish feedback loops and measurement plans before launch; use product, business, and user metrics to assess efficacy, diagnose changes in performance, and continuously improve adoption, retention, and revenue outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe’s product strategy with strategic technology partners and enterprise users, building productive relationships with product and technical counterparts and incorporating their feedback into roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive launches, beta programs, user acceptance testing, and go-to-market readiness in partnership with Marketing, Sales, Partner Management, and Support; ensure teams have the materials and operating model needed to support adoption at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make and drive important cross-functional decisions, align senior stakeholders around a shared strategy, and communicate progress, risks, and outcomes clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance new feature development with investment in quality, reliability, technical debt, and foundational platform capabilities across the app portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve how Stripe builds and operates strategic integrations by turning user, partner, and performance signals into scalable product and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant product-management, engineering, or equivalent experience, including ownership of a high-quality product or feature area at scale or a major evolution of an existing product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting product strategy and driving execution across multiple cross-functional teams or a complex product area, from ambiguous problem definition through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to use qualitative and quantitative evidence to define success metrics, evaluate product performance, and make prioritization decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment and fluency working with engineers on API-based products, integrations, technical constraints, and product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging directly with enterprise users and external technology partners, and translating their needs into clear product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a track record of influencing senior stakeholders and leading through organizational boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise business systems and workflows, such as CRM, ERP, quote-to-cash, support, or reporting platforms; familiarity with Salesforce, Oracle, SAP, or Microsoft Dynamics is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling platform, ecosystem, marketplace, or partner-integrated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing product adoption, usage, or revenue through product-led and go-to-market initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or other regulated technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in computer science, engineering, or another technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-0pr3nfz:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
