job-024vy5u:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Business Development Desk is a proactive outbound sales team responsible for general asset gathering and migrating customers into our Concierge program through consolidation of assets. This team serves as brand ambassadors, education and creating awareness of all the available products and solutions available that would help the customer reach their financial goals. The team works closely with all of our customer facing teams to ensure a truly white glove/Concierge experience through the onboarding process. In this role, you will lead a team responsible for growing assets and expanding customer relationships here at Robinhood..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Manager of Business Development, you will lead, coach, and develop a team of Onboarding Specialists who support customers throughout their onboarding journey while also exploring any additional opportunities to consolidate/win more share of wallet. You will oversee and enhance sales pipelines, review opportunities worked for Compliance and Oversight and coaching to overall sales process and customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for driving team strategy, establishing operating efficiency, and driving asset growth through pipeline management and ongoing coaching and development of sales agents. In addition to developing your team, you will partner closely with product, compliance, legal, and external service providers to evolve the Business Development Desk offering, expand pipelines of opportunities and ensure all customer interactions meet all regulatory standards including RegBI and telemarketing compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly cross-functional leadership role where you will work closely with our customer facing teams and business partners to drive/increase referrals to the desk and identify operational and account signals to automate additional opportunities to win new business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our Denver, CO or Westlake, TX office(s), with in-person attendance expected 5 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams. Local travel may be required to meet with customers and participate in in-person events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of Onboarding Specialists, driving high performance, new new assets and professional growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all team goals are being met/exceeded, including gross deposits (COV), agent productivity (opportunities worked) and limiting/addressing all Compliance infractions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee customer interactions from a team of Onboarding Specialists ensuring compliance with all RegBI, telemarketing rules and internal policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a culture of high performance while reinforcing policies, supervisory procedures, and regulatory standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with our customer facing partners, product, compliance, legal, and external service providers to improve workflows, expand capabilities, and enhance the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and improve team performance through data, coaching, and process optimization, identifying opportunities to scale impact efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure high-quality documentation and adherence to firm and regulatory standards across all customer interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support escalation management and complex customer situations, providing guidance and oversight where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive initiatives to increase customer engagement, including asset consolidation, product adoption, and deeper relationship development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a strong customer-first mindset, fostering a culture of empathy, clarity, and trust in all client interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clean U5&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current SIE, Series 7 and 66&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Series 24 or 9/10&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience in sales coaching/leadership, or related financial services roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to guide agents through the sales process and develop their skills in uncovering assets through consultative engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with sales coaching and supervision/oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to support asset consolidation, deepen client relationships, and increase engagement with financial products in a compliant, customer-first manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to acting in the customer’s best interest while adhering to all regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive in a dynamic and evolving environment, with a constant drive to increase and enhance the value of our offering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness and aptitude to leverage AI tools to enhance productivity and drive innovation within your role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In addition to the base pay range listed below, this role is also eligible for bonus opportunities + equity + benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected base pay range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$123,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$145,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 (Denver, CO; Westlake, TX; Chicago, IL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$109,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$128,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 (Lake Mary, FL; Clearwater, FL; Gainesville, FL)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$96,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$113,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-0r51nwu:
&lt;h1 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Infrastructure organization builds and operates the shared platforms that make it possible for engineering teams to build, deploy, run, and scale reliable products. The organization owns foundational capabilities across service networking and discovery, safe feature and configuration changes, data storage and orchestration, and batch computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our platforms support a global engineering audience and power systems at significant scale. This includes the control plane for secure service-to-service communication across tens of thousands of microservices, service and feature deployment infrastructure that helps teams introduce and recover from changes safely, infrastructure for running Stripe&#39;s containerized services, and data platforms for storage, pipeline orchestration, and large-scale processing. Our batch compute platforms support technologies including Apache Airflow, Apache Spark, Apache Iceberg, Apache Hadoop, and Apache Celeborn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager, you will lead or strongly influence teams working on business-critical infrastructure with broad internal adoption. You will balance reliability, scalability, security, developer experience, and operational rigor while helping Stripe move quickly with confidence. You will partner closely with product, security, data, support, and adjacent infrastructure leaders to set direction, resolve cross-team dependencies, and turn recurring needs into durable platform capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager at Stripe, you will operate with full autonomy across a complex, high-impact area of our infrastructure. Your scope extends beyond a single team. You lead or strongly influence multiple engineering teams, execute parallel high-priority workstreams, and develop senior engineering talent. You set direction, align stakeholders, make decisions that hold up over time, and deliver results without close direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with scope and autonomy by driving impact across multiple teams or a significant infrastructure area independently, translating organizational goals into concrete execution plans, and delivering results across parallel workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define strategy and roadmap for your area, anticipating internal user needs, technical challenges, reliability risks, and business priorities, then communicating a clear plan to your team and senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop senior talent by coaching senior engineers and emerging leaders, creating meaningful stretch opportunities, and giving candid feedback that improves individual and team performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional alignment with product, security, data, support, and adjacent engineering teams, resolving ambiguity at team boundaries and aligning stakeholders around shared priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and scale the team by attracting, developing, and retaining senior engineering talent while maintaining a high hiring bar and building an inclusive, high-performing organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with rigor by setting high standards for reliability, availability, scalability, incident response, and engineering craft, and by addressing systemic issues that affect internal users across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Staff engineers on architecture decisions involving distributed systems, service discovery, configuration propagation, production change management, data processing, and internal platform design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience with 10+ years of software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of engineering management experience with a demonstrated track record of autonomous impact as an engineering manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading high-complexity engineering teams that deliver multiple difficult, high-impact workstreams in parallel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence and align cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority, communicating a clear direction that others follow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful recruiting experience, including a track record of attracting and developing senior engineering talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth sufficient to guide architecture decisions and hold teams to a high standard for product quality, reliability, and engineering craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating high-availability distributed systems, internal platforms, or developer infrastructure used by a broad engineering audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with service networking, service discovery, service mesh, feature flags, configuration management, progressive delivery, deployment tooling, or production change governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data infrastructure, including large-scale storage, data orchestration, batch compute, or processing frameworks such as Apache Airflow, Apache Spark, Apache Iceberg, Apache Hadoop, or Apache Celeborn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving reliability through observability, health checks, incident response, automated recovery, capacity planning, or reducing the impact of production changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing secure access controls, audit systems, approval workflows, or governance mechanisms for production infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud infrastructure and distributed systems technologies such as Amazon Web Services, DynamoDB, Aurora, S3, Ruby, Go, Java, or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product mindset for internal platforms, including empathy for internal users, a focus on self-service, and a commitment to making safe workflows straightforward to adopt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;in-office-expectations&quot;&gt;In-office expectations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Office-assigned Stripes in most locations are expected to spend at least 50% of their time in a given month in their local office or with users. This expectation may vary by role, team, and location. The hiring manager will discuss the expectations for this role during the process.&lt;/p&gt;

job-182nu8e:
&lt;p&gt;Since we opened our doors in 2009, the world of commerce has evolved immensely, and so has Square. After enabling anyone to take payments and never miss a sale, we saw sellers stymied by disparate, outmoded products and tools that wouldn’t work together.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;So we expanded into software and started building integrated, omnichannel solutions – to help sellers sell online, manage inventory, offer buy now, pay later functionality, book appointments, engage loyal buyers, and hire and pay staff. Across it all, we’ve embedded financial services tools at the point of sale, so merchants can access a business loan and manage their cash flow in one place. Afterpay furthers our goal to provide omnichannel tools that unlock meaningful value and growth, enabling sellers to capture the next generation shopper, increase order sizes, and compete at a larger scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Today, we are a partner to sellers of all sizes – large, enterprise-scale businesses with complex operations, sellers just starting, as well as merchants who began selling with Square and have grown larger over time. As our sellers grow, so do our solutions. There is a massive opportunity in front of us. We’re building a significant, meaningful, and lasting business, and we are helping sellers worldwide do the same.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Reseller &amp;amp; Channel Partnerships Manager at Square, you will be responsible for developing, deploying, and managing partnerships that enrich our products and strengthen our go-to-market motions to acquire sellers. This includes working closely with cross-functional teams, like our Product, Marketing, Sales, Finance, and Legal teams, to develop and drive a high-impact partnerships strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a critical role on the Partnerships team. We are looking for an experienced partnerships operator with a track record of leading complex channel partnerships end-to-end, strong business, product acumen, the ability to work effectively cross-functionally internally and externally, strong communication and interpersonal skills, and a desire to drive significant growth of our business. This position reports to Square&#39;s Partnerships Retail Vertical Lead and will support a key vertical and GTM initiatives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and GTM teams to develop and execute a holistic partner strategy, from partner integrations that enhance Square’s products to channel partners that drive new seller acquisition&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute partnerships end-to-end, from business development to partner launch and management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable to KPI’s and business objectives each quarter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert on Square&#39;s products, the market landscape, and seller needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine and prioritize the appropriate mix of partner benefits, incentives, and co-marketing + sales opportunities necessary to secure a lucrative partnership deal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate autonomously, being both a proactive executor and strategic thinker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional initiatives with internal and external teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for your partners while balancing Square’s goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in the technology sector, including 3+ years in partnerships at a technology company. Experience with API integrations and/or channel partnerships is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to negotiate, sign, launch, and manage partnerships from tactical, mid-size opportunities to complex, strategic partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing and distributing new products with partners via compelling economic incentives and close collaboration with internal and external sales and marketing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly entrepreneurial, proactive, and comfortable working in a fast-paced, highly-matrixed environment with the ability to thrive under minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of working cross-functionally with various teams, managing initiatives at scale, and delivering results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and managing relationships with senior business leaders, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to think and communicate creatively, thoughtfully, and with diverse technical and non-technical groups, spanning all organizational levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Guidelines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates may submit up to 9 active applications within a 60-day period. Reapplications to the same role are accepted 90 days after a previous application has been reviewed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use of AI in Our Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We may use automated AI tools to evaluate job applications for efficiency and consistency. These tools comply with local regulations, including bias audits, and we handle all personal data in accordance with state and local privacy laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact us &lt;a href=&quot;https://privacy.block.xyz/privacyportal/form&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;with hiring practice or data usage questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Every benefit we offer is designed with one goal: empowering you to do the best work of your career while building the life you want. Remote work, medical insurance, flexible time off, retirement savings plans, and modern family planning are just some of our offering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://block.xyz/employee-benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://block.xyz/documents/benefits.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Check out our other benefits at Block.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Block, Inc. (NYSE: XYZ) builds technology to increase access to the global economy. Each of our brands unlocks different aspects of the economy for more people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Square&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;makes commerce and financial services accessible to sellers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Cash App&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is the easy way to spend, send, and store money.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Afterpay&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is transforming the way customers manage their spending over time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;TIDAL&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a music platform that empowers artists to thrive as entrepreneurs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Bitkey&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a simple self-custody wallet built for bitcoin.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Proto&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a suite of bitcoin mining products and services. Together, we’re helping build a financial system that is open to everyone.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://block.xyz/en/legal/applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-17s3pmo:
&lt;h3&gt;About the position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to give you a real sense of what it&#39;s like to work at Jane Street full time while providing a truly unparalleled educational experience. &amp;nbsp;We are looking for individuals of all majors who are interested in exploring what a career as a Trading Desk Operations Engineer (TDOE) might be like. Our TDOE internship is an immersive and fast-paced program that allows you to work on real-world projects directly tied to the challenges we face daily on the trading desk, all guided by a dedicated TDOE mentor.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have the opportunity to wear many hats and tackle diverse projects such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and optimizing infrastructure and operational processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting trading systems and workflows by executing data queries and coordinating with stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and implementing solutions for a range of trading and operations-related issues on the desk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through these experiences, you&#39;ll gain a comprehensive understanding of the trading product, including its life cycle, regulatory considerations, and operational workflows. Plus, you&#39;ll have a chance to build off your new professional growth with bootcamps and classes that are tailored to accelerate your technical and operational expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our collaborative trading desks are central to our office environment, and we believe the best way to integrate our interns is through a hands-on, interactive approach. Some of the tools developed by our interns have had a real impact on our trading desks. We can&#39;t wait to teach you what we know, and learn a few things from you as well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about Jane Street&#39;s internship programme &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.janestreet.com/join-jane-street/internships/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;ve never thought about a career in finance, you&#39;re in good company. Many of us were in the same position before working here. If you have a curious mind, a collaborative spirit, and a passion for solving interesting problems, we have a feeling you&#39;ll fit right in. We&#39;re more interested in how you think and learn than what you currently know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Planning to graduate in 2027 or 2028, all backgrounds are welcome!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A critical thinker with a strong quantitative foundation and an interest in growing your programming skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player with a &quot;no job too small&quot; attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interested in finance and passionate about STEM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to balance competing priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, organised, reliable, and courteous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An excellent verbal and written communicator; able to use technical knowledge and strong collaboration skills to reach solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectually humble; eager to ask questions and learn new things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note: Jane Street will provide flights to and from London as well as accommodation throughout the entirety of the programme.&lt;/p&gt;

job-0s6ltuo:
&lt;p&gt;Since we opened our doors in 2009, the world of commerce has evolved immensely, and so has Square. After enabling anyone to take payments and never miss a sale, we saw sellers stymied by disparate, outmoded products and tools that wouldn’t work together.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;So we expanded into software and started building integrated, omnichannel solutions – to help sellers sell online, manage inventory, offer buy now, pay later functionality, book appointments, engage loyal buyers, and hire and pay staff. Across it all, we’ve embedded financial services tools at the point of sale, so merchants can access a business loan and manage their cash flow in one place. Afterpay furthers our goal to provide omnichannel tools that unlock meaningful value and growth, enabling sellers to capture the next generation shopper, increase order sizes, and compete at a larger scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Today, we are a partner to sellers of all sizes – large, enterprise-scale businesses with complex operations, sellers just starting, as well as merchants who began selling with Square and have grown larger over time. As our sellers grow, so do our solutions. There is a massive opportunity in front of us. We’re building a significant, meaningful, and lasting business, and we are helping sellers worldwide do the same.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Square is seeking a Channel Sales Manager to build and lead a high-performing network of independent sales consultants (auto-entrepreneurs) across France. In this role, your primary responsibility is to enable and develop your team—recruiting, onboarding, training, coaching, and supporting a portfolio of 20–30 independent consultants to drive adoption of Square&#39;s payment and business solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Channel Sales Manager, you operate as a full-time employee of Square in a dedicated team-support capacity. You are not expected to carry a personal sales quota or close deals yourself—your success is measured entirely through the performance and growth of your consultant network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Building &amp;amp; Recruitment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recruit, and onboard independent sales consultants (auto-entrepreneurs) across your assigned region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and continuously scale a high-performing team of 20–30 independent consultants through rigorous, quality-driven recruitment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Square&#39;s internal recruiting resources to maintain a healthy pipeline of candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver structured onboarding programs to get new consultants productive quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coaching &amp;amp; Consultant Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular 1:1 coaching sessions, joint field visits, and structured feedback to maximize each consultant&#39;s performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify skill gaps and design targeted training plans to address them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of excellence, accountability, and continuous improvement within your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip consultants with the tools, resources, and product knowledge they need to succeed autonomously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Management &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze sales performance at both team and individual consultant levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear KPIs, monitor progress, and proactively address underperformance with structured support plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce reliable regional forecasts, pipeline updates, and performance summaries for leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data-driven insights to make strategic decisions and drive continuous improvement across your network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Cross-functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture insights from the field regarding local SME needs, market trends, and competitive dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share learnings with leadership and cross-functional teams to inform go-to-market strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Square professionally in the market and support brand awareness initiatives in your region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in sales channel management, indirect sales, or team leadership, ideally in the French market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to recruit, develop, and manage networks of independent contractors or self-employed salespeople&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong appetite for fintech, payment solutions, and point-of-sale (POS) systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performance-based sales models and a solid understanding of pipelines, metrics, and sales processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional coaching and leadership abilities, particularly with non-employee, commission-based contractors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Natural talent for recruiting and evaluating sales talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills to build trust and alignment with independent consultants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset—able to interpret performance data and act strategically&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter with entrepreneurial drive and the ability to work autonomously in a remote environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, payments, POS, or working with French SMEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience building sales teams from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with auto-entrepreneur regulations and contractor management in France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in French (native or business fluency)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional proficiency in English is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is based in France and will operate remotely within your assigned region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular travel across your region is required; occasional national travel may also be required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package including base salary and variable compensation (bonus-eligible)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive benefits in accordance with French employment standards&lt;/li&gt;
