&lt;p&gt;Engineering on this team is distinguished by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product taste.&lt;/strong&gt; We simplify complex financial workflows without hiding the details that matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-end ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; Engineers shape, build, launch, and improve the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Speed with confidence.&lt;/strong&gt; We scope sharply, move quickly, and hold a high quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security and correctness.&lt;/strong&gt; Access control, auditability, privacy, and failure behavior are design constraints from the start.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High agency and low ego.&lt;/strong&gt; We act without waiting, invite direct critique, and make the team better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Full-Stack Engineer focused on Compliance, you will design the foundations of Ondo&#39;s onboarding and compliance platform. You will own the systems that determine how users establish eligibility, move through KYC/KYB and compliance review, and how Operations and Compliance teams investigate and resolve cases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your scope spans the full workflow—from the user-facing onboarding experience to the internal tools, decision logic, data models, and third-party integrations behind it. You will set technical direction, define system boundaries and invariants, and evolve the platform as our products, policies, and scale change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a foundational ownership role for a senior engineer. You will turn ambiguous policy and operational requirements into precise product behavior and durable architecture. You will partner closely with Compliance, Legal, Risk, Operations, Product, and Design while owning the engineering judgment: what must be true, how the system can fail, and how it remains secure, explainable, and resilient in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an engineer who sees the whole system, anticipates what comes next, and raises the standard for critical product infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own compliance-focused product areas from problem definition and architecture through implementation, launch, production operation, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build clear, maintainable interfaces along with the APIs, data models, workflows, and integrations that make them work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn complex regulatory and operational requirements into intuitive, testable product behavior for customers and internal users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate third-party APIs and webhooks from identity, sanctions, blockchain analytics, fraud, and case-management providers while maintaining strong data quality, privacy, observability, and auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for real-world failure modes, including delayed and reordered vendor events, manual review, partial outages, retries, and conflicting state across systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with Compliance, Legal, Risk, Operations, Product, Design, and users to understand the domain and make sound product and technical tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI and machine learning where they can safely reduce manual work or improve decision support, with appropriate security, human review, explainability, and audit trails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the level of the team through clear design work, thoughtful code review, strong operational ownership, and effective use of modern AI engineering tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience building and operating production full-stack applications with React, Next.js, Node.js, and TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fundamentals in API and data-model design, relational databases, distributed systems, cloud infrastructure, testing, observability, and third-party integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building KYC/KYB, identity verification, onboarding, or similarly sensitive workflows, with a strong understanding of access controls, data protection, auditability, and secure system design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of owning complex product work end to end—not only implementing requirements handed to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product and technical judgment: you can translate ambiguous policy into precise system behavior, identify consequential edge cases, and make pragmatic tradeoffs without compromising critical controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High standards for security, correctness, reliability, usability, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to communicate clearly, learn unfamiliar domains quickly, and create alignment across technical, legal, compliance, and operational partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency and low ego. You move important work forward, invite strong critique, surface risk early, and care more about getting the system right than being right.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with financial-crime controls and frameworks such as BSA/AML, OFAC, FinCEN, KYC/CDD, SEC, or FATF.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building fintech, payments, trading, crypto, or other products where correctness, trust, and regulatory obligations are essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with systems that combine offchain identity and compliance data with onchain activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting audits, regulatory examinations, control testing, or compliance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying AI or machine learning to regulated operational workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We do not expect every strong candidate to know every framework or arrive with deep crypto experience. We do expect curiosity, sound engineering judgment, respect for the domain, and the ability to become effective in unfamiliar regulatory and technical terrain quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work building the trust and control layer for a new category of financial infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation including salary, future token rights, and/or equity, according to your preferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full medical, vision, and dental benefits, plus a flexible vacation policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A remote-first environment with meaningful autonomy and influence over product and technical direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional colleagues from Goldman Sachs, BlackRock, Two Sigma, Bridgewater, SpaceX, AWS, Meta, Google, McKinsey, Coinbase, Circle, and Uniswap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backing from leading crypto experts and investors, including Pantera Capital, Founders Fund, and Coinbase Ventures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;

