job-0croxhf:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation practice (within Professional Services) works with our most strategic users. The team serves as a transformation &amp;amp; growth partner to our most strategic and frontier users — helping them achieve complex business goals and enabling greater certainty in their outcomes when they invest with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will establish and lead a new sub-practice within Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation: &lt;strong&gt;Growth &amp;amp; Monetization Advisory&lt;/strong&gt;. As Stripe&#39;s users grow in scale and ambition — launching new revenue channels, embedding payments &amp;amp; finance into platforms, pricing AI-powered products, and expanding into new geographies — they need a trusted, opinionated advisor in their corner to advice them with prescriptive point of view on revenue acceleration, GTM, pricing &amp;amp; monetization strategy. This role &amp;amp; practice will span both traditional fiat rails and the emerging crypto and stablecoin infrastructure across Stripe, Bridge, Privy, and Tempo — positioning it as one of the most forward-looking advisory capabilities in financial services today. You will run workshops for c-suite &amp;amp; senior management around this capabilities and support the team globally on including this workstream in their respective enterprise transformation workshop&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe works with the world&#39;s most ambitious platforms, marketplaces, and enterprises building the next generation of financial products — and the scale of what they&#39;re building creates an extraordinary opportunity to go deeper. As these users expand into new markets, launch AI-powered products, and layer embedded finance onto their core offering, the topics that unlock their next phase of growth become increasingly strategic: &lt;em&gt;design a monetization strategy that captures full value, price competitively across geographies without eroding margin, structure go-to-market motions and sales enablement for white-labelled financial products, and translate Stripe&#39;s capabilities into durable revenue streams for their business.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role exists to meet that moment — bringing a more prescriptive, hands-on advisory approach to the users where commercial model design is the primary lever for growth, and ensuring that Stripe&#39;s most strategic relationships are supported not just with best-in-class infrastructure, but with the monetization and revenue strategy expertise to make the most of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a strategy &amp;amp; transformation advisor for growth &amp;amp; monetization, you will own and build Growth &amp;amp; Monetization sub-practice end-to-end. You will be the globally recognised expert in this space working directly with and advising some of Stripe’s strategic users and in process enabling your teammates to do the same. Your work will sit at the intersection of commercial strategy, product economics, and payments infrastructure — and will span five core advisory domains:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. New Revenue Channel Growth &amp;amp; Discovery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with platforms, marketplaces, and enterprise users at the earliest stages of their thinking to identify, validate, and prioritise new revenue channels. This includes embedded finance, monetization of distribution, bundled value-added services, and adjacency expansion. You will bring structure, data, and commercial rigour to decisions that are often made on instinct.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. AI Product Pricing Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SaaS companies are racing to launch AI-powered features and products — and most are flying blind on pricing. You will develop a repeatable advisory model that helps users design pricing architectures for AI products: usage-based vs. seat-based vs. outcome-based models, packaging strategy, willingness-to-pay research, and competitive positioning. This is a fast-moving space and an area where Stripe can take a distinctive, opinionated stance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Platform &amp;amp; Marketplace monetization on Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe powers some of the world&#39;s most sophisticated platforms and marketplaces. You will help existing and prospective platform users unlock the full commercial potential of their Stripe integration — including but not limited to buy-rate modelling, revenue share to interchange-plus transitions, merchant segmentation and tiered pricing, and product-to-commercial-model fit across Connect, Terminal, Money management products (Capital, Treasury, Issuing), and Billing. You will draw on and extend the existing monetization Strategy capability &amp;amp; offering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Geographic Expansion &amp;amp; Payments monetization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As users expand into new markets, their payments economics change significantly. You will advise on how monetization models need to evolve across card mix, scheme fee structures, local regulation, and competitive pricing dynamics in new geographies. The output will be clear market-entry pricing strategies, multi-year margin models, and phased expansion plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Embedded Finance &amp;amp; Digital Assets monetization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As platforms increasingly embed financial products into their core offerings, monetization strategy becomes one of the most complex and consequential decisions they face. This advisory domain covers the full spectrum of Money as a Service (MaaS) products: how platforms, marketplaces, and vertical SaaS companies can design and price the financial products they embed — including &lt;strong&gt;payments acceptance, card issuing programmes, treasury and money-movement capabilities, working capital and lending facilities, and stablecoin or crypto-native infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt; You will help users build monetization models that capture the full economic value of their embedded financial stack, advising on revenue share structures, margin stacks, product bundling, and the commercial trade-offs between depth and scale across each financial product category. This domain spans both traditional fiat rails and emerging digital asset infrastructure, and is relevant wherever a platform is moving beyond pure SaaS economics into financial services revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sub-practice build and leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, launch, and own the Growth &amp;amp; Monetization advisory sub-practice within Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the methodology, offering structure, engagement models, and pricing for advisory workstreams across all five domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a library of reusable frameworks, financial models, benchmarks, and pitch materials that the global S&amp;amp;T team can deploy independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish Stripe as having a distinctive, opinionated position on growth and monetization in our target verticals and segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report sub-practice performance: pipeline contribution, closed Professional Services revenue, NPS, and user outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client advisory and pre-sales&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the lead advisor and subject matter expert in strategic pre-sales engagements, bringing structured monetization thinking to the earliest commercial conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery workshops, pricing strategy sessions, and monetization blueprint engagements with C-suite and senior leadership at strategic users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of Professional Services workshops, engagements &amp;amp; deals in this domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives and Solutions Engineers to position the capability as a differentiator in competitive deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable the Strategy &amp;amp; Transformation team globally to incorporate Growth &amp;amp; Monetization thinking into their existing client engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop training programmes, playbooks, and certification paths for the ProServ team to deliver foundational Growth &amp;amp; Monetization advisory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an internal escalation point and thought partner for complex monetization questions arising from any strategy &amp;amp; transformation engagement worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product and market intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deep knowledge of pricing and monetization trends across SaaS, platforms, AI, and industries including but not limited to fintech — and bring those insights back into Stripe&#39;s GTM motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Stripe&#39;s Product and Engineering teams to inform product roadmap decisions based on user monetization needs and gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce thought leadership content — frameworks, benchmarks, reports — that reinforces Stripe&#39;s credibility in this space externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross Functional collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Stripe&#39;s internal product, finance, and go-to-market leadership to help explore our own monetization model around these services — advising on how we can package this engagement to improve margin and revenue outcomes for our business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an internal thought partner to senior Stripe leadership on how the monetization model should evolve as the company&#39;s product surface expands across fiat rails, stablecoins, and new financial infrastructure categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in management consulting, product/commercial leadership role, with a demonstrable track record in pricing strategy, monetization design, or growth advisory with payments experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in: SaaS pricing and packaging, platform/marketplace monetization, payments economics, AI product commercialisation, and geographic market expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building a practice, capability, or offering from scratch — including the methodology, commercial model, and go-to-market collateral — within a consulting, technology, or financial services firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modelling skills and the ability to build rigorous buy-rate, revenue share, and unit economics models that hold up in C-suite conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and executive presence — able to present complex monetization strategy clearly and persuasively to senior business leaders, and to build credibility quickly in pre-sales environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in pre-sales advisory or solution-selling in a technology or professional services context, with a track record of closing sizable engagements and developing Statements of Work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to enable and upskill colleagues — not just to do the work yourself, but to build the capability across a distributed global team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising high-growth SaaS or fintech companies on pricing strategy for new product lines, including AI-powered features or usage-based models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with payments infrastructure — including Stripe Connect, interchange economics, scheme fee structures, and embedded finance — and how these translate into platform commercial models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in working across multiple geographies, with an understanding of how payments pricing, regulation, and competitive dynamics vary by market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A network and reputation in the monetization or pricing strategy community, with published thought leadership a distinct advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in a high-growth internet or software company, particularly one that navigated a significant monetization or business model transition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with crypto, stablecoin, or digital assets economics — including an understanding of how platforms like Bridge, Privy, and Tempo are reshaping financial infrastructure monetization and what commercial models are emerging in this space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to build something genuinely new inside one of the most important technology companies of our generation. Stripe&#39;s users are at inflection points — launching new products, entering new markets, monetising new capabilities — and they are hungry for expert guidance they can trust. The person who builds this practice will have a direct impact on the trajectory of hundreds of companies, the revenues of Stripe&#39;s Professional Services business, and the confidence of our sales teams globally. If you have strong opinions about how businesses should monetise and grow — and the drive to turn those opinions into a global offering — this role was built for you.&lt;/p&gt;

job-04f3ulp:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace team’s mission is to create and support work environments that are welcoming, comfortable, and intuitive. These spaces are designed to promote collaboration, well-being, and productivity while adhering to the rigorous safety, security, and confidentiality standards required of a financial services company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace Experience team comprises operations, hospitality-focused and financially responsible professionals who directly shape the daily experiences of Stripes, visitors, and candidates across 20+ global office locations. This geographically dispersed team oversees facilities management, daily operations, and programs, including a culinary team dedicated to preparing nutritious meals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a strategic leader and experienced workplace manager with a high EQ who&#39;s enthusiastic about, and has a driving need to deliver, the best possible workplace experience for Stripes. You will be a key member of our Experience team and responsible for ensuring that workplace operations, experiences, facilities, and programs run smoothly at our Dublin office. As a business partner, you have a deep understanding of the needs, experiences, and day-to-day realities of Stripes at your location and build strong relationships not only with site leads but also with cross-functional partners across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a high level of expertise and operational oversight—from understanding how the building functions top to bottom to governance of contractor team performance and ensuring financial accountability. A key part of the role is anticipating the needs of the business by understanding both the site and the broader context of company growth. You will gather and synthesize feedback from multiple sources to ensure the workplace strategy is informed by real insights from the ground. While enterprise workplace strategy is developed centrally, you are expected to bring informed recommendations based on local business needs and operational insight, and to own successful implementation and adoption at your site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee workplace operations at your site(s), providing direction on all workplace services, including building operations, front of house, shipping &amp;amp; receiving, events support, and employee health and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound, independent operational decisions by balancing business impact, risk, cost, and employee experience, seeking alignment when decisions create broader organizational impact or precedent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and motivate a team of workplace services professionals, providing direction, coaching, and performance management to drive team excellence and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders, including senior leadership, department heads, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong rapport with locally assigned Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operational performance for your site by monitoring service levels and utilization, identifying trends, resolving root causes, and driving continuous improvement across workplace operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively anticipate business needs by understanding both local context and company priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop thoughtful, data-informed recommendations that help shape workplace programs and experiences while maintaining alignment with global standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold workplace partners and service providers accountable for performance, ensuring contractual obligations, service levels, and operational standards are consistently achieved while driving continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our Finance &amp;amp; Strategy partner and IFM partner to develop and oversee the opex budget for all facilities, opex, fixed assets and events of the Dublin office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the local site leadership team to activate the office by creating engagement, connection, and an inclusive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft relevant communications and documentation regarding Workplace policies and programs for Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent execution of global workplace programs, standards, and policies at your site,&amp;nbsp; as developed by our Food, Space Planning, and Programs teams, adapting implementation to local operational requirements while maintaining alignment with enterprise objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Workplace team&#39;s goals by taking on ad hoc tasks and projects as they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in workplace/hospitality management in a fast-paced environment with a strong customer service orientation and an understanding of operational best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong demonstrated ability in facilities management, vendor, and budget management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strength in building relationships with key internal partners to ensure efficiency and understanding on cross-functional projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team focused on customer service, hospitality, and operations, with the ability and desire to develop and coach your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize operational data, stakeholder feedback, and business context into clear recommendations that support sound decision making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An innovative mindset with the ability to drive exceptional workplace services and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Suite, Slack and Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear willingness to take a hands-on approach and dive into the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional partners and translate enterprise strategy into effective local execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, digging into problems to understand the root cause and delivering scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive in a fast-paced workplace with rapidly changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept at using and experimenting with provided AI tools for things like, identifying practical opportunities to automate routine work, generate operational insights from workplace data, and improve the experience for employees and visitors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An innovative mindset with the ability to drive exceptional workplace services and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-0wfb3aj:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Talent Wanted. For hazardous journey. &lt;s&gt;Small wages&lt;/s&gt;, bitter cold, long months of complete darkness, constant danger, safe return doubtful. Honour and recognition in case of success.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fridtjof Nansen crossed the Arctic, going places no human had ever been. Together with our users, we&#39;re doing the same onchain: charting entirely new territory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nansen is the onchain analytics platform traders and funds use to see what&#39;s actually happening on-chain. We label and track 500M+ blockchain addresses, the largest such dataset in the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our mission:&lt;/strong&gt; Surface the signal and create winners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This seat also comes with a defined runway: you&#39;ll start as an IC, with a clear path to Engineering Manager within 12–18 months for the right person.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do at Nansen&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work with data engineers and ML engineers to build the data infrastructure that powers Nansen&#39;s customer-facing analytics product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and scale data pipelines and infrastructure in ClickHouse, Postgres, Python, and dbt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the pipelines behind 500M+ labeled addresses, moving terabytes of streaming and batch data every day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with crypto researchers, software engineers, and product to shape how data gets modeled, surfaced, and productized&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own data quality, reliability, and observability end-to-end. At most analytics companies a wrong number is a support ticket. Here, it&#39;s a position someone took.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other data engineers and raise the technical bar across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools and agents to move faster and cut the busywork out of your day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve shipped and scaled high-performance data systems in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in SQL and Python, with real hands-on experience in dbt, ClickHouse, and Postgres&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of streaming data architectures, comfortable operating at genuine scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work the full data stack: ingestion, transformation, storage, modeling, serving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You already build with tools like Cursor, Claude Code, and MCPs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write clearly. This team is remote and async, so most decisions get made in writing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: experience leading or managing projects in a smaller team, fluency in onchain data structures, Web3 technologies, and crypto markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we offer our crew&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary. Meaningful equity. Real ownership in what you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully remote with support for in-person co-location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual company retreat and team off-sites in Singapore, Bangkok, or Oslo, with flights and accommodation covered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited AI tokens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your own OpenClaw for work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nansen Pro account: full access to the most detailed onchain data in the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speed, ownership, curiosity, courage, transparency, simplicity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A front-row seat (and a hand in building) the next chapter of finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Work visa sponsorship is not provided for this role.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Safe return doubtful. Honour and recognition in case of success.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

job-0g9w5ba:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and pursue new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. We have significant work ahead, which gives you the opportunity to do important work that expands access to the global economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The APAC Risk team helps Stripe launch and grow products responsibly. We work closely with global Product, Partnerships, and Risk teams to identify product risks early, define practical controls, and make risk decisions easier to execute at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Risk Strategist, you will help Stripe launch new Local Payment Methods (LPMs) and other products safely as part of our broader global expansion efforts. You will be part of a team that identifies, assesses, and manages risk across LPMs and other product launches. Your focus will be on building agent-based workflows that help scale LPM launches and related risk assessments across cross-functional teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify risk scenarios associated with new products, product changes, and LPM initiatives. Translate those scenarios into clear requirements, controls, and actions for different cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve and automate product-risk workflows through AI tools, data, and agent-based solutions. Define and build consistent, scalable processes with reduced manual load&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help set the risk strategy and operating approach for product launches, including how teams assess risk, record decisions, and monitor outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate complex risk issues clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders, with practical recommendations that support responsible product growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define metrics that track risk exposure, control effectiveness, and operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships across Risk and Product, and help align teams when trade-offs or ambiguity arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop expertise that can support adjacent product-risk areas over time, including fraud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are comfortable working in ambiguous spaces where products, risks, and processes are still being defined. You can reason through risk scenarios, bring structure to complex questions, and work with technical partners to turn recommendations into scalable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are also motivated by improving how work gets done. You do not only identify risks. You look for ways to make risk assessment, decision-making, and monitoring more automated, consistent, and useful for the teams building Stripe products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in risk, financial services, fintech, product strategy, data, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with cross-functional teams, especially Product, Engineering, Data Science, Operations, or Partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical judgment and the ability to turn complex information into clear recommendations and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with and a keen interest in building and applying automation, tools, or agent-based workflows to improve processes and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data to investigate problems, assess performance, or inform decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate clearly with a range of stakeholders and build alignment across teams with different priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience assessing risk for new products, product launches, or material product changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, product risk, platform risk, fraud, or financial crimes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using and building agentic workflows and using AI tools to simplify processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, data analysis, data science workflows, or building operational tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with technical teams to define requirements and improve internal systems or processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with risk-control design, monitoring, or policy development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-19gjbre:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Counsel, Money Movement Legal (Asia-Pacific)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Legal team at Stripe manages the legal and regulatory aspects of designing, building, and launching products and services. The team works on technical, commercial, and regulatory matters and advises product, engineering, and partnerships teams on issues across financial services, business, and technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role supports the Money Movement and Storage business across Asia-Pacific. The business includes stored-value and e-money, foreign exchange, cross-border transfer, stablecoin and digital asset, and other financial products. The team helps ensure these products comply with applicable laws and regulations while supporting responsible product development and commercialization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Product Counsel, you&#39;ll advise teams on the legal and regulatory considerations for money movement products across Asia-Pacific. You&#39;ll partner with product, engineering, partnerships, compliance, risk, marketing, and Legal teams to navigate emerging requirements and bring products to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the Product Legal team deliver products that comply with laws and contractual commitments to users globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise product teams on the intersection of technological innovation, e-commerce user experiences, and financial services compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, engineering, partnerships, compliance, risk, and marketing teams on product development and commercialization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise teams on new and emerging legal and regulatory developments, identify potential effects on business activities, and apply existing laws to new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with colleagues across the global Legal team to support regulatory structures, customer agreements, and strategic financial partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and build scalable processes for legal review and product launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date on money movement laws and regulations, and serve as a strategic advisor to senior managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a qualified lawyer in a law firm, in-house legal team, or government agency, with expertise in payment services laws and regulations, such as the Payment Services Act of Singapore&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualification to practice law, preferably in a jurisdiction in Asia-Pacific&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising technology teams and translating complex legal requirements into clear, actionable advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate with teammates, share knowledge, understand complex business models and product use cases, and exercise sound judgment with imperfect information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, project management, and prioritization skills in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on the development of stablecoin and digital asset products, particularly across multiple regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting legal, regulatory, or commercial matters for money movement or financial services products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

