job-0fh1lbh:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a seasoned and self-driven Senior Talent Acquisition Partner to join our team as a contract for 6 - 9 months, with a focus on engineering/tech hiring and coverage across general functions such as commercial, finance, and operations. This is a high-impact individual contributor role, ideal for someone who works independently, partners closely with hiring managers, and brings strong insights into the Web3/crypto industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own full-cycle recruitment, provide market insights and reporting, and be a strategic partner in improving our TA processes—especially in sourcing and talent mapping.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7 years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with solid exposure to tech/engineering and generalist functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the Web3/crypto industry, including key talent pools and hiring challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferably fluent in Mandarin and English, both written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work independently and manage recruitment workflows with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and business partnering skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset; comfortable working with recruitment metrics and reporting tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ATS platforms and sourcing tools (e.g., LinkedIn Recruiter, GitHub, Web3-focused platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end recruitment across a variety of roles including engineering/tech and general functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a TA Business Partner, offering counsel and strategic input to hiring managers on talent market trends and hiring strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute sourcing strategies, with a focus on building pipelines for technical and hard-to-fill roles in the Web3/crypto space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide weekly reporting and analytics to hiring managers and the Head of TA, using data to track progress and identify improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct talent mapping and market intelligence to support proactive hiring and better decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously review and enhance TA processes, especially around strategic sourcing and candidate experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with Web3/crypto talent trends, bringing insights into how to attract and engage top talent in the space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with People/HR teams on cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to think outside the box to create new ways of sourcing and building a strong pipeline. Shows creativity in finding talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1s4yasm:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive on the Enterprise team at Stripe, you&#39;ll drive future growth at Stripe by building new relationships with prospective companies, turning them into happy Stripe users. You&#39;ll manage and elevate relationships with a named account list within a key vertical while identifying new growth opportunities and ways Stripe can exceed expectations. This role will be dedicated to accounts focused in Australia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive, you will own a portfolio of established enterprise customers and drive their continued growth with Stripe. This is a hunting role within existing accounts: you will identify new opportunities to increase payment volume, activate additional products, expand Stripe’s footprint across business units and subsidiaries, and build long-term customer stickiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will create and execute account strategies for complex technology customers, engaging both executive and technical stakeholders to understand their priorities and translate Stripe’s platform into clear commercial and operational value. The role spans the full expansion cycle, from account planning and opportunity creation through commercial negotiation, activation, and post-launch growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercially ambitious and highly autonomous seller who can balance near-term revenue delivery with the long-term relationship building required to grow a strategic book of business. You should be comfortable navigating technical and business conversations with leaders across the business.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;esponsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a named portfolio of existing enterprise customers and develop strategic account plans to grow Stripe’s revenue, product adoption, and market share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, create, and progress expansion opportunities across customer business units, subsidiaries, geographies, and product lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute outbound strategies within existing accounts to develop new executive relationships and create qualified opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the full expansion sales cycle, from opportunity identification and discovery through commercial negotiation, activation, go-live, and continued growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand customers’ complex business and technical challenges, and position Stripe’s core platform and products as solutions to those needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product workshops, business case development, and financial analyses that help customers quantify the value of investing further in Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with internal teams including Product, Engineering, Partnerships, and Post-Sales to coordinate migrations, activations, and strategic customer initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of sales experience, with at least 2 years working with enterprise customers, preferably in a technology company, with a demonstrated record of exceeding commercial targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing and expanding existing upper-middle-market or enterprise customer relationships, including identifying new opportunities within a portfolio rather than relying solely on renewals or inbound demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop and execute strategic account plans across complex organisations with multiple business units, stakeholders, or subsidiaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience leading complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles from discovery through commercial negotiation, activation, go-live, and continued growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex technical capabilities into clear business value and engage confidently with senior business and technical stakeholders, including Product, Engineering, Finance, and executive leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth-stage internet or software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech or payments is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1vrqz10:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;The Stablecoin team builds and operates Coinbase Custom Stablecoins (CCS), the platform that lets partners launch their own branded, USDC-backed stablecoins on Coinbase&#39;s infrastructure. As a Software Engineer on this team within the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers/product-groups&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Developer&lt;/a&gt; group, you&#39;ll build and extend the backend services and onchain contracts that power issuance, reserves, minting and burning, and rewards distribution for a fast-growing roster of partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and extend smart contract functionality for minting, burning, and safeguarding custom stablecoin supply, working closely with senior engineers on design and security review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement backend services that power onboarding, issuance, reserve accounting, and rewards distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineers, designers, and product managers to turn the stablecoin roadmap into shipped features every quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reporting, monitoring, and internal tooling that improve reliability and operational excellence for the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write high-quality, well-tested code across both backend and smart contract surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience building and maintaining production backend services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to writing, testing, or deploying smart contracts (Solidity or similar EVM languages), or demonstrated ability to ramp quickly in new technical domains with mentorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working within a service-oriented architecture and contributing to established systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Golang and blockchain fundamentals (Ethereum or similar EVM chains).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates the ability to responsibly use generative AI tools and copilots (e.g., LibreChat, Gemini, Glean) in daily workflows, continuously learn as tools evolve, and apply human‑in‑the‑loop practices to deliver business‑ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
