job-1qk3hzv:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive covering strategic accounts, you’ll manage existing relationships and identify new opportunities to expand Stripe’s footprint within existing accounts. Specifically, we’re looking for someone who can execute on long-term sales strategies, engage with internal and external stakeholders, align on technical and business requirements with product teams, build value in competitive situations, lead commercial negotiations, and close deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work strategic Stripe customers to develop and execute long-term sales strategies to expand Stripe’s revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand business with high growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop outbound strategies to create and nurture opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal strategy and commercial negotiations for large, complex renewals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships with executive stakeholders within your book of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for account mapping and coordinating effective meetings with the appropriate external stakeholders expanding the customer relationship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to team projects to develop and refine our sales process and help shape the Stripe sales culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of sales experience, preferably selling a highly technical product to enterprise customers, with a track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and execute account plans spanning multiple business units across complex organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for working well with a wide range of people, both internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, particularly for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-0zaozjv:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who are we?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FalconX is a pioneering team of operators, investors, and builders committed to revolutionizing institutional access to the crypto markets. Operating at the intersection of traditional finance and  cutting-edge technology, FalconX addresses the industry&#39;s foremost challenges: Navigating the digital asset market can be complex and fragmented, with limited products and services that support trading strategies, structures, and liquidity found in conventional financial markets. As a comprehensive solution for all digital asset strategies from start to scale, FalconX operates as the connective tissue empowering clients with seamless navigation through the ever- evolving cryptocurrency landscape.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Low-Latency Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, provision, and maintain ultra-low latency AWS and hybrid network topologies, including VPCs, exchange gateways, and regional deployment expansions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Tuning:&lt;/strong&gt; Optimize Linux OS kernels and compute performance using CPU isolation (isolcpus), AWS Cluster Placement Groups, and enhanced networking (ENA/ENI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure as Code:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive infrastructure automation, provisioning, and configuration management using Terraform and Ansible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Scaling:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect infrastructure to support expanding Exchange Market Making (EMM), Project Market Making (PMM), and TradFi exchange convergences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability &amp;amp; Reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Build telemetry and monitoring pipelines using Grafana Cloud and Alloy to ensure continuous visibility into platform performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Guide the technical roadmap, mentor junior engineers, and act as an escalation lead for critical system incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; in Infrastructure Engineering, Systems Engineering, or SRE, with a focus on &lt;strong&gt;low-latency electronic trading environments&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep Linux Internals Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced experience with kernel-level performance tuning, memory management, and network I/O optimization (isolcpus, network profiling, ring buffers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AWS Low-Latency Design:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated experience leveraging AWS low-latency constructs (Placement Groups, ENA/ENI, high-performance EC2 instance optimization).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trading Protocols &amp;amp; Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with FIX protocol, Aeron messaging, or low-latency colocation connectivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HFT &amp;amp; Market Workflows:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with high-frequency trading (HFT) workflows or crypto exchange API integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation Mastery:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;Terraform&lt;/strong&gt; for cloud infrastructure and &lt;strong&gt;Ansible&lt;/strong&gt; for OS configuration and patching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Networking Fundamentals:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of physical network topologies, TCP/IP, UDP, and low-latency network routing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Containers &amp;amp; CI/CD:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with Docker, Docker Compose, Jenkins, and modern deployment pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability Ecosystem:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience setting up production monitoring using Grafana Cloud, Alloy, or Prometheus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on scripting capability in Python/Bash, with development experience in &lt;strong&gt;Rust&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;Java&lt;/strong&gt; preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hardware acceleration technologies (FPGAs, SmartNICs) or custom network card driver tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of PTP (Precision Time Protocol) / IEEE 1588 or clock synchronization setup for high-precision trade timestamping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The base pay for this role is expected to be between $179,000 - $218,000 in New York City.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;This expected base pay range is based on information at the time this post was generated. This role will also be eligible for other forms of compensation such as a performance linked bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package. Actual compensation for a successful candidate will be determined based on a number of factors such as location, skillset, experience, qualifications &lt;strong&gt;and the level at which the candidate is hired.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notice at Collection and Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants located in California and/or applying to a role based in California, please refer to our Notice at Collection and Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://docs.google.com/document/d/14H2RKQ1L1ezo605QXotmqxCOnKgIuv21oB-95zR7_0I/edit?usp%3Dsharing&amp;amp;sa=D&amp;amp;source=calendar&amp;amp;ust=1715533493387657&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1Q6amAagRdjSqTfoecQ4aY&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusivity Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FalconX is committed to building a diverse, inclusive, equitable, and safe workspace for all people. Our roles are intended for people from all walks of life. We encourage all those interested in applying to our organization to submit an application regardless if you are missing some of the listed background requirements, skills, or experiences!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our commitment to inclusivity, FalconX would like to acknowledge that the EEOC survey has limited potential responses that you can select. For legal reasons, FalconX must use this language to align with federal requirements, however, we want to ensure that you are able to provide a response to our own voluntary survey questions about your identity that best aligns with your most true self.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;FalconX is an equal opportunity employer and will not discriminate against an applicant or employee based on race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, ethnicity, sex (including gender, pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), age, physical or mental disability, veteran or military status, genetic information, citizenship, or any other legally-recognized protected basis under federal, state, or local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Applicants with disabilities may be entitled to reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act and other applicable state or local laws. A reasonable accommodation is a change in the way things are normally done which will ensure an equal employment opportunity without imposing undue hardship on FalconX. Please inform FalconX’s People team at recruiting@falconx.io, if you need assistance with participating in the application process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-0fli729:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Flow Traders is strengthening leadership across its Research Engineering department and is hiring an Engineering Manager. Research Engineers conduct applied research jointly with quants to deliver our trading models and research platform. As the firm scales, the quality of engineering management has become one of the most important factors in how well our teams grow, retain talent, and deliver - and this role exists to raise that bar.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering Managers are accountable for the planning and people side of the organisation - project deliveries, growth, performance, culture and hiring - and partner with technical leads who own architecture, technical direction, and hands-on execution. The two work in close partnership; neither succeeds without the other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be measured on the engineers you develop and the outcomes your team delivers. You will spend the large majority of your time leading people and managing delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will do:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;Own the roadmap: manage priorities, planning, and sequencing of the work in line with company goals.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Develop your engineers: own career planning, promotions, coaching, and structured, continuous performance management.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Plan and build the team: lead hiring, headcount planning, and resource allocation in line with the team&#39;s roadmap and the firm&#39;s priorities.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cultivate a healthy team: actively manage culture, morale, and productivity, and address conflict early and constructively.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Lead with rhythm: hold regular one-on-ones, give clear and timely feedback, and invest in team building.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Translate technical and business requirements into clear delivery plans, identifying dependencies with other teams and risks up front.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Act as the liaison between Engineering, Trading, and Quant teams to design and roll out new products.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Drive delivery predictability: track progress against plan, manage risk and scope trade-offs, and report status clearly to stakeholders.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Continuously improve delivery processes and team velocity.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Ensure alignment: keep your team&#39;s work connected to organisational goals and delivery timelines, collaborating closely with Tech Leads and Staff Engineers on research and technical direction.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you need to succeed:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;Strong people-leadership skills: coaching, feedback, conflict resolution, and building an environment in which engineers thrive&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;Strong project management skills: experience building roadmaps, sequencing work, managing dependencies and risk, and driving delivery predictability in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A technical or research background sufficient to earn the respect of the engineers you manage and to engage credibly in technical discussions.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Demonstrated experience leading, growing, and managing the performance of applied researchers and software engineers.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A track record of delivering applied research through a team, balancing scope, quality, and timelines.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Sound judgment in hiring and developing talent.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Excellent communication with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, including experience managing cross-functional stakeholders (e.g. Trading, Quant).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Based in Amsterdam, or willing to relocate.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

