job-1w0baq3:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ripple Treasury is redefining how businesses move, manage, and settle money across borders — and we’re looking for a Director of Global Transformation to help lead that charge internally. This senior individual-contributor and leadership role is part of our Program Management team. It requires broad collaboration with Product, Engineering, Operations, Finance, and Go-to-Market teams. The role focuses on driving sophisticated, enterprise-wide initiatives from strategy to execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own end-to-end transformation programs that improve the way Ripple Treasury functions at scale — spanning process development, technology adoption, leading shifts within the organization, and performance measurement. This role requires someone who thrives in ambiguity, builds trust with senior team members quickly, and can translate high-level strategic goals into actionable roadmaps and measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead enterprise-wide transformation initiatives across Ripple Treasury, driving cross-functional alignment from ideation through delivery and post-launch optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders from Product, Engineering, Finance, Operations, and GTM to define program scope, success metrics, and governance structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own sophisticated program roadmaps: build and maintain project plans, identify dependencies, proactively surface risks, and drive resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion organizational change management — develop communication strategies, training plans, and adoption frameworks that embed lasting change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate ambiguous strategic priorities into structured, executable work with clear ownership and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain program health reporting and executive-level status updates; facilitate steering committees and cross-functional working sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify systemic inefficiencies in how Ripple Treasury operates and develop the argument, roadmap, and delivery plan to address them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with peer Program Managers and serve as a senior thought partner, elevating the practice of coordinating programs across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the PMO perspective in planning cycles, crafting how transformation initiatives are prioritized and resourced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BRING:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in program management, management consulting, strategy, or a related field, with at least 3–5 years in a Director-level or equivalent senior role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning and delivering large-scale, cross-functional transformation programs at a high-growth tech company or financial services firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional collaborator leadership skills — you build credibility quickly with executives and peers alike, and can navigate organizational complexity with ease.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong process design and systems-thinking skills; you can map current-state, develop future-state, and build the bridge between them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across product, engineering, and operations contexts — you don’t need to be a technical expert, but you know how to partner with teams who are.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in written and verbal expression, capable of making complex topics accessible for executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with modern program management tooling (Asana, Jira, Smartsheet, or equivalent); familiarity with data tools (e.g., Looker, Tableau) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience applying AI tools to program management or operational workflows — including using large language models (e.g., Claude, ChatGPT) to accelerate research, synthesize information, draft communications, or automate routine tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort adopting and evaluating emerging AI capabilities; able to identify where AI tooling can meaningfully improve team productivity and program outcomes, and champion adoption across cross-functional collaborators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in FinTech, payments, or financial infrastructure is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Claude (Anthropic) for business workflows — including prompt design, Cowork or API-based automation, or deploying Claude within team tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in management consulting (top-tier firm) or corporate strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to global or multi-regional program delivery across time zones and regulatory environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with B2B payments, treasury management, or cross-border settlement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP, PgMP, or equivalent certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Ripple Treasury&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ripple is the leading provider of crypto solutions for businesses, helping financial institutions move money globally with speed, transparency, and cost-effectiveness. Our Treasury team sits at the center of that mission — managing the capital and operational infrastructure that makes real-time global payments possible. You’ll join a high-performing, passionate team where your work has direct impact on how the global financial system evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role works alongside a peer Director-level Program Manager and reports to the Head of Program Management within Treasury. You’ll have the scope, sponsorship, and autonomy to drive meaningful transformation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For positions that will be based in IL, the annual salary range for this position is below. Actual salaries may vary based on numerous factors including, among other things, an individual applicant’s experience and qualifications for the position. This range does not include equity or additional compensation, such as bonuses or commissions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;IL Annual Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$196,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$240,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Do Your Best Work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The opportunity to build in a fast-paced start-up environment with experienced industry leaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A learning environment where you can dive deep into the latest technologies and make an impact.&amp;nbsp; A professional development budget to support other modes of learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Thrive in an environment where no matter what race, ethnicity, gender, origin, or culture they identify with, every employee is a respected, valued, and empowered part of the team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In-office collaboration for moments that matter is important to our culture, and we give managers and teams the flexibility to decide which 10+ days a month they come in.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bi-weekly all-company meeting - business updates and ask me anything style discussion with our Leadership Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We come together for moments that matter which include team offsites, team bonding activities, happy hours and more!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Control of Your Finances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, bonuses, and equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive benefits that cover physical and mental healthcare, retirement, family forming, and family support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Employee giving match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mobile phone stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Care of Yourself&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;R&amp;amp;R days so you can rest and recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous wellness reimbursement and weekly onsite &amp;amp; virtual programming&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous vacation policy - work with your manager to take time off when you need it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Industry-leading parental leave policies. Family planning benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Catered lunches, fully-stocked kitchens with premium snacks/beverages, and plenty of fun events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Benefits listed above are for full-time employees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ripple is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We’re committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. We do not discriminate against qualified employees or applicants because of race, color, religion, gender identity, sex, sexual identity, pregnancy, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, military status, or any other characteristic protected by local law or ordinance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please find our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/eu-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;UK/EU Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/a&gt;and our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/ca-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;California Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for reference.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-0vnawk2:
&lt;h4&gt;About the company&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Ondo Finance. Our mission is to provide institutional-grade, blockchain-enabled investment products and services. We have both a technology arm that develops decentralized finance technology, and an asset management arm that creates and manages tokenized funds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We were the first company to tokenize exposure to US Treasuries, and have since expanded into several other assets. We are also focused on incubating protocols that can support both tokenized real-world assets and traditional crypto.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by folks from Goldman Sachs Digital Assets Team, we’re backed by some of the best investors in the world including Founders Fund, Coinbase Ventures, Pantera Capital, Tiger Global, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently the leaders in the space in terms of AUM and are well capitalized to continue to grow the firm. We&#39;re fully remote, with team members across the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Affiliate Manager to build and scale relationships with affiliates, creators, traders, and key opinion leaders across the global crypto ecosystem, supporting the growth of Ondo’s products and mindshare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the strategy and day-to-day operation of our affiliate and KOL programs—from identifying and recruiting high-potential partners to negotiating terms, launching campaigns, managing relationships, and measuring performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly hands-on role for someone who combines strong relationship-building skills with commercial judgment, crypto-native market knowledge, and a rigorous approach to performance. Working closely with Growth, Content, Product, Business Development, Legal, and regional teams, you will build a scalable partner network that drives measurable awareness, acquisition, trading activity, and retention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the global affiliate and KOL program and strategy, with clear goals across awareness, qualified acquisition, trading activity, retention, and return on investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, evaluate, recruit, and manage high-potential affiliates, creators, traders, educators, and community leaders across priority platforms, audiences, and regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop distinct partner and campaign strategies supporting Ondo’s narrative and product initiatives, reflecting their different audiences, use cases, product mechanics, and regulatory considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate compensation, referral structures, deliverables, exclusivity, and performance incentives while managing the complete partner lifecycle from outreach through activation, review, and renewal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute campaigns around product launches, new markets, trading competitions, incentives, partnerships, and company milestones, working with Content and Design to provide effective messaging and creative assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Growth to improve referral journeys, tracking, attribution, and conversion, using performance data to optimize partner selection, incentives, campaign design, and budget allocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish scalable reporting, partner tiers, playbooks, workflows, and governance while coordinating with Legal and Compliance on agreements, disclosures, claims, geographic restrictions, and partner conduct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Requirements&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building or managing affiliate, creator, influencer, ambassador, or KOL programs for a crypto exchange, trading platform, brokerage, DeFi protocol, fintech company, or comparable digital product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of the crypto creator and trading ecosystem, including how different audiences discover, evaluate, and engage with financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of tokenized stocks and perpetual futures, including leverage, liquidity, market structure, trading risks, and the needs of investors and active traders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to source, recruit, negotiate with, activate, and retain valuable affiliates or KOLs across multiple channels or regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of delivering measurable acquisition, funded-account, trading, revenue, or retention outcomes through partner-led campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and analytical judgment, with experience evaluating audience quality, attribution, acquisition cost, fraud risk, partner economics, and return on investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent relationship-management, negotiation, organization, and cross-functional execution skills, with the ability to operate independently in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with affiliate disclosures, financial promotions, geographic restrictions, tokenized securities, and leveraged-product marketing is strongly preferred; international experience, additional languages, and established industry relationships are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we offer&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation including but not limited to salary, future token rights, and/or equity (according to your preferences) — We are well-funded and believe that great talent deserves great compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full benefits (medical, vision, and dental) and flexible vacation policy (PTO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first team across many countries — You will be an early team member helping shape our vision, culture, and design practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A+ colleagues — Our team includes alumni from: Goldman Sachs, Blackrock, Two Sigma, Bridgewater, SpaceX, AWS, Meta, Google, McKinsey, Coinbase, Circle, Uniswap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best-in-class investors — We are proud to be backed by leading crypto experts and VCs, including Pantera Capital, Founders Fund and Coinbase Ventures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

job-0vj8b6q:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link Partnerships team sources, develops, and manages relationships with the payments ecosystem partners that power Link, Stripe&#39;s consumer wallet. Our team drives the growth and utility of Link by building partnerships with card networks, card issuers, local payment methods, crypto providers, and emerging commerce platforms. We execute on high-impact, cross-functional initiatives that expand Link&#39;s acceptance, improve performance, and enable new payment experiences—including agentic commerce. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and the products used by millions of our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Partner Development Manager who builds and manages Link&#39;s payments partnerships with card networks, card issuers, local payment method providers, and crypto and stablecoin providers. You&#39;ll own the strategy and execution of partnerships that expand Link&#39;s payment capabilities, improve transaction performance, and position Link as the default payments layer for agentic commerce. You&#39;ll negotiate commercial agreements, drive technical integrations, and shape Link&#39;s payments roadmap in collaboration with these partners. As part of these efforts, you&#39;ll collaborate closely with cross-functional stakeholders, including Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, Risk, and others. You&#39;ll also lead relationship management and partner closely with external partners&#39; executive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute Link&#39;s payments partnership strategy across card networks, card issuers, local payment methods, and crypto and stablecoins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and manage commercial agreements with payment partners that expand Link&#39;s acceptance footprint, improve authorization rates, and unlock new payment capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the card network and issuer landscape—including scheme rules, tokenization frameworks, authentication protocols, and competitive dynamics—to inform partnership strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive partnerships that enable Link to serve as the payments layer for agentic commerce, working with networks and issuers to establish rules, liability frameworks, and technical standards for agent-initiated transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather inputs from and coordinate with internal cross-functional stakeholders (including product, risk, compliance, engineering, and security) to drive creation and execution of partner strategy including our global LPM roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product and Engineering to define requirements and shape Link&#39;s payments product roadmap based on partner capabilities and market opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify partner stakeholders who will champion Stripe, educate them about Link&#39;s value proposition, and build alignment between Stripe and our partners&#39; executive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and effectively analyze new partnership opportunities, ultimately making recommendations to relevant decision makers and cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibit an operationally focused mindset, with an ability to lead teams through complex relationship management activities by setting a clear vision and running tight processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You&#39;re a skilled dealmaker and a strategist by nature. You understand how to work closely with Product and Engineering teams and can formulate partner strategies that drive tangible and measurable results. You&#39;re energized by the intersection of payments infrastructure and emerging commerce models, and you see the opportunity to define how payments work in an agentic world.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in or working closely with card networks, card issuers, digital wallets, or payments infrastructure providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience negotiating commercial deals with partners, including scaling such deals across multiple partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, in both verbal and written form, and ability to influence stakeholders across a wide variety of functions, including at executive levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical acumen, especially an ability to understand product strategy and use this understanding to define requirements for scaling products through partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing partnership strategies and identifying, sourcing, and analyzing new partnership opportunities in greenfield segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong agency, can handle ambiguity in a fast-moving organization, and thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with card scheme rules, tokenization (network tokens, device tokens), authentication frameworks (3DS, SCA), and issuer-side authorization optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with emerging payment models such as agentic commerce, embedded payments, or programmable payment flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a new partnership category or vertical from zero—defining the strategy, establishing first partnerships, and scaling the program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1p8044v:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;As a Luxembourg Audit Manager, you&#39;ll join the Internal Audit team and own a portfolio of operational, financial, and compliance audits across Coinbase&#39;s Luxembourg entity operations. This team delivers independent, third-line assurance over governance, risk management, and control effectiveness, helping Coinbase protect customers and maintain trust at scale. You&#39;ll shape audit coverage aligned with European and Luxembourg regulatory requirements (CSSF, ECB, EBA, ESMA), ensure findings from complex audit work are communicated to executive, Board-level, and regulatory audiences, and lead team members to build a best-in-class operational audit function.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and coordinate a portfolio of operational, financial, and compliance audits covering financial controls, regulatory compliance, business processes, vendor/third-party risk, and data governance in accordance with CSSF, CBL, ECB, EBA, and ESMA requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the multi-year operational and compliance audit roadmap, coordinating coverage with co-sourced partners and aligning with enterprise risk initiatives and European regulatory frameworks (MiCA, PSD2, AMLD, DORA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize complex audit findings into high-impact reports and presentations for executive leadership, the Chief Audit Executive, Audit Committee, Board of Directors, and regulatory bodies, ensuring conclusions are rigorous, documented, and actionable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive remediation strategy for operational and compliance findings, challenging management on risk-based solutions, validating corrective actions, and escalating thematic concerns to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business unit leadership across Finance, Compliance, Legal, and Operations to deliver independent advisory value while maintaining third-line independence and objectivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and develop audit talent, mentoring team members and contributing to the growth and modernization of the Internal Audit function across EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in internal audit, external audit, or compliance audit in a regulated financial services environment, with demonstrated experience managing audit teams, concurrent audit portfolios, and co-sourced engagements across EMEA/APAC time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of European and Luxembourg regulatory frameworks (CSSF, CBL, ECB, EBA, ESMA) with proven experience executing audits within these regimes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on audit execution experience across financial controls, operational processes, compliance requirements, data governance, and control certifications using COSO, COBIT, SOC 2, or ISO 27001 frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant professional certifications (CIA, CISA, or CFE) with demonstrated ability to present findings and recommendations to executive, Board-level, and regulatory audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency Notice:&lt;/strong&gt; The target annual &lt;strong&gt;base&lt;/strong&gt; salary for this position can range as detailed below. Total compensation may&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;also include equity and bonus eligibility and benefits (including medical, dental, and vision).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual base salary range (excluding equity and bonus):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€125.970&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€132.600 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
