job-0ughbff:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripes on the Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team operate in a fast-paced internal and external environment that requires collaborating with teams across our organization and with outside stakeholders. The culture is thoughtful, transparent, academically rigorous, and kind. In this role, you will have the opportunity to impact the trajectory of Stripe in the US and enhance financial innovation and inclusion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a team player who wants to represent millions of businesses around the world growing on Stripe, we look forward to hearing from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will deal with a diverse set of issues that straddle financial services, technology, internet regulation, and economic policy. You will define, shape, and advocate for initiatives that increase the GDP of the Internet. You will maintain deep relationships with Members of Congress, committee staff, key federal regulators, and the Executive Branch — building and executing legislative and regulatory strategies on issues central to Stripe&#39;s mission, including payments modernization, financial regulation, artificial intelligence, and the future of agentic commerce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role must reside in the DC, Maryland, Virginia area. We are not accepting remote candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work as part of our Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team across the globe to strategically develop, pursue, and execute policy objectives as part of Stripe&#39;s global policy priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and execute federal legislative advocacy — managing Stripe&#39;s engagement with Congress on key legislative priorities including stablecoins, digital assets, open banking, AI governance, and payments regulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with Members of Congress, committee and personal staff, and serve as Stripe&#39;s frontline representative on federal legislation affecting the payments and technology industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage federal regulatory agencies — including the Treasury Department, OCC, FDIC, Federal Reserve, CFPB, and others — to educate them about Stripe&#39;s business, advocate for sound policy outcomes, and navigate regulatory proceedings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, develop, and execute policy initiatives and campaigns that advance Stripe&#39;s policy goals and those of our users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help colleagues across Stripe understand federal legislative and regulatory developments, identify policy opportunities to grow our business, and translate complex policy dynamics into actionable guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe on trade groups, coalitions, and industry bodies engaged on federal policy issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 10+ years of experience in a policymaking, government, or senior advocacy role — ideally a mix of time on Capitol Hill, in a federal regulatory agency, or in a world-class organization as an in-house government relations expert or other business-related role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background working for a Member of Congress, a committee or leadership office, or in a senior policy role at the US Treasury, OCC, FDIC, White House, or comparable federal institution — with a track record of navigating bipartisan legislative environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in financial services regulation and payments policy, with a strong understanding of the legislative and regulatory landscape across banking, money transmission, and digital assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with, and ideally direct experience on, emerging technology policy — including artificial intelligence, agentic commerce, and the regulatory questions that arise at the intersection of AI and financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationships with policymakers and staff on both sides of the aisle and a reputation for credibility, reliability, and good judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of managing complex, technical policy issues — capable of managing major initiatives independently, driving coalitions, or project managing a cross-functional team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent judgment — capable of making smart decisions in the face of ambiguity and imperfect information and learning from them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A terrific communicator and writer, adept at working with lawyers, regulators, engineers, business teams, and colleagues to make complex concepts clear and understandable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for Stripe&#39;s mission of helping businesses grow and thrive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, curious team-first mindset with experience thriving in ambiguous, high-growth or startup environments across global offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy, humility, and a respect for those who have views that are different from yours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to work with a diverse group of policy, regulatory, and product professionals who care deeply about Stripe&#39;s policy issues, our users, and each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel 25% for meetings and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1fxztrk:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Figure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Figure (NASDAQ: FIGR) is transforming capital markets through blockchain. We’re proving that blockchain isn’t just theory - it’s powering real products used by hundreds of thousands of consumers and institutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By combining blockchain’s transparency and efficiency with AI-driven automation, we’ve reimagined how loans are originated, funded, and traded in secondary markets. From faster processing times to lower costs and reduced bias, our technology is helping borrowers, investors, and financial institutions achieve better outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together with our 170+ partners, we’ve originated over $22 billion in home equity loans (HELOCs) on our blockchain-native platform, making Figure the largest non-bank provider of home equity financing in the U.S. Figure’s ecosystem also includes YLDS, an SEC-registered yield-bearing stablecoin that operates as a tokenized money market fund, and several other products and platforms that are reshaping consumer finance and capital markets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be recognized as one of &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.forbes.com/lists/fintech50/&quot;&gt;Forbes’ Most Innovative Fintech Startups in 2025&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fastcompany.com/91269557/finance-personal-finance-most-innovative-companies-2025&quot;&gt;Fast Company’s Most Innovative Companies in Finance and Personal Finance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a results-driven, customer-focused Team Manager to lead a team of up to 18 Customer Success Associates at varying levels. As a Team Manager, you will oversee daily operations, track performance metrics, develop team members through coaching and training, and manage escalated customer issues to ensure swift, effective resolution. This role plays a key part in delivering outstanding customer service while collaborating with cross-functional departments to drive operational success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*This position requires holding an NMLS License, or obtaining one within 90 days of employment and meeting qualifications for Qualified Individual licensing in needed states.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on leadership to create a positive, collaborative work environment by setting clear expectations, motivating the team, and supporting professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee team performance, focusing on metrics like productivity, efficiency, quality, and SLA adherence, while driving continuous improvement through coaching and regular evaluations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip the team with up-to-date product knowledge, best practices, and company policies to ensure consistent, high-quality customer interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage daily team operations, addressing escalated issues, monitoring workflows, and empowering agents to meet SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure team adherence to Figure’s policies and standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle administrative responsibilities, such as managing performance records, PTO, and disciplinary actions, in compliance with company policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a liaison with Workforce Management, HR, and IT to resolve employee concerns and maintain operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of leadership experience in customer support, preferably in contact centers or financial services industries, with a proven ability to manage performance metrics and drive team improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to inspire, develop, and hold team members accountable while fostering a culture of excellence and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to ensure policy adherence, taking full ownership of team results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker with advanced problem-solving skills, capable of implementing innovative solutions in dynamic, evolving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Results-driven leader with confident, compassionate communication skills, effective in engaging with both team members and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High proficiency in workforce management tools, CRM systems, and data analysis platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to all company security policies and data handling procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete mandatory security awareness training within required timeframes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promptly report any suspected security incidents or suspicious activity to the Security team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Base Compensation Range: $77,400 - $86,000/yr&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;25% annual bonus target, paid quarterly&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Company equity in the form of RSUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the compensation range for the role in the United States. Actual compensation may vary based on a candidate’s experience, skills, location, internal equity, and evolving business needs. While most offers are generally made within the middle of the range, final compensation is determined based on the factors above.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, with 100% employer-paid premiums for employees and their dependents on select plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Company HSA, FSA, Dependent Care FSA, 401(k), and commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Employer-paid life and disability insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;11 observed holidays and PTO plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Up to 12 weeks of paid family leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Continuing education reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on your residential location certain laws might regulate the way Figure manages applicant data. California Residents, please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.figure.com/ca-employee-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;California Employee&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.figure.com/workforce-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;General Workforce Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for further information.&amp;nbsp;By submitting your application, you are agreeing&amp;nbsp; and&amp;nbsp;acknowledging&amp;nbsp;that you have read and understand the above notice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Figure will not sponsor work visas for this position. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-JR1 #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;

job-001neap:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Strategic Program Lead on the International CX Strategic Programs team within the Customer Experience org, you&#39;ll ensure customer experiences are globally relevant, locally compliant, and regionally optimized across APAC, EMEA, and the Americas. You&#39;ll work horizontally across product domains and with regional partners to adapt, localize, and scale initiatives, bringing the CX perspective into launch planning so regional customers are never an afterthought.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional launch readiness by ensuring every product or policy launch is adapted for local markets, including language, payment methods, regulatory coverage, and agent enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface and prioritize region-specific friction by monitoring emerging issues and themes, elevating local trust-breaking patterns to Program Managers and Product teams with clear paths to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt global programs for local context by partnering with Program Managers and Product teams to customize policies, workflows, and automation where regulatory requirements or cultural behaviors differ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional CX, Ops, Risk, and Compliance leads to align on local experience quality, legal requirements, and proactive mitigation of market-specific risks, including producing monthly SLA reports for regulated entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent regional customers in global forums, ensuring roadmap discussions, launch planning, and issue prioritization reflect the needs of customers across all markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in program management within customer support operations, including hands-on work with technical product or ops integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to use quantitative analysis and regional data to prioritize issues, inform launch decisions, and measure CX outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of operating across multiple regulated markets (e.g., EMEA, APAC) with working knowledge of compliance requirements such as AML/KYC, vulnerable customer obligations, or financial services regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Compliance, and Operations teams to drive programs from planning through execution across multiple geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Base salary varies by location (see range below). Total compensation may also include equity and bonus eligibility, and benefits (medical, dental, vision, 401(k)).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual base salary range (excluding equity and bonus):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$108,630&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$108,630 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Application Limit: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Candidates may submit a maximum of 3 applications within a 6-month period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer: &lt;/strong&gt;Coinbase is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. Applicants with criminal histories will be considered consistent with applicable federal, state, and local laws.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Applicants: &lt;/strong&gt;View&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/WHD/legacy/files/eppac.pdf&quot;&gt; Employee Rights&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt; Know Your Rights&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://static-assets.coinbase.com/e-verify.pdf&quot;&gt; E-Verify&lt;/a&gt; Notice of Participation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations: &lt;/strong&gt;If you are an individual with a disability who needs a reasonable accommodation, email us your request and contact info at accommodations[at]coinbase.com.&amp;nbsp;Need screen reading technology?&lt;a href=&quot;https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/screen-reader/kgejglhpjiefppelpmljglcjbhoiplfn&quot;&gt; Click here&lt;/a&gt; to download a free compatible screen reader and view the&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.chromevox.com/tutorial/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;tutorial&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy &amp;amp; Arbitration: &lt;/strong&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/legal/applicant_privacy_notice&quot;&gt; Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. US applicants: By submitting your application, you agree to&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/legal/application-arbitration-agreement&quot;&gt; Arbitration of Disputes&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
