job-0xvdosr:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Securitize, the leader in tokenizing real-world assets with $3.7B+ AUM (as of May 5, 2025), is&amp;nbsp;bringing the world on-chain through tokenized funds in partnership with top-tier asset managers,&amp;nbsp;such as Apollo, BlackRock, Hamilton Lane, KKR, and others. Securitize, through its&amp;nbsp;subsidiaries, is a SEC-registered broker dealer, digital transfer agent, fund administrator, and&amp;nbsp;operator of a SEC-regulated Alternative Trading System (ATS).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Securitize is a global, fully remote team consisting of top talent from the blockchain and&amp;nbsp;financial services industries. Having raised $170M overall to date, we are backed by some of the&amp;nbsp;largest names in finance and technology, including BlackRock, Morgan Stanley, Blockchain&amp;nbsp;Capital, MUFG, Sumitomo Mitsui Trust Bank, Sony Finance, Banco Santander, Coinbase,&amp;nbsp;among others. Securitize has also been recognized as a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.forbes.com/lists/fintech50/&quot;&gt;2025 Forbes Top 50 Fintech&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before applying, we encourage you to visit us to learn more:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.securitize.io/&quot;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;|&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.x.com/Securitize&quot;&gt;X/Twitter&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;|&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/securitize&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Lead Brand Designer to work directly with our Creative Director as one of the core hands-on makers on the Marketing team. This is a foundational, high-impact individual contributor role for someone who can take conceptual direction, sharpen it, and carry it all the way through to exceptional execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help establish and evolve the Securitize brand across campaigns, events, social, editorial, presentations, partnerships, launches, and digital experiences. Because the team is intentionally lean, you will have real influence over both the work and the systems behind it: what we make, how we make it, and the quality bar we hold.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is first and foremost a brand design role. You will also partner closely with our website marketing manager, product design, and other digital partners to create a coherent experience across brand, web, and product. You will not be expected to own core product UX, but you should be comfortable shaping how the brand comes to life in digital products and collaborating with specialists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and evolve the brand. &lt;/strong&gt;Translate brand strategy and creative direction into a distinctive, flexible visual system that can grow with the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the creative bar. &lt;/strong&gt;Develop concepts and execute high-visibility work across integrated campaigns, events, launches, social, editorial, partnerships, presentations, and executive communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create systems, not just assets. &lt;/strong&gt;Build practical guidelines, Figma libraries, templates, and toolkits that make the brand easier to use without flattening the work into a formula.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connect brand, web, and product. &lt;/strong&gt;Design and prototype brand-led digital experiences, working with web, product design, product, and engineering partners to carry the trust, clarity, and distinctiveness of the brand into the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead through influence. &lt;/strong&gt;Present work clearly, explain the thinking behind it, navigate feedback, and build alignment with partners and senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct and elevate external partners. &lt;/strong&gt;Brief and art direct agencies, freelancers, illustrators, photographers, motion designers, and production partners when the work calls for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own work from ambiguity to delivery. &lt;/strong&gt;Frame the problem, identify what is missing, explore the right range of ideas, and carry the strongest direction through final production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve how the team works. &lt;/strong&gt;Help prioritize requests, scope projects, identify repeatable needs, and build a more deliberate and effective creative practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in brand, visual, or graphic design, with meaningful ownership of work at a senior level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that shows exceptional craft and strong ideas across identity systems and real-world applications - not just isolated campaign assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent typography, layout, composition, and visual storytelling skills, with the judgment to make complex information feel clear and compelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Figma, including components, auto layout, libraries, and prototyping, plus strong command of Adobe Creative Cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building or evolving a brand system and applying it across multiple channels, formats, and audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong conceptual thinking: you can generate distinctive directions, connect creative choices to a larger idea, and distinguish between work that is merely polished and work that is truly good.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital fluency, including responsive design, accessibility fundamentals, and the practical realities of designing work that will be built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work independently, manage multiple priorities, communicate directly, and make progress without a perfectly defined brief or constant oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with complex, technical, or regulated subject matter and turning it into experiences people can understand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for fintech, financial services, blockchain, digital assets, or another high-trust category.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful web, digital experience, or product design experience, even if it has not been the center of your role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with motion, 3D, illustration, photography, data visualization, or other disciplines that can expand a brand system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing event identities, environmental graphics, or high-impact physical brand moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working both in-house and at an agency, mentoring other designers, or providing creative direction without formal people-management authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Securitize has a clearer, more distinctive, and more consistently expressed brand across its highest-visibility touchpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The team has a practical visual system and reusable foundations that improve both quality and speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flagship campaigns, events, launches, and digital experiences establish a noticeably higher creative bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brand, web, and product experiences feel more connected, even when different teams deliver them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a trusted senior creative partner who can take an ambiguous challenge, make the work better, and move it forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The kind of person who will thrive here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are hands-on, curious, and comfortable moving between the big idea and the last five percent of craft. You care deeply about the work without becoming precious about your first answer. You know when a problem needs exploration, a system, or simply needs to ship. Most importantly, you do not wait for perfect conditions to make meaningful progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like you, we would like to hear from you - even if your background does not match every line above.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Become a part of our rapidly expanding organization and enjoy a supportive and rewarding work environment:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off – Promoting a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity Grant Opportunities&amp;nbsp;– Share in the success and future growth of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote Work Flexibility&amp;nbsp;– Work from anywhere while staying connected with a dynamic and collaborative team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Benefits for US employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive Insurance Coverage – Employer-paid Medical, Dental, and Vision benefits for you and your family.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) Retirement Plan – Secure your financial future with employer-sponsored savings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;231&quot; data-end=&quot;638&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Securitize is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and equitable workplace. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, marital or family status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;640&quot; data-end=&quot;830&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;All employment decisions at Securitize are based on job-related qualifications, merit, and business needs. We welcome candidates from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-1vnvapk:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sales Development Representative (SDR) at Stripe, you will drive Stripe’s future growth engine by working with Demand Gen and the Account Executive team to qualify leads and collaboratively build Stripe’s sales pipeline. You get excited about engaging with prospects to better qualify needs. You are adept at identifying high value opportunities and capable of managing early sales funnel activities.You are used to delivering value in complex situations and are energized by learning about new and existing products. Finally, you enjoy building – you like to actively participate in the development of the demand generation and sales process, the articulation of Stripe’s value proposition, and the creation of key tools and assets. If you’re hungry, smart, persistent, and a great teammate, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We take a data driven, analytical approach to sales development, and are looking for someone who is confident in both prospecting to customers and in helping design our strategy. If you’re hungry, smart, persistent, and a great teammate, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify high-potential businesses, verticals and markets, and develop and execute outbound strategies to bring them to Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow up with Marketing generated leads to qualify as sales opportunities. Move solid leads through the funnel connecting them to a salesperson, and arranging meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and lead campaigns from idea-generation through to qualified calls and determine how best to scale them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and codify best practices and sales workflows for scaled and bespoke interactions with prospects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate contact with potential customers through cold-calling or responding to inquiries generated from Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives to build strategy and prospect into designated accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships with prospects to uncover needs through effective questioning to qualify interest and viability to prepare hand-off to sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow-up with potential customers who expressed interest but did not initially result in a sales opportunity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively work through lead list meeting/exceeding SLAs, consistently update activity and contact information within the CRM system and support weekly reporting efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and provide feedback and insights to Marketing to help improve targeting and messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with customers to support their activation &amp;amp; deployment of Stripe services contracted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Hebrew and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of top performance or prior success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self starter who is able to operate in a hyper growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a high-growth tech company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-0yf57xu:
&lt;h4&gt;This is a customer-facing, technical pre-sales role — not a cloud/infrastructure architecture position.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Intro&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;M0 is the modular stablecoin infrastructure. It gives businesses everything they need to launch a stablecoin built around their product, with separate, configurable layers for application, distribution, and issuance. Choose your regulated issuer, with the option to switch them later. Design how your stablecoin behaves with templates and custom logic. Tap shared liquidity across the network from day one. Other stablecoin platforms bundle every layer into a single fixed stack. M0 keeps them independent, so your stablecoin stays yours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;M0 is seeking a Solutions Architect to serve as the technical voice in our sales process. You&#39;ll work alongside Account Executives to understand each prospect&#39;s architecture, articulate how M0&#39;s modular stack fits their needs, and own the technical narrative from active evaluation through close. Sitting at the intersection of Sales, Product, and Integrations Engineering, you&#39;ll know what to answer directly, when to bring in Product for roadmap and direction, and when to loop in Integrations Engineering to scope or unblock an implementation. The ideal candidate combines genuine technical depth with the communication skills to make complex infrastructure clear and credible to technical and non-technical buyers alike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join sales calls as the technical lead—running product deep-dives, whiteboarding architectures, and fielding detailed questions from prospects&#39; engineers, architects, and technical decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer requirements into a clear picture of how M0&#39;s application, distribution, and issuance layers fit their stack, and translate M0&#39;s capabilities into the customer&#39;s language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical discovery, demos, and proofs-of-concept, and scope integration work with the customer to move deals toward close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercise judgment on escalation—surfacing roadmap and product-fit questions to Product, and handing off implementation, scoping, and technical blockers to Integrations Engineering with clean, complete context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle technical objections and security, compliance, and architecture questions, and lead responses to RFPs and RFIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the feedback loop from the field to Product, bringing back patterns, gaps, and competitive signals that shape the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7 years in a customer-facing technical role—Solutions Architect, Solutions Engineer, Sales Engineer, Integrations/Implementation Engineer, or a developer who has moved toward go-to-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine technical depth: comfort reading API documentation, reasoning about system architecture and integrations, and holding your own with senior engineers. Hands-on coding experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling or implementing technical infrastructure, APIs, or developer-facing platforms; familiarity with stablecoins, crypto, payments, or fintech is a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to lead technical discovery and evaluations that result in closed business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication, including experience presenting to and building trust with technical and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Attributes:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically credible: You can go deep with engineers and architects, then zoom out and make the same system clear to a non-technical stakeholder—often in the same call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment: You know the difference between &quot;I&#39;ve got this,&quot; &quot;let&#39;s get Product on this roadmap question,&quot; and &quot;Integrations needs to scope this,&quot; and you route accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative communicator: You build strong relationships across Sales, Product, Integrations Engineering, and with customers&#39; technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery-focused: You keep the end goal—a technically sound, closed deal—in view and drive toward it without getting lost in distractions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive problem solver: You anticipate objections and technical blockers early and take decisive action to resolve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation (base salary with equity/token grant) commensurate with experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global team and flexibility: Join a truly global team with the flexibility to work remotely or from one of our hubs in NYC or Berlin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health and wellness: Enjoy comprehensive healthcare insurance coverage as well as a wellbeing allowance and gym membership to support your physical and mental health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customizable IT setup: Tailor your workspace with access to top-notch IT equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development: Benefit from an annual development budget to enhance your skills and grow professionally, including opportunities to participate in conferences and on-site company events worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

