job-1dkgx8r:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gemini is a global crypto and Web3 platform founded by Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss in 2014, offering a wide range of simple, reliable, and secure crypto products and services to individuals and institutions in over 70 countries. Our mission is to unlock the next era of financial, creative, and personal freedom by providing trusted access to the decentralized future. We envision a world where crypto reshapes the global financial system, internet, and money to create greater choice, independence, and opportunity for all — bridging traditional finance with the emerging cryptoeconomy in a way that is more open, fair, and secure. As a publicly traded company, Gemini is poised to accelerate this vision with greater scale, reach, and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Department: Institutional Sales&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Senior Principal, Institutional Sales&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gemini is seeking a highly experienced Institutional Sales &amp;amp; OTC Senior Principal to own and grow our institutional OTC and broader execution business. This individual will sit at the center of Gemini’s institutional revenue engine, responsible for driving OTC trading flow, expanding institutional relationships, and ensuring seamless execution across spot, derivatives, and structured flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is required to be in person twice a week at our New York City, NY office.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Originate, onboard, and grow institutional OTC relationships across hedge funds, prop trading firms, asset managers, family offices, and crypto-native institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive spot, derivatives, and structured flow through Gemini’s OTC platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high-touch coverage of key institutional clients, providing market color, trade ideas, and risk-aware execution strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Trading to improve spreads, liquidity depth, and overall execution quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop new institutional revenue opportunities across OTC, custody, staking, and derivatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and expand strategic partnerships across funds, intermediaries, fintechs, and crypto-native ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Gemini in institutional sales cycles, client engagements, and industry conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture and synthesize client feedback to inform Trading and Product improvements across execution and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and help shape institutional go-to-market strategy across OTC and adjacent product lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in institutional sales, OTC trading, or execution roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of generating meaningful institutional trading volume and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep existing relationships across hedge funds, prop trading firms, family offices, asset managers, and crypto-native institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of OTC market structure, liquidity dynamics, derivatives, and execution workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across traditional markets (FX, equities, commodities, fixed income) and/or digital assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with institutional onboarding, DDQs, and regulated financial environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and negotiation skills with senior institutional counterparts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial mindset with ability to operate in a fast-paced, high-accountability environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree required; advanced degree a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;It Pays to Work Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;The compensation &amp;amp; benefits package for this role includes:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive starting pay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive commission-based bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Long-term incentive in the form of a new hire equity grant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Comprehensive health plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;401K with company matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range&lt;/strong&gt;: The base salary for this role is $200,000 in the State of New York. In addition to the base salary, this role is eligible for our competitive bonus commission plan, including a direct percentage commission payout based on revenue generated from covered clients. The base salary is also not inclusive of our equity package. When determining a candidate’s compensation, we consider a number of factors including skillset, experience, job scope, and current market data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the United States, we offer a hybrid work approach at our hub offices, balancing the benefits of in-person collaboration with the flexibility of remote work. Expectations may vary by location and role, so candidates are encouraged to connect with their recruiter to learn more about the specific policy for the role. Employees who do not live near one of our hubs are part of our remote workforce. All employees, however, are required to onboard in-person at one of our office locations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Gemini, we strive to build diverse teams that reflect the people we want to empower through our products, and we are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, or Veteran status. Equal Opportunity is the Law, and Gemini is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. If you have a specific need that requires accommodation, please let a member of the People Team know.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-MW1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

job-0wlo65p:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Design team defines and delivers user-facing experiences across Stripe. Product Designers work closely with engineers, product managers, researchers, strategists, operations, data scientists, and marketers to shape products from early strategy through launch and iteration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the Risk team, where design shapes how businesses get started on Stripe, stay compliant, and grow with confidence. Stripe&#39;s ability to innovate, expand globally, and serve the world&#39;s most ambitious companies depends on world-class risk management. But great risk management requires clear, trustworthy, and surprisingly well-crafted experiences during some of the most important moments in a user&#39;s relationship with Stripe. From onboarding and verification to account health, your work will help users understand what&#39;s happening, know what to do next, and feel confident that Stripe is growing with them as a trusted partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risk at Stripe is also evolving into a product pillar in its own right. As Stripe builds more modular, configurable, API-first risk capabilities, we have the opportunity to turn internal strength into external products for some of the largest and most innovative companies in the world to leverage. This role will shape that future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of building trust in the internet economy, platform design, and new product creation, making it one of the most strategically important design opportunities at Stripe. You&#39;ll lead design across critical Risk experiences, shaping the strategy for new products, defining AI-driven and agent-friendly workflows, and setting design standards for the team. It&#39;s a strong fit for a designer who is energized by ambiguity, motivated by impact, and excited to shape the future of how businesses get started and grow on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the future of Risk at Stripe, from core user journeys to entirely new product surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design experiences that help users onboard quickly, stay compliant, and manage risk with clarity and control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, engineering, policy, operations, and research to define both near-term improvements and longer-term opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the craft bar in a domain where quality and trust matter deeply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across dozens of teams to create beautiful patterns for risk and compliance experiences across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore, shape, and prototype new ideas and products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence strategy through strong product thinking, storytelling, and design judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design on complex, cross-functional problems with multiple stakeholders and constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across the Risk team and the wider Stripe design team to influence the shape and visual standards for all product surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help other Risk designers and cross-functional partners raise the bar on craft, and adopt systems thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience designing products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio demonstrating excellent craft, systems thinking, and end-to-end design, including a strong understanding of AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex product work in close partnership with product management and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping ambiguous spaces and driving clarity through design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of influencing cross-functional teams and product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in environments where the opportunity spans systems, strategy, and 0-1 product thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy turning complex systems, policies, and edge cases into elegant product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are energized by ambiguous, strategic problem spaces—not just well-defined execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are an influential storyteller who can align partners around a clear point of view&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can move fluidly between big-picture thinking and interaction-level craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know how to build trust through design, especially in high-stakes or sensitive user moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work well across disciplines and build credibility with technical, operational, and policy-oriented partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-07jumwo:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mesh&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, our mission is to enable consumers to pay and be paid with any asset. Today, trillions of dollars in tokenized assets exist but remain largely unusable for everyday commerce. Mesh is bridging this gap by making crypto payments reliable, useful, and ubiquitous. We combine a powerful orchestration engine with a seamless consumer app to unlock liquidity for the world. Backed by leading investors like PayPal Ventures, Paradigm, and Galaxy Ventures, we are building the infrastructure for the next era of the global economy. Join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Solutions Engineer, you will be instrumental in executing our pre-sales customer lifecycle. You’ll be working closely with our support engineering and product teams while serving as the technical bridge between customers and our internal teams. While Sales owns the account and commercial relationships, you&#39;ll become an expert in our demos, API’s, SDKs, best practices, implementation and lessons learned that enable successful customers and long-term self-service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside our Solutions Architects and Product to create industry-specific playbooks, mentor customer engineering teams, share best practices, and develop innovative solutions that accelerate sales and implementation timelines across our diverse customer base including Payment Service Providers, iGaming, Wallets, Exchanges, Trad-fi and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as solutions/sales engineer, building strong customer relationships and trust with prospect and customers to drive rapid implementation and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement solutions for pre-sales, including analytics, processes, documentation, and technical infrastructure that accelerate sales and implementation timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize tools and data from Gong, Pylon, Kapa, Datadog, Amplitude, and AI-powered self-service solutions to enhance internal workflows, improve ease of closing deals, handling customer objections/questions, and elevate customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide customer business and technical teams on SDK and API implementation best practices to significantly reduce timelines and facilitate broader platform rollouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage and resolve technical issues between prospects/customers and internal&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel occasionally (approximately once monthly) for strategic customers, company meetings, or industry events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Data, or equivalent work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-5 years of experience as a sales/solution engineer, solutions architect, support engineer or equivalent, ideally with some experience in a startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as an early stage team member or early team builder is highly valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to build and maintain customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated technical knowledge, use and troubleshooting skills with APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with API management tools, SDK’s, and demo software like Coast is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of crypto and fintech, including blockchain technology, digital assets, financial regulations, and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical skills: Coding, API/SDK, and AI (Claude/Codex), /automation experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The compensation range provided may span multiple career levels and will be narrowed during the interview process based on factors including a candidate&#39;s experience, skills, qualifications, and geographic location. For candidates outside of New York or San Francisco, compensation will be adjusted to reflect the applicable market and location-based pay band. The base salary range listed excludes commission (if applicable), equity, and benefits. The pay range represents the minimum and maximum target for new-hire compensation. Actual compensation may vary and may be higher or lower depending on individual circumstances.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$180,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love It Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, you&#39;re not stepping into a typical role—you&#39;re joining a rocket ship in mid-liftoff. You&#39;ll tackle complex, meaningful problems that actually move an industry forward, working alongside a sharp, motivated team that moves quickly, collaborates deeply, and expects everyone to operate with ownership. This is the kind of place where you&#39;ll see your work ship fast, make real impact, and be able to point to something and say, &quot;I built that.&quot; You&#39;ll grow fast, level up your skills, and get a front-row seat to how a high-growth company scales from the inside, with competitive comp, solid benefits, and room to stretch your craft all coming standard. If you&#39;re energized by building, learning, and shaping something big—this is where you&#39;ll want to be.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Office Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees based in our &lt;strong&gt;San Francisco, New York, and Bangalore&lt;/strong&gt; hubs are expected to work from the office at least 40% of the time (approximately two days per week). This expectation may vary slightly depending on role, team, and business needs. Certain roles that require closer cross-functional collaboration or operational support may have additional in-office requirements, which will be discussed during the interview process. Our hybrid approach is designed to balance meaningful in-person collaboration, team building, and real-time decision-making with the flexibility to work remotely. We believe this structure supports strong execution while preserving autonomy and focus time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Care For Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe great work happens when people feel valued and supported. That starts with competitive salary and equity that grows as you and the company grow, plus comprehensive health coverage for you and your family. We offer unlimited PTO—and we mean it. Take the time you need to recharge and show up at your best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re invested in your growth with a dedicated budget for courses, conferences, and certifications. Work from wherever you&#39;re most productive with our remote-friendly approach, and count on having the top-tier tools and equipment you need to do exceptional work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh Pay is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, genetic information, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, lawful alien status, national origin, age, marital status, and non-job related physical or mental disability, or protected veteran status. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-14sq7o5:
&lt;p&gt;At Shakepay, we’re on a mission to usher in the Bitcoin golden age. We’re reimagining financial services to give every Canadian their fair shake.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our culture is built around doing work that matters, winning as a team, and celebrating success. If you&#39;re the kind of person who values growth, shipping fast, and sharing your ideas openly with a group of like-minded people, come and build with us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Shakepay&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since 2015, we&#39;ve been on a mission to help Canadians build long-term wealth through bitcoin. Over the past few years, we&#39;ve expanded beyond buying and selling bitcoin to offer a growing suite of everyday financial products - including the Shakepay Card, direct deposit, bill payments and Interac e-Transfer - making it easier to earn, save and use bitcoin every day. Today, more than 1.5 million Canadians use Shakepay to grow their bitcoin savings and take control of their financial future as we continue to push the boundaries of what modern financial services can look like.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re regulated as an investment dealer across all Canadian provinces and territories, and backed by renowned venture capitalists with a funding of $44M. We have a passionate, loyal, and growing community, and we’re looking for people who want to help us build something truly special.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Legal team sits at the center of some of Shakepay’s most important decisions. We partner closely with Product, Compliance, Operations, Finance, People, and leadership to bring new products to market, navigate complex regulatory questions and help the business move quickly with confidence. We believe ownership over hierarchy, practical judgment over perfection, and using technology and AI to rethink how legal work gets done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Legal Counsel, you’ll help shape how millions of Canadians interact with money. You’ll work alongside product, compliance and executive leadership to solve novel legal questions at the intersection of crypto, payments and financial regulation. This is a hands-on role for someone who can navigate ambiguity, provide practical recommendations and wants to help build - not just protect - the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Compliance and business teams to help design and launch new products, translating complex legal and regulatory requirements into practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on a broad range of legal and regulatory matters across securities, AML/ATF, payments, consumer protection and other areas impacting Shakepay&#39;s business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regulatory initiatives, including supporting examinations, audits, licensing work, policy development and engagement with regulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide practical, business-oriented advice to leaders across the company, helping teams navigate ambiguity and make informed decisions while balancing legal, regulatory and operational considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to leverage AI, automation and scalable processes to improve how legal work gets done and enable the business to move faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the team on a variety of other legal matters as needed, including commercial agreements, corporate governance, employment and strategic projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who we’re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Canadian-qualified lawyer with 5+ years of experience, ideally in fintech, payments, financial services, crypto, or a fast-moving technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to operate independently in a lean team, make decisions with incomplete information, and move work forward without heavy oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-oriented legal judgment: you start from the product or business outcome, then help the team understand risk, options, and a recommended path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable advising product and operational teams directly, including on ambiguous questions where there may not be a perfect answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to turn complex legal issues into clear, practical guidance for non-legal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus points&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across both a law firm and an in-house legal team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a startup or scaleup environment where priorities change quickly and legal support needs to be pragmatic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Bitcoin, crypto, securities, payments, AML, or regulated financial products in Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI, automation, or lightweight tooling to improve legal work product and team efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why join us?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the future of money: Be part of a team that&#39;s revolutionizing financial services in Canada, one sat at a time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impact millions: As cryptocurrency continues to gain traction, our potential for growth is massive. You can help us bring Shakepay and Bitcoin to all Canadians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow your career: We’re growing, and so can you! We have programs in place to encourage continuous learning, growth, and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideas, not titles: We want the best ideas to make their way through, no matter where they come from.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Perks and benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🤝 Be an owner: Every employee has stock options as part of their total compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🥅 Reach your goals: Develop with continuous feedback and quarterly performance and compensation review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🦷 Health &amp;amp; wellness: Access to health and dental coverage, including health and wellness spending accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌎 Remote-friendly: Work from anywhere in Canada, with optional access to our office spaces in Montreal and Toronto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🆙 Level Up: A $2,000 annual budget for courses, certifications, and training to support your career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌴 Time off: 20 days of vacation per year. And if you use all your vacation, we give you a $1,000 bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🐣 Parental leave: Enjoy a parental leave top up to 100% of your salary for 18 weeks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🙌 Have fun together: quarterly team-specific or company-wide offsite to connect with each other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this position is 150,000 - 220,000 CAD. Base pay may vary based on factors such as years of experience, skills and qualifications. Additionally, employees are eligible for equity, pay increases based on performance, benefits including health and dental care, and paid time off.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We understand that potential can be just as valuable as experience. If you&#39;re eager to learn, grow, and contribute to the mission but worry that you may not have the “right” experience, we still want you to apply. We encourage applications from everyone, regardless of background and life experience. We’re firm believers that a little bit of slope makes up for a lot of y-intercept.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use technology, including artificial intelligence (AI), to support certain parts of our hiring process. This can include tools that assist with scheduling, application review, candidate communications, and generating interview notes, guides, or summaries so our team can stay focused on the conversation. All hiring decisions are made by our hiring team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fluency in English is required due to the percentage of English-speaking customers and the nature of our platform, which is available to all Canadians.&lt;/p&gt;

job-01uqk0n:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW161772177 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW161772177 BCX0&quot;&gt;Flow Traders is looking for a Staff Engineer to join us in our Amsterdam office. This is a unique opportunity to join a leading proprietary trading firm with an entrepreneurial and innovative culture at the heart of its business. We value quick-witted, creative minds and challenge them to make full use of their capacities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are looking for a senior individual contributor to lead the architectural and technical direction for our Trading Automation and Backend Engineering teams. Operating across the full trade lifecycle (pre-trade, execution, and post-trade), you will bridge the gap between engineering, trading, and operations. As a Staff Engineer, you will tackle ambiguous, large-scale problems, set global engineering standards, and scale your impact by mentoring tech leads and engineers across multiple teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP Selected SCXW161772177 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you will do:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW210372668 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW210372668 BCX0&quot;&gt;Strategic Architecture &amp;amp; Vision&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP Selected SCXW210372668 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;Define and own the long-term technical architecture for our trading automation, risk, and post-trade platforms.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Translate complex, ambiguous business problems into clear, executable technical roadmaps.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Architect scalable, event-driven systems optimized for high throughput, data integrity, and reliability.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;Engineering Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate engineering standards across the organization, focusing on system design, observability, reliability, and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an IC multiplier: mentor senior engineers, guide tech leads, and drive technical alignment across fragmented systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead efforts to responsibly decommission legacy systems in favor of modern, scalable services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business &amp;amp; Operational Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with trading, quant, risk, and operations teams to align technical choices with business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive automation in post-trade and middle-office workflows (allocations, settlements, reconciliations) to drastically reduce operational risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you need to succeed&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience, with a proven track record operating at a Staff, Principal, or cross-team Lead level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence senior technical and business stakeholders and drive consensus across multiple teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in building distributed, high-performance, and highly reliable backend systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in at least one (or more) core backend language (Python, Go, C++, or Java).Experience with event-driven architectures (e.g., Kafka, Flink, Databricks, Dataproc) and data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of modern infrastructure, observability, and cloud platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of specific financial workflows (ETF creation/redemption, clearing, custody).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial reference data, symbology, or instrument modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulatory frameworks (MiFID II, EMIR, SFTR) and their data lineage requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid background in financial services, trading, or market making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of the trading lifecycle (order flow, execution, and post-trade/settlement flows).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we offer&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flow Traders, we create the conditions for hard‑working, high‑performing people to do their best work. From a thorough onboarding and ongoing access to Flow Academy, to latest technology and a collaborative, non‑hierarchical culture, we give you the tools, ownership, and support to move fast and drive outcomes. We keep a close‑knit, small‑company feel while offering competitive salary, annual discretionary profit share, and comprehensive benefits,&amp;nbsp;so talent can grow here, and stay here.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;See our benefits below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flow Academy and opportunities to attend domain-related conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily catered lunch, great coffee, and a fully stocked kitchen and snack bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house Bar and Lounge with arcade, table tennis, billiards, and game consoles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company boat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house gym and sessions with our nutritionist or personal trainer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bi-weekly massages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual company trip and a variety of events throughout the year, such as the New Years Event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global rotations across our offices worldwide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;and more
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: Montserrat; font-size: 10.0pt; color: #242424;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
