job-0fe8iun:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div data-page-id=&quot;HladdPLXIoNz4nxkqkCuk4rAs8v&quot; data-lark-html-role=&quot;root&quot; data-docx-has-block-data=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-XCikdRR2xoZIjdxtCKcuOflrs8d&quot;&gt;Established in 2018, Bybit is one of the world’s leading cryptocurrency exchanges and digital financial platforms, serving over 80 million users across more than 200 countries and regions. Powered by world-class technology and a user-first mindset, Bybit delivers a seamless ecosystem across trading, payments, wealth management, custody, institutional services, and Web3 — connecting users to the future of digital finance.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-IF06dI0MPoBwYfxbZ4zui13HsoC&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-X5EbdOwvMoYuOmxQBbuueUEDsDd&quot;&gt;Our core values define how we build. We listen, care and improve to create products and experiences that put users first. Backed by a global team of ambitious builders, problem-solvers, and innovators, we foster a high-performance and fast-moving environment where talent is empowered to drive real impact at the global scale. Supported by 24/7 multilingual customer service and a strong commitment to innovation, we are shaping the future of finance through technology, collaboration, and bold execution.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-LtVud2dO7oglqJxxZoOucqjJsPc&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-RMHkdm4bPo66l3xMVO8ui1o8sle&quot;&gt;Today, Bybit is recognized as one of the most trusted and transparent platforms in the digital asset industry, continuing to expand its global presence while building the infrastructure for the next generation of financial services.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support risk operations by conducting campaign reviews, activity data quality checks, case reviews, and user behaviour analysis based on operational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform in-depth analysis combining internal and external data to provide actionable insights supporting operational decisions, strategy development, and model iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously monitor data, define risk indicators, optimise workflows, and establish a standardised risk operations framework to improve operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong cross-functional relationships with Marketing, Operations, Customer Service and other teams to ensure smooth execution of campaigns and risk control strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or above; 2+ years of experience in data analysis or data operations, with exposure to at least one of the following: business risk control, marketing anti-fraud, account security, or fund security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in SQL with the ability to conduct independent data analysis; experience with R or Python is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and risk intuition, with solid logical thinking and data sensitivity — candidates should be able to identify risks from anomalous data and articulate the underlying causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in spoken Mandarine is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Bybit, we are committed to fostering a supportive and enriching work environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;br&gt;- Study Growth Fund: We support your professional development and continuous learning.&lt;br&gt;- Internal Events: Participate in regular team-building activities, workshops, and events designed to promote collaboration and innovation.&lt;br&gt;- Global Collaboration: Be part of a diverse, international team, working alongside colleagues from around the world.&lt;br&gt;- Career Advancement: Access opportunities for growth and advancement within a rapidly expanding global company.&lt;br&gt;- Internal Mobility: Grow with us- Your long-term development is important to us. We offer internal job opportunities to help build your career path.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-19980gt:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, Finance will be involved in all aspects of local and global operations and will support critical initiatives to facilitate the expansion of the company’s financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the International Controller, you will be immersed in all aspects of our operations, working closely with internal and external partners at all levels. Problem solvers are welcome, especially those with commercial acumen. You will play a vital role in recommending solutions and driving strategic decision-making processes. Your organizational skills will be key in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a genuine curiosity about emerging payment technology and the blockchain industry, you will be at the forefront of innovation, fueling the expansion of our financial infrastructure and contribute to the future of our finance team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial controllership&lt;/strong&gt; - Responsible for the delivery of all Brazilian &amp;amp; Bacen GAAP reporting including implementing accounting processes related to month-end, quarter-end, and year-end close including P&amp;amp;L, Balance Sheet, variance analysis, and management reports, including legacy businesses. This will include ensuring data integrity of the ledger, working with operations and other teams to ensure timely receipt of trading and operational data to prepare financial records and other returns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate (and explain)&lt;/strong&gt; local requirements into Group actionable deliverables, being the bridge between finance, and local providers (auditors, banking providers, tax authorities and others).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preparation and coordination of:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statutory and regulatory audits&lt;/strong&gt; - are completed and filed on / ahead of time, including managing / co-ordinating external audit teams efforts effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial regulatory filings&lt;/strong&gt; – Ensure financial data / components of financial requests are completed on time ensure sufficient granularity that is repeatable on a regular basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prepare financial updates&lt;/strong&gt; - to external trading partners and investors as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial management reporting (departmental reporting)&lt;/strong&gt; – ensure Exco members have sufficient operating / expense cost date for them and their teams and work with the Head of FP&amp;amp;A to follow up on action items&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation&lt;/strong&gt; – help document policies, procedures and ensure best practice for expansion of the department and to provide for contingency / global handover between teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outsourced Partners&lt;/strong&gt; - Work with outsourced partners on a timely basis to provide financial and other information to enable financial support and assistance to be completed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Treasury and Liquidity Management&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Reporting&lt;/strong&gt; – Assist the Head of Treasury and Capital Management report capital and liquidity positions and ongoing reporting requirements in conjunction with senior management. This requires the firm has sufficient liquidity to meet the ongoing needs for Operating, Trading (aka Risk capital) and Regulatory capital requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk framework&lt;/strong&gt; – help monitor the Finance risk requirements for the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial forecasting&lt;/strong&gt; – assist with financial modelling the operating businesses and the impact on the wider group, including leveraging new tools and best practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assist with assessing the financial and reporting impact - &lt;/strong&gt;of new Products and markets / entities, including advising on pricing and other analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assist in the development of Management Information&lt;/strong&gt; – Help create and set up new timely and accurate financial reporting to monitor the current and future needs of the business;&lt;/li&gt;
