job-1o37e0i:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sr. Sales Engineer at Alpaca, you will be the go-to expert for all products and services offered to our partners. Your role is to leverage your technical skills, excellent communication, and creative problem-solving abilities to support the sales process for Alpaca&#39;s growing suite of products and services. You will focus on expanding our base of enterprise partners within your assigned territory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Things you get to do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the product and technical subject matter expert, capable of thoroughly understanding and articulating all aspects of the Alpaca platform to diverse audiences and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a regional market-specific expert in regulations, compliance, and jurisdictional requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with senior leaders and C-level executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the Sales and Customer Success teams, providing essential technical advisory and product expertise throughout the client lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present compelling product and technical use cases to prospective clients, while building trust and confidence in Alpaca&#39;s technical capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex business and technical requirements into clear, simple solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create sales support materials and documentation for new features and products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical sales engagement end-to-end: discovery calls, solution validation, RFPs, and questionnaires that win deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead demo strategy and execution, creating technical narratives that convert prospects into customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel as needed to support sales activities and customer engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay updated on internal product development timelines and work closely with the product team to test and roll out new features to partners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are (must-haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited by the prospect of working in a startup environment, the ideal candidate is a self-starter who will take the lead in defining new processes where appropriate&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a Sales Engineering, Solutions Engineering, Technical consulting, Technical Product Management or Partner Engineering client-facing role, with experience working at API or SaaS-first companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background, including hands-on experience working with APIs, WebSockets, Postman, Grafana and JSON&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with FIX eXchange protocol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial services / fintech / brokerage exposure: trading lifecycle, settlements, regulatory awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills in English are essential for driving clarity on goals, setting expectations, and effectively collecting feedback from clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must be able to translate complex technical concepts into simple, understandable terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple assignments simultaneously, work independently and drive projects to completion with minimum guidance and close attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional or business-level fluency in spoken and written Korean&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be a rockstar 🤩, if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working at a Broker-Dealer or FinTech company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Closing &lt;strong&gt;Enterprise&lt;/strong&gt; deals alongside AEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Securities Industry Essentials (SIE) and or Series 7&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Metabase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience or familiarity with Bloomberg tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Coast (demo software)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited to learn more about the securities industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with OpenAPI, ReadMe and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

job-1j2qkoy:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h1 class=&quot;section-header section-header--large font-primary&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;About Digital Asset &amp;amp; the Canton Network&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Digital Asset builds the technologies that are reshaping the foundations of financial markets. Our mission is to create the world’s most trusted, privacy-enabled, and interoperable digital infrastructure for global finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of this mission is the Canton Network - the blockchain purpose-built for institutional finance. Uniquely combining privacy, compliance, and scalability, Canton enables real-time, secure settlement across multiple asset classes. Governed by the Canton Foundation with participation from leading financial institutions, it is the proven link between the promise of blockchain and the power of global finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2014 and headquartered in New York City, with offices in London, Zurich, Budapest, Hong Kong, and Sydney— we are on a mission to transform finance— and that transformation is now playing out rapidly on the Canton Network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you’re interested in playing a crucial role at the intersection of traditional and crypto-capital markets and want to help bring the next trillion dollars of finance on-chain, join us.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The SDK team designs, builds, and maintains the APIs, libraries, and tools that empower third-party developers. The resources we provide, facilitate the creation of applications that interact with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.daml.com/canton/about.html&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Canton ledger&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.canton.network/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Canton Network&lt;/a&gt;. The solutions developed using our product are predominantly mission-critical workflows within the financial and insurance sectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a software engineer in the SDK team, you&#39;ll have the unique opportunity to work with cutting-edge technology that spans the entire stack. This includes everything from the database back-end and Pekko Stream implementation, through gRPC and HTTP interfaces, to the Java and TypeScript client libraries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to the SDK’s (mostly) Scala code base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other teams such as the Canton Ledger team on the integration of APIs in the Canton core or the product team on developer education.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hardening and testing the APIs to satisfy the production non-functional requirements in particular performance, scalability, and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist other team members by providing code reviews, giving feedback and helping set direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Following a collaborative approach that fosters, embraces, and insists upon diverse perspectives. We are a powerful team where everyone pulls more than their weight, where everyone matters and all opinions are valuable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced Scala software engineer as demonstrated by either your open-source libraries or commercial experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specializing in either database development or writing secure APIs (more details below)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced with reactive streams (in particular akka/pekko) would be a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong oral and written communication skills, ideally experience writing technical documentation and specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with developing and deploying production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree or PhD in computer science or a related discipline; or equivalent demonstrable experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in Budapest or Zurich&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specializing in database development&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solid understanding of SQL and relational databases. In particular PostgreSQL.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Functional Relational Mappings in scala: slick, anorm, doobie or others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specializing in writing secure APIs&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solid understanding of network protocols and libraries: HTTP, gRPC, Netty, Tapir and others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience driven ability to empathize with API users allowing them to write efficient, robust and idiomatic client code in various front end languages such as TS and Python.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experienced with writing secure APIs. Familiarity with the technologies such as TLS, JWT, Auth0. Knowledge of frequent attack vectors and their mitigation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior exposure to security audit procedures would be a strong plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
