job-1wj8l1c:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Figure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Figure (NASDAQ: FIGR) is transforming capital markets through blockchain. We’re proving that blockchain isn’t just theory - it’s powering real products used by hundreds of thousands of consumers and institutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By combining blockchain’s transparency and efficiency with AI-driven automation, we’ve reimagined how loans are originated, funded, and traded in secondary markets. From faster processing times to lower costs and reduced bias, our technology is helping borrowers, investors, and financial institutions achieve better outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together with our 170+ partners, we’ve originated over $22 billion in home equity loans (HELOCs) on our blockchain-native platform, making Figure the largest non-bank provider of home equity financing in the U.S. Figure’s ecosystem also includes YLDS, an SEC-registered yield-bearing stablecoin that operates as a tokenized money market fund, and several other products and platforms that are reshaping consumer finance and capital markets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be recognized as one of &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.forbes.com/lists/fintech50/&quot;&gt;Forbes’ Most Innovative Fintech Startups in 2025&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fastcompany.com/91269557/finance-personal-finance-most-innovative-companies-2025&quot;&gt;Fast Company’s Most Innovative Companies in Finance and Personal Finance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Figure is looking for a highly experienced and detail-oriented Senior Manager of SEC Reporting with an eye for accuracy and a passion for cutting edge technology in the financial services industry. This role will be responsible for leading our financial reporting efforts, ensuring compliance with US GAAP and SEC regulations, and contributing to the overall success of our Controllership. Ownership and pride in your work are key to being a part of a team that is changing the financial services industry. This is a great opportunity to work at a rapidly growing company in a pivotal stage alongside some of the brightest minds and experienced leaders in the Fintech space.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll play a critical role in leading our SEC and financial reporting function as we scale. This role blends deep technical expertise with cross-functional collaboration, offering visibility across leadership and the opportunity to influence process improvements as we grow. You will report to the Director of Technical Accounting and SEC Reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SEC &amp;amp; Financial Reporting:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the preparation and timely filing of SEC reports, including 10-Ks, 10-Qs, 8-Ks, proxy statements and other required filings, ensuring compliance with US GAAP, SEC regulations, and XBRL tagging.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare or review supporting schedules for financial statements, footnotes, and MD&amp;amp;A sections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare disclosure checklists and tie-out documentation for SEC filings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the reporting calendar and ensure timely execution of deliverables to meet deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the review process with legal, external auditors, and internal stakeholders to ensure accuracy and alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the end-to-end accounting, valuation, and financial disclosures for stock-based compensation (ASC 718), including calculating monthly/quarterly expense, tracking equity grant activity, performing diluted EPS computations, and drafting footnote disclosures for Form 10-Q and 10-K filings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement across the reporting function: streamlining processes, simplifying disclosures, and implementing best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish and maintain SOX-compliant internal controls over financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in preparing internal management and investor reports, as well as materials for the Audit Committee.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support regulator inquiries and information requests, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze financial data to identify trends, anomalies, or areas of risk and improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with executive leadership, legal, investor relations, and auditors to deliver high-quality reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote a culture of learning, ownership, and operational excellence within the controllership team and broader finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Accounting &amp;amp; Strategic Projects:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and assess new accounting standards and SEC requirements, translating complex guidance into practical application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical accounting guidance to finance and cross-functional teams as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad-hoc financial reporting initiatives and other strategic projects as the company scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Background:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance or a related field; active CPA required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of progressive accounting experience, including at least 2–3 years in a leadership or managerial role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience in SEC reporting (Regs S-X and S-K), including ownership of 10-Ks/10-Qs and financial statement preparation in a public company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in US GAAP, SEC regulations, and financial reporting best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mix of public company and Big 4 experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fintech, tech, or high-growth industry experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Workiva (required) and NetSuite (preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public company reporting experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to all company security policies and data handling procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete mandatory security awareness training within required timeframes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promptly report any suspected security incidents or suspicious activity to the Security team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How You Work:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, confident communicator; able to synthesize technical information for executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with excellent project management skills and a continuous improvement mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resourceful, curious, and proactive; driven to take ownership and grow within a scaling organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient, optimistic, and energized by challenge and change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High integrity and strong ethical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Precision-focused with strong attention to detail and awareness of the bigger picture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to lead through ambiguity, work independently, and coordinate across teams and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Base Compensation Range: $140,250-$189,750/yr&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;25% annual bonus target, paid quarterly&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Company equity in the form of RSUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the compensation range for the role in the United States. Actual compensation may vary based on a candidate’s experience, skills, location, internal equity, and evolving business needs. While most offers are generally made within the middle of the range, final compensation is determined based on the factors above.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, with 100% employer-paid premiums for employees and their dependents on select plans&lt;br data-start=&quot;2866&quot; data-end=&quot;2869&quot;&gt;Company HSA, FSA, Dependent Care FSA, 401(k), and commuter benefits&lt;br data-start=&quot;2936&quot; data-end=&quot;2939&quot;&gt;Employer-paid life and disability insurance&lt;br data-start=&quot;2982&quot; data-end=&quot;2985&quot;&gt;11 observed holidays and PTO plan&lt;br data-start=&quot;3018&quot; data-end=&quot;3021&quot;&gt;Up to 12 weeks of paid family leave&lt;br data-start=&quot;3056&quot; data-end=&quot;3059&quot;&gt;Continuing education reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on your residential location certain laws might regulate the way Figure manages applicant data. California Residents, please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.figure.com/ca-employee-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;California Employee&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.figure.com/workforce-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;General Workforce Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for further information.&amp;nbsp;By submitting your application, you are agreeing&amp;nbsp; and&amp;nbsp;acknowledging&amp;nbsp;that you have read and understand the above notice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Figure will not sponsor work visas for this position. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-MM1 #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;

job-1ylxob6:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The GTM Product Marketing team sits within Stripe&#39;s Product Marketing org. We make sure Stripe sellers walk into every conversation prepared, confident, and armed with the right story. As Stripe&#39;s center of excellence for general product enablement, we set the standard for how sellers learn and pitch our products, drive consistency across product suites, and act as Marketing&#39;s Voice of the Field — surfacing seller insights to sharpen upstream messaging and positioning. We translate product value into seller-ready narratives, resources, and enablement — and we measure our impact on seller confidence and how effectively our teams pitch, qualify, and close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Commerce Experiences products (Optimized Checkout Suite, Link, Terminal, Agentic Commerce) help businesses convert more customers across every channel — from online checkout, to digital wallets, to in-person commerce, to the emerging world of AI-driven shopping. We&#39;re looking for an exceptional GTM product marketer to bring Stripe&#39;s story to market. In this role, you&#39;ll be the connective tissue between product, marketing, and the field. You&#39;ll translate complex commerce and checkout capabilities into compelling narratives and seller resources that resonate with our users and drive adoption. You&#39;ll equip customer-facing teams to confidently pitch all our solutions, answer technical questions, and speak to the roadmap. You&#39;ll also elevate seller and field insights to refine product positioning and messaging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the GTM PMM for Commerce Experiences, you’ll need to quickly build a deep understanding of Stripe’s Commerce Experiences products, buyer personas, and differentiation. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the content development and GTM enablement strategy across the sold funnel — creating seller-ready resources (pitch decks, FAQs, value props, talking points) that translate product positioning into clear, differentiated customer value propositions for enterprise, mid-market, and platform buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Market Intelligence to monitor and understand commerce, checkout, and emerging agentic commerce market trends, competitive dynamics, and seller-facing competitive narratives — synthesize insights, and leverage these to build differentiated positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver training programs that build seller expertise across the Commerce Experiences portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare sellers for major product launch events like Stripe Sessions, and to understand the details of the roadmap product is building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data and insights to identify enablement and knowledge gaps, prioritize asset development, launch new content, and measure effectiveness on seller confidence and other KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface field insights on a regular cadence — through monthly readouts and structured retros — to inform core PMM positioning and product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of product marketing experience, preferably in B2B tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with checkout, ecommerce, digital wallets, agentic commerce or other commerce platforms is strongly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Enterprise sales cycles and technical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation abilities, with a proven track record of distilling complex strategies into clear, compelling narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to move quickly without compromising attention to detail or polish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who thrives in fast-paced, ambiguous environments and can manage multiple priorities simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with data-driven decision making and measuring marketing impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with stakeholders across Product, Sales, and Marketing, and contribute to alignment on shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated comfort working with, and presenting to, senior leaders across a variety of disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills, a tendency to seek and share alternative views, and an ability to earn stakeholder confidence&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using or building AI-powered tooling to accelerate seller productivity or content development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

job-1tj5ujz:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;This role offers a unique opportunity to shape the financial strategy of a leading regional fintech. Reporting to the Chief of Staff, you will own the FP&amp;amp;A engine across multiple markets, products, and entities, with your analyses directly informing strategic decisions across new products, partnerships, and markets. This is not a reporting-coordination role: on the processes you own, your judgment is the deliverable. We are looking for someone who forms a view and puts their name on it, challenges the business when the numbers don&#39;t support the story, and is hungry to build rather than maintain.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Financial Planning &amp;amp; Analysis (FP&amp;amp;A): Own budgeting, forecasting, and monthly and weekly reporting cycles - delivered decision-ready and owning the recommendation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Management &amp;amp; Board Reporting: Prepare board and management materials, distilling complex analyses into clear narratives on company performance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Business Partnering: Work with product and commercial leaders to challenge business logic, optimize unit economics, and drive accountability for growth targets. Surface variances and deliver actionable insights independently&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Fundraising &amp;amp; Investor Relations: Support capital-raising efforts by leading data room preparation — assembling, analysing, and quality-checking the financial models, performance data, and supporting materials that underpin investor due diligence. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Process &amp;amp; Systems Enhancement: Partner with accounting, commercial, and data teams to proactively identify inefficiencies in finance systems and processes, applying automation and AI to sharpen analytics and strengthen reporting accuracy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a related field; MBA or professional certification (CFA, CPA) preferred&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;8–10+ years of experience in investment banking, strategic finance, or corporate FP&amp;amp;A, ideally in a high-growth or tech-driven environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Advanced financial modelling, with the ability to turn complex data into a recommendation, not just an output&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Strong communication and storytelling, with the presence to influence senior stakeholders and hold a view in front of them&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Deep curiosity and understanding of fintech business models, unit economics, and market trends&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Strategic, ownership-driven mindset — able to operate autonomously and lead cross-functional initiatives from concept to execution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Prior experience in fintech, payments, or high-growth technology companies is a strong plus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

