&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a highly capable, adaptable, and proactive team member who can support the day-to-day management, rollout, and ongoing evolution of modern AI platforms and related technology initiatives across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who is comfortable operating across multiple domains. The right person will help manage enterprise AI tools, connectors, settings, access, governance, and API-related work, while also being ready to assist with broader IT, security, and AI engineering needs as priorities shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person should be organized, dependable, and willing to jump in where needed — whether that is helping evaluate new AI features, supporting connector setup and administration, assisting with cleanup and operational tasks, documenting processes, coordinating follow-ups, or contributing to technical and security-related initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is someone who can help bring more structure, follow-through, and proactive support to a fast-moving environment. They should be curious about emerging AI capabilities, comfortable learning new tools quickly, and able to translate requests into action independently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will support the administration, coordination, and continuous improvement of a growing set of AI tools and related technical programs. Responsibilities may include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping manage enterprise AI platforms, including configuration, access, settings, connectors, permissions, and operational support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tracking and evaluating new features, releases, integrations, and connector capabilities across AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, and related platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting governance, risk review, and general oversight of AI tooling, including coordination with IT and security considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting with API-related work, documentation, testing, and operational follow-up for AI-driven initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handling operational cleanup, organization, process follow-through, and general support tasks to improve efficiency and reduce manual overhead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering on AI engineering efforts where needed, including testing, implementation support, and coordination of technical tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing support on adjacent IT and security work based on business needs and team priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping move work from reactive to proactive by identifying gaps, organizing next steps, and ensuring important items do not get missed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking ownership of assigned tasks and executing reliably across a wide range of responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years experience working with enterprise technology tools, IT operations, security, or technical program coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in AI platforms, emerging features, integrations, and real-world enterprise use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work across both strategic and operational tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on mindset with strong follow-through and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
