job-093kszd:
&lt;div class=&quot;overview-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Linux Engineers work with the critical infrastructure underlying the rest of the firm’s technology. Members of this group are hard-working Systems Engineers, Administrators and Programmers, tasked with maintaining and improving the platform that powers Jane Street&#39;s production trading systems. Our mix of in-house and open source software allows you to investigate and innovate at every level. On any given day, you could be debugging kernel performance, developing management tools, or resolving production issues in real time. Diving into tricky systems problems is our specialty.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment automation, scalable configuration management, and obsessive monitoring are the focus of some of our ongoing projects. We automate as much of our work as we can, but not because we are lazy. We find that automation reduces our error rate and overall workload - plus, we think it&#39;s fun.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in our group provides opportunities for involvement with almost every other facet of the company. We work directly with colleagues in Trading, Technology, and Operations to build and maintain systems with a firm-wide scope. Using feedback from other groups and our custom monitoring tools, we strive to resolve production issues quickly, perform comprehensive root-cause analyses, and integrate long-term fixes in a clean and robust way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;qualifications-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to hire Systems Programmers and Administrators with a deep knowledge of Unix internals and the Linux ecosystem. Candidates should have a willingness to learn OCaml, our language of choice, and meet the following requirements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering or other technical discipline (or equivalent experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and concise communication skills, as well as the ability to efficiently analyze and deconstruct technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of operating system fundamentals, especially Linux&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with the Unix command line and shell scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with modern Linux systems and systems programming concepts like C, sockets, virtual memory, and the process life cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of network protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting skills and knowledge of profiling/debugging tools such as gdb, perf, DTrace, eBPF, or SystemTap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience in any language (functional languages a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you&#39;re a recruiting agency and want to partner with us, please reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:agency-partnerships@janestreet.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;agency-partnerships@janestreet.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

job-0wxx0ug:
&lt;div class=&quot;overview-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for Software Engineers with a background in programming languages to join one of our PL-focused teams at Jane Street.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Programming languages work at Jane Street spans a wide variety of different areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language design and type systems.&lt;/strong&gt; Designing language features and stronger type-level guarantees that let our developers express more of what they mean, and catch more mistakes at compile time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compilers and optimization.&lt;/strong&gt; Investing in optimization, code generation, and backend work that translates directly into measurable speedups across the firm&#39;s most performance-sensitive systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incremental and parallel computation.&lt;/strong&gt; Building runtimes that can evaluate large, irregular, dynamic computation graphs &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/janestreet/incremental&quot;&gt;incrementally&lt;/a&gt; and/or parallel across many cores and machines, with first-class attention to scheduling, memory, and resource accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support for high-performance computing,&lt;/strong&gt; including work on tooling, verification techniques, and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/janestreet/hardcaml/&quot;&gt;languages for hardware design&lt;/a&gt;, as well as support for programming GPUs and other ML accelerators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain-specific languages.&lt;/strong&gt; Designing, implementing, and evolving custom languages that power some of our most important internal platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tooling and developer experience.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/janestreet/memtrace/&quot;&gt;Profilers&lt;/a&gt;, debuggers, language servers, IDE integrations, documentation tools, and the surrounding infrastructure that makes a language genuinely pleasant to use at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some of this work involves working on open-source language implementations, like those of OCaml and Python, and for those areas, a meaningful portion of our work is open-source as well. Some of it involves custom languages and DSLs that we’ve built entirely in-house, some open-source, some purely internal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people who have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with—and love for—programming languages. There&#39;s no specific checklist; we are interested in people with experience in language design, type systems, compilers, runtimes, or DSL implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top-notch programming skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills. Software engineering at Jane Street is highly collaborative, and we are looking for people who can work effectively in small, close-knit teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No previous experience with OCaml or functional programming is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You only need to submit one application for Programming Language Engineering at Jane Street. We’re excited to evaluate folks for areas across all of these roles, but if you feel like your experience relates best to a more specific area, please indicate that in the notes section of your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
